        "id":  "mihir-kumar-singh-appointed-as-bihars-new-development-commissioner",
        "title":  "Mihir Kumar Singh Appointed as Bihar’s New Development Commissioner",
        "summary":  "“A New Chapter for Bihar’s Governance: Mihir Kumar Singh Takes Charge as Development Commissioner” A New Dawn in Bihar’s Administration Big changes often reshape a state’s direction, and this moment feels exactly",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e“A New Chapter for Bihar’s Governance: Mihir Kumar Singh Takes Charge as Development Commissioner”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA New Dawn in Bihar’s Administration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBig changes often reshape a state’s direction, and this moment feels exactly like that. Bihar begins a fresh chapter as IAS officer Mihir Kumar Singh takes over as the new Development Commissioner of Bihar, replacing S. Siddharth. The appointment marks a major administrative shift, and many citizens now look forward to stronger development momentum across the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis decision is part of a larger IAS reshuffle by the new Bihar government. Moreover, the move includes several high-level transfers that aim to streamline departments and accelerate progress.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWho Is Mihir Kumar Singh?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA 1993-batch IAS officer, Mihir Kumar Singh brings decades of hands-on experience to this crucial role. He previously served as the Additional Chief Secretary (Industries Department). He also handled the Transport Department as well as the role of Director General-cum-Chief Vigilance Commissioner in the General Administration Department.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith such extensive exposure, he understands Bihar’s growth challenges and business potential. Therefore, his new role becomes even more important as Bihar pushes for industrial expansion, improved connectivity, and investment-friendly reforms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey Transfers Reshaping Bihar’s Bureaucracy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe state government has made several strategic changes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCK Anil (1991 Batch)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCK Anil, earlier serving as the Advisor at Bihar Rajya Yojna Parishad, now becomes the Additional Chief Secretary of Revenue \u0026 Land Reforms Department. This shift signals an increased focus on land management and digital land records.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDipak Kumar Singh (1992 Batch)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDipak Kumar Singh, ACS of the Rural Works Department, continues in his core role. However, he also takes charge as DG-cum-Chief Vigilance Commissioner, strengthening internal accountability mechanisms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKundan Kumar (2004 Batch)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKundan Kumar, previously Resident Commissioner (New Delhi), now steps in as the Secretary of Industries Department. He will also continue holding additional charge as Resident Commissioner and MD of BIADA. This combination of roles hints at aggressive industry outreach and investor engagement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(Tag: #KundanKumarIAS #BIADA)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eB Kartikey Dhanji (2008 Batch)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKartikey Dhanji will now focus entirely on the Minor Irrigation Department, after his additional charge of the Industries Department was relieved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSanjay Kumar Singh (2007 Batch)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSanjay Kumar Singh, Secretary of Commercial Taxes, takes on added responsibility as OSD in the Home Department. This strengthens coordination between taxation, enforcement, and administrative oversight.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKaushal Kishore (2010 Batch)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKaushal Kishore, Commissioner of Darbhanga Division, now also handles the charge of Tirhut Commissioner, Muzaffarpur. This decision aims to ensure continuity and smoother regional governance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRaj Kumar (2010 Batch)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRaj Kumar moves from Tirhut Division to become the new Transport Secretary, a department critical to Bihar’s growing road network and mobility expansion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Reshuffle Matters for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis restructuring may appear administrative, but it directly impacts governance quality. New leadership often introduces new energy. Additionally, these officers bring diverse experience from industries, land reforms, transport, rural development, and district administration. Together, they can build faster systems and better services.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePeople now expect quicker decision-making, stronger vigilance, and more development-driven policies. Since every department connects with the public, these changes could boost efficiency across Bihar’s growth landscape.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Ahead With Reliable, Apolitical Stories\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is changing fast. The state is pushing past old narratives and building new ones. If you want to follow every important update — from governance to grassroots stories — there’s only one place that brings it all together with honesty and depth:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Follow www.biharsay.com for more such regular updates and become part of the 13k community worldwide!Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical storytelling platform. We focus on culture, business, development, and the real voices shaping Bihar’s future. With 13,000+ followers, top-ranking LinkedIn impressions, and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, we continue to redefine the way Bihar’s stories reach the world.Join us and walk with the Bihar that inspires.\u003c/p\u003e",
