        "id":  "bihar-health-dept-announces-drive-to-fill-46000-vacancies",
        "title":  "Bihar health Dept. announces drive to fill 46,000 vacancies",
        "summary":  "“46,000 New Healthcare Jobs: Bihar Launches Its Biggest Recruitment Drive Ever — A New Era of Hospitals, Jobs and Hope” “46,000 Vacancies. One Big Promise. Bihar’s Healthcare System Gets Its Boldest Upgrade",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e“46,000 New Healthcare Jobs: Bihar Launches Its Biggest Recruitment Drive Ever — A New Era of Hospitals, Jobs and Hope”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen a state announces over 46,000 new healthcare positions, people listen. But when the announcement comes with clear timelines, fresh infrastructure plans, and rapid progress across departments, it feels like a turning point for every family waiting for better healthcare.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Massive Recruitment Push That Touches Every Corner of Healthcare\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Health Minister Mangal Pandey returned to office with an ambitious goal—strengthen the entire healthcare workforce as fast as possible. He revealed that recruitment exams or advertisements have already been issued for 25 different job categories.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, these categories range from general duty medical officers to nursing staff, paramedics, dental officers, and even specialist doctors. The scale is huge, and the work has already begun.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNearly 12,627 technical-level posts have completed examinations. Additionally, recruitment for doctors, nurses, pharmacists and technicians has moved into the final stages, bringing much-needed relief for hospitals across the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat’s Filling Up First? A Quick Breakdown\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe numbers are impressive, but the speed matters even more.Here’s how the drive is progressing:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e663 General Duty Medical Officer posts will be filled by December. 808 Dentist posts are nearing completion. 11,389 Staff Nurse exams by BTSC are already done. Examinations for 498 Nursing Tutors have also finished. Tests are complete for: 2,473 Pharmacists 3,326 Dressers 2,969 Lab Technicians 1,232 X-ray Technicians 1,683 Surgical Room Assistants 242 ECG Technicians 702 Dentists\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e663 General Duty Medical Officer posts will be filled by December.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e808 Dentist posts are nearing completion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e11,389 Staff Nurse exams by BTSC are already done.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExaminations for 498 Nursing Tutors have also finished.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTests are complete for:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2,473 Pharmacists 3,326 Dressers 2,969 Lab Technicians 1,232 X-ray Technicians 1,683 Surgical Room Assistants 242 ECG Technicians 702 Dentists\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2,473 Pharmacists\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3,326 Dressers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2,969 Lab Technicians\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1,232 X-ray Technicians\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1,683 Surgical Room Assistants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e242 ECG Technicians\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e702 Dentists\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAltogether, more than 26,000 appointments are now in their final stages.This pace directly supports the health system and reduces pressure on existing staff.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e32,700 More Appointments Under NHM — A Second Big Push\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile the first round is already massive, Bihar is preparing for another 32,700 appointments under the National Health Mission (NHM). Interestingly, this includes key positions like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1,504 AYUSH medical officers 5,000+ ANMs 216 Community Health Officers 220 Ophthalmological Assistants 36 Specialist Doctors 449 General Medical Officers 7,600+ other essential posts\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1,504 AYUSH medical officers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e5,000+ ANMs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e216 Community Health Officers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e220 Ophthalmological Assistants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e36 Specialist Doctors\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e449 General Medical Officers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e7,600+ other essential posts\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith these additions, the state aims to improve last-mile healthcare delivery and strengthen rural centres.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNew Hospitals and Centres: Bihar’s Infrastructure Gets Bigger\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJobs alone don’t build a healthcare system. Therefore, Bihar is adding fresh infrastructure to match the growing workforce.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHealth Minister Mangal Pandey confirmed that:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFoundation stones for ₹925 crore worth of projects are already laid. 610 new Health and Wellness Centres will be allotted soon. The flagship project—a new 400-bed superspecialty orthopaedic hospital in Patna—is being fast-tracked and targeted for completion within three months.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFoundation stones for ₹925 crore worth of projects are already laid.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e610 new Health and Wellness Centres will be allotted soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe flagship project—a new 400-bed superspecialty orthopaedic hospital in Patna—is being fast-tracked and targeted for completion within three months.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis hospital, costing ₹215 crore, will transform orthopaedic treatment for thousands.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAyushman Cards and Medical Relief: Support Beyond Hospitals\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar has issued over 4 crore Ayushman Cards, creating easier access to cashless healthcare. Additionally, the state spends ₹350 crore every year under the Chief Minister Medical Relief Scheme, helping families who cannot afford critical treatment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese support systems bridge gaps for people who rely on government hospitals.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e🌱 Healthcare jobs. New hospitals. Real timelines. Bihar’s biggest healthcare leap is happening now.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo stay updated on development stories that shape Bihar, follow www.biharsay.com for regular, honest and apolitical updates — and become part of our 13,000+ global community. Bihar Say is Bihar’s proud storytelling platform, reshaping narratives and celebrating the state through culture, business and grassroots change. Join us and amplify Bihar’s voice.\u003c/p\u003e",
