        "id":  "patna-municipal-corporation-launches-massive-anti-dengue-drive",
        "title":  "Patna Municipal Corporation Launches Massive Anti-Dengue Drive",
        "summary":  "Patna’s War on Dengue: Patna Municipal Corporation’s 18,000-Home Daily Blitz to Defeat Mosquito Menace A City at War — And Everyone’s Involved Every dawn in Patna now begins with action. Streets echo",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA City at War — And Everyone’s Involved\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery dawn in Patna now begins with action. Streets echo with the hum of fogging machines, and residents watch as civic workers spray every corner. The Patna Municipal Corporation (PMC), under the leadership of Municipal Commissioner Yashpal Meena, has launched a war-level anti-dengue drive, reaching 18,000 homes daily.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnlike previous seasonal clean-ups, this mission is intense, structured, and city-wide. Teams are not only eliminating larvae but also spreading awareness door-to-door. The aim is clear — stop dengue before it starts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCoordinated Effort: 375 Teams, Two Shifts, One Goal\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure complete coverage, five anti-larva teams have been deployed in every ward. In high-risk dengue areas, ten special units now work round the clock. The teams check rooftops, pots, overhead tanks, and under-construction sites — all potential breeding spots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAcross 75 municipal wards, 375 teams operate in two shifts daily. They use Temephos for larva control and Malathion for fogging. Meanwhile, a special 500-metre perimeter is sprayed around every dengue-positive home identified by the health department.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis coordinated rhythm of inspection, fogging, and verification ensures that no neighbourhood is left behind.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHospitals on High Alert\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHospitals, often overlooked breeding grounds, are receiving special focus. Dedicated workers visit PMCH, NMCH, AIIMS, IGIMS, IGIC, Gardiner Hospital, and Rajvanshi Nagar Hospital daily for spraying and fogging.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis hospital-level vigilance reduces infection risk for patients and frontline workers. Moreover, it prevents re-infestation from within high-traffic healthcare zones — a crucial step that strengthens Patna’s overall defence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVehicles, Zones, and Rapid Response\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe civic body has also mobilised 57 fogging vehicles across six major zones:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePataliputra Zone – 13 vehicles Nutan Rajdhani Zone – 12 vehicles Azimabad Zone – 7 vehicles Patna City Zone – 6 vehicles Kankarbagh Zone – 10 vehicles Bankipur Zone – 9 vehicles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePataliputra Zone – 13 vehicles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNutan Rajdhani Zone – 12 vehicles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAzimabad Zone – 7 vehicles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna City Zone – 6 vehicles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKankarbagh Zone – 10 vehicles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBankipur Zone – 9 vehicles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery evening, these vehicles move through colonies, markets, and schools, ensuring consistent coverage. Furthermore, each team maintains a logbook for citizen feedback. Random verification calls confirm that ground operations match official reports.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf residents face issues, they can call toll-free number 155304, and a rapid-response unit reaches the location the same day. This real-time grievance redressal has made citizens active partners in the drive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Awareness to Action\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile PMC’s machinery is vast, the true strength lies in citizen cooperation. Commissioner Yashpal Meena repeatedly urges residents to keep their surroundings clean and water-free. Stagnant water, even in a bottle cap, can become a breeding ground within days.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTherefore, small daily habits — covering tanks, cleaning trays, and removing puddles — directly reduce dengue risk. Additionally, responding to fogging teams and sharing feedback builds trust and helps improve the process.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTogether, these collective actions transform awareness into sustained prevention.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bigger Picture: Patna’s Health Revival\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond dengue, this campaign reflects a changing mindset in Patna’s civic governance. It shows urgency, data-driven planning, and citizen-centric response — values that define a modern city.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom fogging lanes to verifying calls, every small act adds up to a safer, cleaner, and healthier Patna. The anti-dengue drive is not just a seasonal measure anymore; it’s a public movement that places health at the core of city life.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBe Part of the Movement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe fight against dengue needs every hand, every household, and every neighbourhood.Cooperate. Stay aware. Stay proactive. Together, we can make Patna mosquito-free.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Follow www.biharsay.com for such impactful stories and real-time civic updates.Join the 13,000+ strong Bihar Say community — Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform reshaping Bihar’s digital image through culture, business, and grassroots stories.\u003c/p\u003e",
