        "id":  "patna-to-get-multi-modal-hub-model-vending-zone-elevated-road-near-airport",
        "title":  "Patna to Get Multi-Modal Hub, Model Vending Zone \u0026 Elevated Road Near Airport",
        "summary":  "“Patna Rising: Multi-Modal Hub, Smart Vending Zone \u0026 Elevated Road Near Airport Set to Redefine the City’s Future!” A City on the Move Drive through Patna today, and you can feel the",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA City on the Move\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDrive through Patna today, and you can feel the pulse of change. The capital of Bihar isn’t standing still anymore—it’s evolving fast. The city is preparing for a major transformation under Chief Minister Nitish Kumar’s Pragati Yatra on February 21, where projects worth nearly ₹1,350 crore will be launched.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmong these initiatives are a multi-modal hub, a model vending zone, and an elevated road near the airport—each one crafted to ease congestion and modernize city life. Together, they mark a turning point for Patna’s urban future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMulti-Modal Hub: Where All Roads Meet\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna’s upcoming multi-modal hub will unify the way people move. It’s designed to bring buses, autos, e-rickshaws, and inter-city transport under one modern roof.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe plan includes a multi-level complex near GPO, linked to Patna Junction through a pedestrian subway. It will feature digital displays, elevators, EV charging bays, and spacious waiting zones. Moreover, real-time coordination between transit modes will cut travel time significantly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not just a structure—it’s a statement of intent. As traffic density grows, the hub will simplify commutes, reduce chaos, and create a smoother, greener mobility experience for citizens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eModel Vending Zone: Empowering the Heart of the Market\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna’s streets have long been a mix of energy and congestion. Street vendors bring life to the city, yet the lack of structured space has caused frequent traffic snarls.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo address this, the administration is developing model vending zones that balance order with opportunity. Vendors will now operate from well-defined stalls with lighting, sanitation, and storage facilities. Additionally, proper footpaths will return to pedestrians, easing both movement and safety.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis initiative celebrates inclusivity. Instead of displacing traders, it integrates them into a cleaner, more organized ecosystem—preserving livelihoods while reshaping urban flow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eElevated Road Near Airport: A Gateway to Global Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new elevated road near Jay Prakash Narayan Airport is another bold step forward. With passenger traffic rising after the new terminal opening, this link will ensure swift and seamless access.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe project envisions a four-lane elevated corridor that cuts travel time from city centers to the airport dramatically. Furthermore, it connects to broader infrastructure goals under the Patna Ring Road plan, strengthening routes to Bihta and beyond.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor travelers, this means fewer jams and quicker routes. For businesses, it’s a sign that Patna is ready for global attention.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Ripple Effect Across Rural Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile urban projects take the spotlight, rural Patna isn’t left behind. A new road will soon link the Bihta–Sarmera route with Daniyawan Top, improving inter-block travel. Local residents near Naubatpur have also been advocating for a flyover at Nispura Lakh—a long-pending demand that might finally see approval.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, large ponds and lakes are being rejuvenated under MNREGA and Jal-Jeevan-Hariyali Yojana, supporting both irrigation and ecology. These parallel efforts ensure that growth spreads evenly, not just within the city but across the district.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy It Matters: Patna’s Image Is Changing\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis transformation is more than construction—it’s confidence in motion. For years, Patna has battled the stereotype of being “slow to grow.” Now, these projects show a city stepping into its own, ready to attract investors, students, and entrepreneurs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery bridge, road, and zone adds a layer of pride. And as these developments unfold, they redefine Bihar’s identity on the national map—not as a story of catching up, but of leading ahead.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBe Part of Bihar’s New Story\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInfrastructure isn’t just about concrete—it’s about community. When residents care, cities rise stronger. Patna’s ongoing projects prove that coordinated efforts between citizens, planners, and leadership can create lasting impact.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay informed, get involved, and share the story that Bihar is writing every day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates—and join our 13K+ global community celebrating Bihar’s growth, culture, and changemakers.\u003c/p\u003e",
