        "id":  "back-to-work-after-chhath-puja-8-special-trains-from-bihar-make-return-to-delhi-mumbai-bengaluru-easier",
        "title":  "Back to Work After Chhath Puja? 8 Special Trains from Bihar Make Return to Delhi, Mumbai \u0026 Bengaluru Easier",
        "summary":  "The Journey Home Made Easy As the fourth day of the vibrant Chhath Puja (which concludes on 28 October) draws to a close, many festival-goers in Bihar are preparing to head back",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eThe Journey Home Made Easy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs the fourth day of the vibrant Chhath Puja (which concludes on 28 October) draws to a close, many festival-goers in Bihar are preparing to head back to their workplaces in other states. According to reports, 8 special trains will be deployed to ease this massive movement of people. These services aim to connect Bihar with major hubs like Delhi, Mumbai, Bengaluru and towns in Gujarat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy These 8 Special Trains Matter\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, the holiday rush after a major festival often leads to congestion, long queues and uncertain travel. Secondly, many travellers find regular trains full or difficult to book. With dedicated special trains, travellers gain better access — including sleepers, general and AC coaches.Notably, these trains will begin operations from 28 October onwards on various routes, thereby enabling smoother return journeys from Bihar. According to local media, they will especially benefit passengers in North Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhich Trains Will Run?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere are the 8 trains announced:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 04651: Jayanagar → Amritsar (Special) Train No. 04097: Hasanpur Road → New Delhi (Special) Train No. 04732: Samastipur → Sriganganagar (Special) Train No. 04449: Darbhanga → New Delhi (Special) Train No. 07358: Raxaul → UBL (Bengaluru) Special Train No. 05557: Raxaul → LTT (Mumbai) Special Train No. 09068: Jayanagar → Udhna Special Train No. 09070: Samastipur → Udhna Special\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 04651: Jayanagar → Amritsar (Special)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 04097: Hasanpur Road → New Delhi (Special)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 04732: Samastipur → Sriganganagar (Special)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 04449: Darbhanga → New Delhi (Special)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 07358: Raxaul → UBL (Bengaluru) Special\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 05557: Raxaul → LTT (Mumbai) Special\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 09068: Jayanagar → Udhna Special\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain No. 09070: Samastipur → Udhna Special\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy introducing these routes, the rail network expands relief and return-options for those heading back to metros and industrial hubs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat to Keep in Mind Before Boarding\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBook early: Seats are limited and with the festival rush, availability drops fast. Check class options: These specials include AC, Sleeper and General—so pick what suits you. Routes and timings: They vary by origin and destination; verify schedule ahead of travel. Extra coaches may be added: Officials say extra coaches will be attached if demand surges. Plan arrival to main hubs: Whether you’re going to Delhi, Mumbai or Bengaluru, ensure onward connectivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBook early: Seats are limited and with the festival rush, availability drops fast.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCheck class options: These specials include AC, Sleeper and General—so pick what suits you.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoutes and timings: They vary by origin and destination; verify schedule ahead of travel.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExtra coaches may be added: Officials say extra coaches will be attached if demand surges.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlan arrival to main hubs: Whether you’re going to Delhi, Mumbai or Bengaluru, ensure onward connectivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Move Matters for Bihar Travellers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy launching these specials, the railways recognise the massive travel demand from Bihar during Chhath and other festivals. For many from Bihar working in metro cities, the return journey often is fraught with uncertainty. Thanks to this move:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt offers better connectivity between Bihar and major employment centres. It shows a responsive transport policy, matching travel peak with supply. It helps families return home, celebrate, and then go back without undue delay.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt offers better connectivity between Bihar and major employment centres.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt shows a responsive transport policy, matching travel peak with supply.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt helps families return home, celebrate, and then go back without undue delay.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Informed, Stay Ahead\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant daily updates on Bihar’s infrastructure, transit news and transport developments? Follow www.biharsay.com for real-time stories. Join our 13K+ global community and be part of Bihar’s transformation through stories on culture, business and grassroots change. 👉 Visit now and never miss a beat!\u003c/p\u003e",
