        "id":  "bihar-stet-2025-admit-card-exam-date-announced",
        "title":  "Bihar STET 2025 Admit Card \u0026 Exam Date Announced",
        "summary":  "Bihar STET 2025 : All You Need to Know शिक्षक बनने का सपना अब आपके हाथ में! Bihar STET 2025 admit card is finally about to release. Here’s how candidates can grab",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar STET 2025 : All You Need to Know शिक्षक बनने का सपना अब आपके हाथ में! Bihar STET 2025 admit card is finally about to release. Here’s how candidates can grab it on time. The Bihar School Examination Board (BSEB) will release the STET 2025 admit card on October 11, 2025. Candidates registered for the Secondary Teacher Eligibility Test can download it from the official portal bsebstet.org. Make sure you have your user ID and password ready. Exam Schedule \u0026 Admit Card Importance The STET 2025 will be conducted through Computer Based Test (CBT) starting 14 अक्टूबर 2025. The admit card is crucial, as it contains: Exam date \u0026 time Exam venue Candidate details The BSEB has emphasized downloading and printing the admit card well in advance. Reporting to the examination centre on time is mandatory for smooth conduct. Bihar STET 2025 Exam Structure The STET exam has two papers: Paper 1 (Secondary Level):Subjects include Hindi, Social Science, Sanskrit, Urdu, Bengali, Maithili, Arabic, Persian, Bhojpuri, English, Mathematics, Science, Physical Education, Music, Fine Arts, and Dance. Paper 2 (Higher Secondary Level):Subjects cover Hindi, Urdu, English, Sanskrit, Magahi, Arabic, Persian, Bengali, Maithili, Bhojpuri, Pali, Prakrit, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, History, Geography, Political Science, Sociology, Economics, Philosophy, Psychology, Home Science, Commerce, Computer Science, Agriculture, and Music. Each paper has 150 questions: 100 are subject-specific, and 50 test teaching aptitude. Duration is 2.5 hours, each question carries 1 mark, with no negative marking. The syllabus follows graduation-level standards for Paper 1 and honours-level graduation for Paper 2. Passing Marks \u0026 Reservation Criteria Passing criteria vary by category: General: 50% Backward Classes: 45.5% Extremely Backward Classes: 42.5% SC/ST/Disabled/Women: 40% Candidates must meet the required score to qualify and appear for further recruitment stages. How to Download Bihar STET 2025 Admit Card Follow these steps: Visit bsebstet.org from October 11, 2025. Click on the ‘STET Admit Card 2025’ link. Enter your user ID and password. Submit to access your admit card. Download and print it for future reference and exam day. Always double-check your details on the admit card and keep it safe until the recruitment process ends. Stay Updated:For the latest news and official notifications, regularly check Bihar School Examination Board. Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become part of the 13k+ worldwide community! Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change. Tags:Bihar Exam Updates Bihar STET Admit Card Bihar Teacher Eligibility Test BSEB STET 2025 ihar STET 2025 STET Admit Card Download\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eशिक्षक बनने का सपना अब आपके हाथ में! Bihar STET 2025 admit card is finally about to release. Here’s how candidates can grab it on time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar School Examination Board (BSEB) will release the STET 2025 admit card on October 11, 2025. Candidates registered for the Secondary Teacher Eligibility Test can download it from the official portal bsebstet.org. Make sure you have your user ID and password ready.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExam Schedule \u0026 Admit Card Importance\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe STET 2025 will be conducted through Computer Based Test (CBT) starting 14 अक्टूबर 2025. The admit card is crucial, as it contains:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExam date \u0026 time Exam venue Candidate details\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExam date \u0026 time\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExam venue\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCandidate details\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe BSEB has emphasized downloading and printing the admit card well in advance. Reporting to the examination centre on time is mandatory for smooth conduct.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar STET 2025 Exam Structure\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe STET exam has two papers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePaper 1 (Secondary Level):Subjects include Hindi, Social Science, Sanskrit, Urdu, Bengali, Maithili, Arabic, Persian, Bhojpuri, English, Mathematics, Science, Physical Education, Music, Fine Arts, and Dance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePaper 2 (Higher Secondary Level):Subjects cover Hindi, Urdu, English, Sanskrit, Magahi, Arabic, Persian, Bengali, Maithili, Bhojpuri, Pali, Prakrit, Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, History, Geography, Political Science, Sociology, Economics, Philosophy, Psychology, Home Science, Commerce, Computer Science, Agriculture, and Music.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach paper has 150 questions: 100 are subject-specific, and 50 test teaching aptitude. Duration is 2.5 hours, each question carries 1 mark, with no negative marking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe syllabus follows graduation-level standards for Paper 1 and honours-level graduation for Paper 2.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePassing Marks \u0026 Reservation Criteria\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePassing criteria vary by category:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGeneral: 50% Backward Classes: 45.5% Extremely Backward Classes: 42.5% SC/ST/Disabled/Women: 40%\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGeneral: 50%\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBackward Classes: 45.5%\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExtremely Backward Classes: 42.5%\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSC/ST/Disabled/Women: 40%\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCandidates must meet the required score to qualify and appear for further recruitment stages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow to Download Bihar STET 2025 Admit Card\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow these steps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit bsebstet.org from October 11, 2025. Click on the ‘STET Admit Card 2025’ link. Enter your user ID and password. Submit to access your admit card. Download and print it for future reference and exam day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit bsebstet.org from October 11, 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClick on the ‘STET Admit Card 2025’ link.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnter your user ID and password.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSubmit to access your admit card.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDownload and print it for future reference and exam day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlways double-check your details on the admit card and keep it safe until the recruitment process ends.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated:For the latest news and official notifications, regularly check Bihar School Examination Board.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become part of the 13k+ worldwide community! Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change.\u003c/p\u003e",
