        "title":  "Patna University Student Soumya Prakash Receives Prestigious My Bharat-NSS Award",
        "summary":  "Patna University Student Soumya Prakash Receives Prestigious My Bharat-NSS Award 2022-23 Soumya Prakash Recognized for Social Service Patna University student Soumya Prakash, a graduate of Patna Women’s College and postgraduate from the",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna University Student Soumya Prakash Receives Prestigious My Bharat-NSS Award 2022-23\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSoumya Prakash Recognized for Social Service\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna University student Soumya Prakash, a graduate of Patna Women’s College and postgraduate from the College of Commerce, has been awarded the My Bharat-NSS Award 2022-23. The award, presented by President Droupadi Murmu, recognizes young individuals for their dedication to social service and youth leadership through the National Service Scheme (NSS).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSoumya has participated in every NSS programme at Patna Women’s College, consistently demonstrating commitment, discipline, and leadership. Her efforts have earned appreciation from faculty members and peers alike.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLeadership and Participation in NSS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince joining NSS, Soumya has actively contributed to cleanliness drives, cultural events, and community service initiatives. She has also taken leadership roles in organizing and coordinating activities, ensuring that programmes achieve measurable outcomes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProf. Ajay Kumar Singh, Vice-Chancellor of Patna University, acknowledged her dedication, while Prof. Anil Kumar, Dean, and Prof. Suheli Mehta, Principal of the College of Commerce, congratulated her on this achievement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMentorship and Professional Recognition\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDr. Avinash Kumar, her team leader during the National Integration Camp and pre-Republic Day parade, highlighted her responsibility and reliability as a volunteer. He noted that her selection for the award reflects her consistent efforts and the high regard in which she is held across Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFormer NSS officers, including Dr. Amrita and Dr. Prem Kumar, also acknowledged her contribution, confirming that her recognition is well-deserved and professional.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePromoting Youth Engagement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSoumya’s recognition underscores the importance of youth participation in social service. Her consistent involvement illustrates how leadership, accountability, and dedication can create meaningful impact in the community. Students and volunteers can look to her example as a model for active engagement in social initiatives.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Informed with Bihar Say\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor regular updates on community initiatives, youth leadership, and developments in Bihar, visit www.biharsay.com. Join a network of over 13,000 followers worldwide and access verified news and stories on Bihar’s culture, business, and grassroots change. Bihar Say, Bihar’s leading apolitical media platform, offers in-depth reporting through its BiharCast podcast and video series, highlighting changemakers, traditions, and emerging voices across the state.\u003c/p\u003e",
