        "id":  "pm-modi-inaugurates-bihars-first-skill-university-4000-youth-appointed",
        "title":  "PM Modi Inaugurates Bihar’s First Skill University | 4,000 Youth Appointed",
        "summary":  "PM Modi Inaugurates Bihar’s First Skill University, 4,000 Youth Begin Their Career Journey! Bihar’s youth just received a game-changing opportunity! On October 4, 2025, Prime Minister @narendramodi inaugurated the Bharat Ratna Jananayak",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePM Modi Inaugurates Bihar’s First Skill University, 4,000 Youth Begin Their Career Journey!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s youth just received a game-changing opportunity! On October 4, 2025, Prime Minister @narendramodi inaugurated the Bharat Ratna Jananayak Karpuri Thakur Skill University, a historic step in skill-based education and employment in the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Leap into Skill-Based Education\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe university will revolutionize vocational training and employment opportunities. It will offer technical and vocational education, while promoting entrepreneurship, research, and innovation. This initiative complements Bihar’s Saat Nischay Part 1 and 2 schemes and helps youth compete nationally and internationally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, the university will affiliate with various skill institutes, conduct exams, and confer degrees. These steps will equip Bihar’s youth with skills needed in today’s competitive job market.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4,000 Youth Receive Appointment Letters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt the same time, 4,000 candidates selected by the Labour Resources Department received appointment letters at Bapu Sabhagar, Patna. The government aims to connect 1 crore youth with jobs and self-employment opportunities in the next five years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMinisters including Health Minister Mangal Pandey and Labour Resources Minister Santosh Kumar Singh emphasized that Bihar is creating new employment pathways. Additionally, a high-level committee will soon draft a five-year jobs policy for the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLeadership and Vision Behind the Initiative\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe inauguration featured Chief Minister Nitish Kumar, Deputy CM Samrat Chaudhary, and senior state ministers including Union Minister Vijay Kumar Sinha. University leaders, such as Vice Chancellor Deepak Anand and Registrar Rajesh Bharti, actively participated in the launch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA senior official said, “The university and today’s appointment letters reflect our commitment to building a skilled, self-reliant, and progressive Bihar.” This initiative demonstrates Bihar’s ambition to become a hub for skilled talent.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Transformational Step for Bihar’s Youth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe university opens doors for thousands of youth to enter the workforce confidently. By merging education, skills, and employment, Bihar bridges the gap between potential and opportunity. Furthermore, structured skill development sets an example for other states in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCall to Action\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay updated with the latest stories and impactful developments in Bihar. Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and join our 11k-strong global community reshaping Bihar’s narrative. Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media platform, highlighting culture, business, grassroots change, and untold stories.\u003c/p\u003e",
