        "id":  "bihar-govt-makes-student-credit-card-loans-interest-free",
        "title":  "Bihar govt makes Student Credit Card loans interest-free",
        "summary":  "Big Relief for Students: Bihar Makes Student Credit Card Loans Interest-Free Patna, Bihar: Imagine studying without worrying about loan interest piling up. For thousands of students in Bihar, that dream is now",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna, Bihar: Imagine studying without worrying about loan interest piling up. For thousands of students in Bihar, that dream is now a reality.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar government has announced that all Student Credit Card (SCC) loans under the Saat Nischay Yojana are now completely interest-free. This step is designed to reduce financial stress for students and give them the freedom to focus entirely on their education.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat’s New in the Student Credit Card Scheme?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarlier, education loans carried interest—4% for general students, and a reduced 1% for female, differently-abled, and transgender students. Now, every student will pay zero interest.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepayment terms have also been made easier:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLoans up to ₹2 lakh: Repayment period extended from 5 years to 7 years. Loans above ₹2 lakh: Repayment period extended from 7 years to 10 years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLoans up to ₹2 lakh: Repayment period extended from 5 years to 7 years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLoans above ₹2 lakh: Repayment period extended from 7 years to 10 years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis means students can pay back in smaller installments over a longer time, easing financial pressure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Change Matters for Students\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe rising cost of higher education often stops students from pursuing their dreams. By removing interest and giving more time to repay, Bihar is helping young learners continue their studies without fear of debt.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe SCC scheme already allowed loans of up to ₹4 lakh for higher education. With the new update, it is now even more accessible and supportive for students from every background.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Step Toward Accessible Education\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis move is more than a policy—it’s a message that education should not come with financial barriers. Students now have the freedom to choose courses and colleges with confidence. They can focus on learning, gaining skills, and building careers, instead of worrying about repayment stress.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the long run, this support can open doors for more engineers, doctors, researchers, and professionals from Bihar, shaping a brighter future for the state and its youth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Road Ahead for Bihar’s Students\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInterest-free loans and flexible repayment terms will inspire many more students to step into higher education. It means better opportunities, more graduates, and stronger representation of Bihar’s talent in India and beyond.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e✨ Want more such powerful updates and grassroots stories from Bihar?👉 Follow www.biharsay.com today and become part of our 12k+ global community. Stay ahead with inspiring stories, updates, and changemakers from Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
