        "id":  "patna-launches-har-din-har-gali-cleanliness-drive",
        "title":  "Patna Launches ‘Har Din Har Gali’ Cleanliness Drive",
        "summary":  "Patna Kicks Off ‘Har Din Har Gali’ Drive to Keep Every Street Clean A Daily Dose of Cleanliness for Patna Imagine waking up to spotless streets every single day. That’s the vision",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna Kicks Off ‘Har Din Har Gali’ Drive to Keep Every Street Clean\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Daily Dose of Cleanliness for Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine waking up to spotless streets every single day. That’s the vision Patna Municipal Corporation has rolled out with its new campaign — ‘Har Din Har Gali’. The goal is simple but powerful: make every street in the city cleaner, safer, and healthier.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaunched on August 14, 2025, the drive focuses on 100% door-to-door garbage collection, mosquito control, and daily road cleaning. The Municipal Commissioner, Animesh Kumar Parashar, shared that this mission is about more than tidiness — it’s about protecting public health and boosting Patna’s rank in the Swachh Survekshan survey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMorning Checks, Real-Time Reports\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis campaign comes with strict monitoring. Every day from 7 AM, ward nodal officers will inspect their areas. By 2 PM, they’ll send detailed cleanliness reports to headquarters.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePublic places will also see lime and bleaching powder spraying to prevent infections. Additionally, anti-larva spraying and fogging will be done regularly to keep mosquito-borne diseases at bay.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eZones Under Strong Leadership\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo make things run smoother, the city has been divided into six zones under two leaders. Ashish Kumar will oversee Patliputra, Kankarbagh, and Patna City. Rajan Sinha will handle Nutan Rajdhani, Bankipur, and Azimabad.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese officials will not only inspect work daily but also coordinate closely with ward officers. Their hands-on approach is expected to speed up problem-solving and improve results.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResidents at the Heart of the Mission\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Municipal Corporation knows that a city can only stay clean if its residents take part. That’s why they are urging people to cooperate with garbage collectors, avoid littering, and keep areas around their homes clean.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this collective effort, Patna is aiming for more than just neat streets. It’s about creating a city that reflects pride, health, and responsibility in every lane.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Follow www.biharsay.com for more such regular updates and become part of the 11k community worldwide! Bihar Say is Bihar’s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the state’s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith over 12,000 followers, top LinkedIn impressions for Bihar-focused content, and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar. Its flagship podcast and video series, BiharCast, dives deep into untold stories, spotlighting changemakers, traditions, and rising voices from the heart of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:bihar say news garbage collection Patna Har Din Har Gali mosquito control Patna Patna cleanliness drive Patna Municipal Corporation Swachh Survekshan Bihar\u003c/p\u003e",
