        "id":  "khadi-training-centres-in-bihar-empowers-rural-women",
        "title":  "Khadi Training centres in Bihar Empowers Rural Women",
        "summary":  "“Thread by Thread, She Rises: How Khadi is Stitching a New Future for Bihar’s Women” ✨ From Fabric to Freedom: Bihar’s Women Weave a New Tomorrow with Khadi Kapda nahi, zindagi badal",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e“Thread by Thread, She Rises: How Khadi is Stitching a New Future for Bihar’s Women”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e✨ From Fabric to Freedom: Bihar’s Women Weave a New Tomorrow with Khadi\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKapda nahi, zindagi badal raha hai Khadi!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKhadi is no longer just about spinning wheels and simplicity. In Bihar, it’s turning into a powerful movement — a tool of empowerment, identity, and income for rural women. With every stitch and every thread, women across the state are stepping into roles of dignity, self-reliance, and leadership.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKhadi Training: Where Skill Meets Self-Reliance\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupported by the Bihar Government, Khadi training centres are now active in multiple districts. These are not ordinary workshops — they are transformation hubs where women learn stitching, embroidery, knitting, soap-making, incense stick production, and detergent creation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnlike traditional training that only scratches the surface, these programs go deeper. Women learn design thinking, fabric selection, and also how to package and market their products effectively. This isn’t just about skill; it’s about sustainability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn 2024–25 alone, 59 training programmes were conducted. Over 950 women and 550 men joined these initiatives, with many women now earning through Khadi centres or launching their own businesses.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRole Models in the Making: Women at the Forefront\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom small villages to block-level towns, women are rewriting their stories. Earlier limited by financial dependence or social norms, these women are now earning, saving, and inspiring. What’s more? They’re becoming symbols of change in their communities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir stories aren’t just personal wins — they reflect a larger shift in rural Bihar’s gender dynamics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Khadi is not just cloth anymore. It is culture, creativity, and confidence,” said Industry Minister Nitish Mishra.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Khadi is not just cloth anymore. It is culture, creativity, and confidence,” said Industry Minister Nitish Mishra.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe also announced the launch of Khadi malls in all divisions and a digital push to sell local products online. His tagline — “Khadi for Fashion, Khadi for Nation, Khadi for Transformation” — is quickly gaining traction.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFashion Meets Livelihood: Khadi Goes Glam\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGone are the days when Khadi was only associated with dull fabrics. Now, it’s turning fashionable. Designers are blending Khadi with trendy cuts and modern silhouettes, making it appealing for the younger generation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis pivot toward fashion is also opening new career paths for trained women — from tailors and artisans to micro-entrepreneurs and local fashion influencers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd it’s not just about income. With every saree stitched and every soap sold, women are gaining confidence, purpose, and recognition.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Grassroots Revolution Backed by Vision\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isn’t a one-off story. It’s a grassroots revolution backed by policy, purpose, and people. With more centres being planned and digital tools being introduced, Khadi is on track to become a pillar of rural economic development.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese women are not waiting for opportunities — they are creating them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to hear more powerful stories like this?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Head to www.biharsay.com for real, raw, and inspiring stories from Bihar’s heartland.Join our 12,000+ global community reshaping the way the world sees Bihar.Because change doesn’t just happen in headlines. It begins with stories.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:Khadi entrepreneurship Khadi fashion Bihar Khadi for nation Khadi training Bihar Nitish Mishra Khadi rural women skill development self-reliant women India women empowerment Bihar\u003c/p\u003e",
