        "id":  "bihar-tree-plantation-drive-2025-5-crore-trees-66-species-one-vision",
        "title":  "Bihar Tree Plantation Drive 2025: 5 Crore Trees, 66 Species, One Vision",
        "summary":  "Bihar’s Bold Green Step: 5 Crore Trees, 1 Mission Can you imagine a Bihar where every breath feels fresher, each street corner shelters under leafy guardians, and children grow up surrounded by",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Bold Green Step: 5 Crore Trees, 1 Mission\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCan you imagine a Bihar where every breath feels fresher, each street corner shelters under leafy guardians, and children grow up surrounded by native trees? That vision is sprouting into reality. The Government of Bihar has kickstarted “पौधरोपण अभियान 2025,” an ambitious mission to plant 5 crore saplings statewide by mid-June.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Mahogany to Mahua: 66 Tree Species to Transform the State\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis initiative goes beyond numbers. It aims to revive ecological balance and build climate resilience. The campaign includes 66 carefully selected tree species, such as:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMahogany, Mahua, Jackfruit Peepal, Neem, Sheesham Kusum, Kanak Champa, Teak\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMahogany, Mahua, Jackfruit\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePeepal, Neem, Sheesham\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKusum, Kanak Champa, Teak\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese trees promise more than just greenery. They boost biodiversity, purify the air, and support rural livelihoods. As a result, Bihar will grow stronger roots—both literally and environmentally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeadline Nears: District Plans Due by 15 June\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo keep the mission on track, Additional Chief Secretary Harjot Kaur Bamhrah directed District Magistrates to submit district-wise plantation plans by 15 June. These plans must clearly mention:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTotal number of trees Exact plantation sites Responsible nursery sources\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTotal number of trees\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExact plantation sites\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResponsible nursery sources\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFurthermore, every district must organize coordination meetings to monitor progress. Timely planning will ensure smooth execution without delays.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhagalpur Sets the Bar: 1.30 Crore Saplings\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome districts have already taken the lead. Bhagalpur plans to plant 1.30 crore saplings on its own. Other major contributors include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya – 22.11 lakh Banka – 20.57 lakh East Champaran – 20.17 lakh Tirhut – 19.84 lakh Madhubani – 19.38 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya – 22.11 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBanka – 20.57 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEast Champaran – 20.17 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTirhut – 19.84 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMadhubani – 19.38 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearly, Bihar is mobilizing every corner of the state for this massive green mission.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEveryone Joins In: From Jeevika Didis to Schoolchildren\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportantly, this isn’t just a government project—it’s a people’s movement. The campaign invites participation from:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJeevika Didis (rural women’s self-help groups) Local farmers and nursery owners NGOs and paramilitary forces Students and teachers in schools and colleges\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJeevika Didis (rural women’s self-help groups)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal farmers and nursery owners\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNGOs and paramilitary forces\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStudents and teachers in schools and colleges\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure higher survival rates, only saplings taller than 3 feet will be used. Each site will also directly coordinate with nurseries, making supply and tracking much more efficient.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e268 Nurseries Ready Across Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrently, 268 nurseries—both government-run and community-based—stand ready to supply the saplings. These nurseries offer species suited to different regions, based on soil and climate conditions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause of this, each planted tree gets a better chance to thrive and contribute meaningfully to the ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreen Today, Greener Tomorrow\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s plantation drive isn’t just an environmental effort—it’s a legacy project. Every tree planted today ensures a greener, more resilient tomorrow. If every citizen plays a role, this mission will leave lasting roots for generations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay updated on this statewide green movement at www.biharsay.com.Join our 11,000+ global community working to rewrite Bihar’s story—one campaign, one change, one story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
