        "id":  "17-year-old-ethical-hacker-from-bihar-enters-nasas-hall-of-fame",
        "title":  "17-Year-Old Ethical Hacker from Bihar Enters NASA’s Hall of Fame",
        "summary":  "“Ek Bihari, NASA Pe Bhaari!” – Meet the 17-Year-Old from Samastipur Who Entered NASA’s Cybersecurity Hall of Fame What happens when a child’s love for video games turns into a mission to",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e“Ek Bihari, NASA Pe Bhaari!” – Meet the 17-Year-Old from Samastipur Who Entered NASA’s Cybersecurity Hall of Fame\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat happens when a child’s love for video games turns into a mission to secure the internet?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRam Jee Raj, a 17-year-old from Samastipur, Bihar, has taken the global tech world by storm. The self-taught ethical hacker recently entered the NASA Hackers’ Hall of Fame after uncovering a major vulnerability on NASA’s official website.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Gaming Curiosity to Global Cyber Fame\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRam’s story began like many childhoods in India—with games. However, unlike others, he looked behind the screen.“What makes a game run?” he wondered.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis simple question launched him into the world of coding, game development, and web design. Eventually, he stumbled across hacking-related films. That curiosity soon grew into a passion for ethical hacking—all self-taught from his small town.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy the age of 11, Ram was already writing code. He began scanning websites for flaws and responsibly reporting them. Over the years, he has quietly contributed to the digital safety of hundreds of platforms, all without formal education in cybersecurity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Email That Shook NASA\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the early hours of May 14, 2024, Ram emailed NASA with a report about a critical flaw on their website.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWithin just five days, on May 19, the agency confirmed the vulnerability, resolved it, and officially acknowledged Ram’s findings.Just like that, a teenager from a lesser-known town in Bihar earned a spot in one of the world’s most prestigious security circles:🚀 The NASA Cyber Security Hall of Fame.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe son of Rinkesh Kumar, Ram represents a powerful truth—you don’t need a Silicon Valley zip code to be a world-class tech innovator.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAI Dreams Rooted in Real Problems\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRam is not stopping at hacking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn fact, he’s already ventured into AI-driven innovation. He has built platforms like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMedVed AI – to assist in affordable healthcare FarmEye – to enhance smart agriculture YUVA Sathi – to empower rural youth with digital education\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMedVed AI – to assist in affordable healthcare\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFarmEye – to enhance smart agriculture\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYUVA Sathi – to empower rural youth with digital education\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese projects have earned him national and global recognition, including listings in the USA Book of World Records and multiple innovation awards.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrently, he’s developing an AI-based startup to revolutionize farming.“My aim is simple,” he says.“If one farmer can take care of five cows today, I want to help him manage five hundred—with tech.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Youth Are Not Behind — They Just Need the Mic\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStories like Ram’s rarely make national headlines, even though they deserve attention. They speak volumes about how youth from Bihar are rising, not just in academics, but in cutting-edge fields like cybersecurity, AI, and tech innovation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn fact, Ram’s journey is a reminder that Bihar doesn’t lack talent — it only needs platforms that spotlight it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s exactly what we do at Bihar Say. We tell stories that matter. Not because they’re viral, but because they’re real, raw, and rooted in change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Want to stay updated on such untold achievements from Bihar and beyond? Follow www.biharsay.com — Bihar’s leading apolitical digital platform for news, stories, and culture. Join our 11,000+ strong community across the globe and be a part of the new narrative.\u003c/p\u003e",
        "category":  "Education \u0026 Social",
        "categorySlug":  "education-social",
        "publishedDate":  "2025-05-30",
        "readingTimeMinutes":  3,
        "imageUrl":  "https://biharsay.com/wp-content/uploads/al_opt_content/IMAGE/biharsay.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bihar-Say-Website-2025-05-30T142446.563.png?bv_host=biharsay.com\u0026amp;bv-resized-infos=bv_resized_mobile%3A480%2A270%3Bbv_resized_ipad%3A820%2A461%3Bbv_resized_desktop%3A1536%2A864",
        "author":  "Bihar Say Amrita",
        "authorName":  "Bihar Say Amrita",
        "url":  "https://biharsay.com/2025/05/30/17-year-old-ethical-hacker-from-bihar-enters-nasas-hall-of-fame/",
