        "id":  "bihar-librarian-recruitment-2025-6500-vacancies-salary-exam-pattern-eligibility",
        "title":  "Bihar Librarian Recruitment 2025: 6500 Vacancies, Salary, Exam Pattern \u0026 Eligibility",
        "summary":  "Bihar’s Library Boom: 6500 Librarians to Be Hired — Here’s How You Can Apply Want a secure government job with a lasting impact?Here’s your chance. For the first time in 14 years,",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Library Boom: 6500 Librarians to Be Hired — Here’s How You Can Apply\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant a secure government job with a lasting impact?Here’s your chance. For the first time in 14 years, the Bihar Education Department has rolled out a plan to hire 6,500 librarians in government schools across the state. This much-awaited announcement brings hope to thousands of qualified candidates who’ve been waiting for such an opportunity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecruitment Details: All Eyes on BPSC\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC) will conduct the recruitment. The education department has already drafted the rules. Officials have sent the draft to the Finance and Law departments for clearance. After that, the State Cabinet will give the final nod.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure completion before the Assembly elections, the department is moving fast. Once approved, the BPSC will release the official notification and exam schedule.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost importantly, this recruitment is permanent. Selected candidates will receive state employee status, with all associated benefits.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSalary Structure: At Par with High School Teachers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile the exact figure isn’t released yet, the salary is expected to match that of high school teachers. According to the BPSC TRE 3.0:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTeachers in Grades 9–10 earn ₹31,000/month Teachers in Grades 11–12 earn ₹32,000/month\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTeachers in Grades 9–10 earn ₹31,000/month\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTeachers in Grades 11–12 earn ₹32,000/month\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, librarians can expect a similar pay scale. In addition, the job comes with:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDA (Dearness Allowance) HRA (House Rent Allowance) New Pension Scheme benefits Retirement age fixed at 60 years\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDA (Dearness Allowance)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHRA (House Rent Allowance)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNew Pension Scheme benefits\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetirement age fixed at 60 years\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, reservation rules and age relaxation will follow state government guidelines.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExam Pattern: What to Expect\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBPSC will conduct a 100-mark written test. The format will include multiple-choice questions (MCQs). To everyone’s relief, the test won’t have negative marking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe likely subjects are:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLibrary Science General Knowledge Bihar’s current and cultural affairs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLibrary Science\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGeneral Knowledge\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s current and cultural affairs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, brushing up on these topics can give you an edge.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEligibility: Are You the Right Fit?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo apply, you must hold either of these:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Bachelor’s degree in Library Science (BLIS) A Master’s degree in Library Science (MLIS)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Bachelor’s degree in Library Science (BLIS)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Master’s degree in Library Science (MLIS)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAge criteria and other conditions will be available once the official notification is out. Therefore, stay alert and get your documents in order.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Recruitment Matters for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrently, only 1,696 librarians work in Bihar’s higher secondary schools. Clearly, the state needs more. This recruitment aims to improve library access, boost reading habits, and support quality education.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore librarians mean better academic environments, especially in rural and semi-urban schools. The move also supports knowledge equity across Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant first-hand updates on such job opportunities, education policies, and Bihar’s growth stories?Head over to 👉 www.biharsay.com and become a part of our global 11K+ community!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e📢 Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar, trusted by thousands for its apolitical and impactful storytelling. From development news to culture, our platform celebrates Bihar’s unsung heroes and grassroots changemakers.\u003c/p\u003e",
