        "id":  "bihar-tre-3-posting-update-36968-teachers-allotted-schools-in-28-districts",
        "title":  "Bihar TRE 3 Posting Update: 36,968 Teachers Allotted Schools in 28 Districts",
        "summary":  "New Chapter in Bihar Education: 36,968 Newly Appointed Teachers Allotted Schools Across 28 Districts, Joining Deadline Set for May 15 In a major step towards improving the education system in Bihar, the",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eNew Chapter in Bihar Education: 36,968 Newly Appointed Teachers Allotted Schools Across 28 Districts, Joining Deadline Set for May 15\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a major step towards improving the education system in Bihar, the Education Department has allotted schools to 36,968 newly appointed teachers selected through the BPSC TRE 3 (Teacher Recruitment Examination). The posting process has been completed in 28 districts, bringing thousands of fresh educators into the government school system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSchool Posting Completed for 21,440 Teachers in 14 Districts\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Monday, the department released the district-wise school allotment list for 21,440 teachers. All teachers must join their assigned schools by May 15, 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s a breakdown by district:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWest Champaran: 302 Muzaffarpur: 2,414 Supaul: 1,356 Siwan: 1,424 Sitamarhi: 1,520 Saran: 2,124 Samastipur: 3,326 Saharsa: 1,664 Lakhisarai: 601 Khagaria: 1,341 Katihar: 2,051 Jamui: 1,398 Buxar: 905 Araria: 1,014\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWest Champaran: 302\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur: 2,414\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupaul: 1,356\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSiwan: 1,424\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSitamarhi: 1,520\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSaran: 2,124\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSamastipur: 3,326\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSaharsa: 1,664\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLakhisarai: 601\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKhagaria: 1,341\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKatihar: 2,051\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJamui: 1,398\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuxar: 905\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAraria: 1,014\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarlier Postings Done for 15,528 Teachers in 14 Other Districts\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarlier, on Saturday, 15,528 teachers were allotted schools in the following districts:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBanka: 667 Bhojpur: 1,178 Arwal: 289 Bhagalpur: 961 Gopalganj: 1,315 Kaimur: 959 Kishanganj: 1,184 Sheohar: 214 Nawada: 1,386 Nalanda: 1,465 Munger: 832 Begusarai: 1,543 East Champaran: 2,241 Rohtas: 1,294\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBanka: 667\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhojpur: 1,178\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArwal: 289\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhagalpur: 961\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGopalganj: 1,315\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKaimur: 959\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKishanganj: 1,184\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSheohar: 214\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNawada: 1,386\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNalanda: 1,465\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMunger: 832\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBegusarai: 1,543\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEast Champaran: 2,241\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRohtas: 1,294\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this, the total number of teachers allotted schools has reached 36,968 out of the 51,389 selected through TRE 3.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoining by May 15 Is Mandatory\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDr. S. Siddhartha, Additional Chief Secretary of the Education Department, clarified that all teachers must join their allotted schools by May 15.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“This is the teacher’s first official posting. Joining is mandatory, even if there are logistical difficulties,” he stated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“This is the teacher’s first official posting. Joining is mandatory, even if there are logistical difficulties,” he stated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTeachers facing challenges can request transfers later through their District Education Officers (DEO).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProvisional Appointment Letters Already Issued\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe provisional appointment letters for all selected teachers were distributed on March 9, 2025. Now that school postings have begun, this marks the final step before they begin their teaching journey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRemaining Postings to Be Completed Soon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePostings for the remaining teachers (out of 51,389) are expected to be finalized by Tuesday, ensuring a timely start to the academic calendar across all districts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters: A Boost to Bihar’s Education System\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis massive teacher deployment is a positive sign for government schools in Bihar. With thousands of new teachers entering classrooms, students across the state — especially in rural and under-served areas — stand to benefit from improved learning outcomes and better academic support.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Informed\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow our platform for the latest updates on:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar teacher recruitment Government job notifications Education department announcements\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar teacher recruitment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGovernment job notifications\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEducation department announcements\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e🌐 Want more such powerful updates from Bihar?📲 Follow www.biharsay.com — Bihar’s leading apolitical storytelling platform🎙️ Dive into real stories from grassroots to growth — become a part of our 11k+ strong global community today!\u003c/p\u003e",
