        "id":  "mahila-samvad-2025-bihars-48000-village-campaign-to-empower-2-crore-women",
        "title":  "Mahila Samvad 2025: Bihar’s 48,000 Village Campaign to Empower 2 Crore Women",
        "summary":  "Bihar’s Bold Step: Mahila Samvad to Reach 48,000 Villages and Empower 2 Crore Women “अब सुनवाई ही नहीं, समाधान भी होगा — गाँव की हर महिला की आवाज़ सरकार तक पहुंचेगी।” From",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Bold Step: Mahila Samvad to Reach 48,000 Villages and Empower 2 Crore Women\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“अब सुनवाई ही नहीं, समाधान भी होगा — गाँव की हर महिला की आवाज़ सरकार तक पहुंचेगी।”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom April 18, Bihar is set to witness one of its most ambitious people-led programs—Mahila Samvad. Over the next two months, this initiative will span 48,000 villages, involving nearly 2 crore women. It’s not a speech—it’s a two-way dialogue. And it’s all about real change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat Is Mahila Samvad All About?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt its core, Mahila Samvad is a statewide initiative by the Nitish Kumar-led Bihar Government, aimed at creating direct communication with women at the grassroots. The Rural Development Department, in partnership with Jeevika, is conducting this campaign with a simple yet powerful goal—to listen, learn, and act.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure inclusivity, the dialogues will happen in two daily shifts:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMorning: 9:00 AM to 11:00 AM Evening: 4:00 PM to 6:00 PM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMorning: 9:00 AM to 11:00 AM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvening: 4:00 PM to 6:00 PM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause women’s lives are busy and layered, the program respects their time and routine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow the Government Plans to Engage\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery single day, 1,200 villages will host these sessions. That’s not all—600 Digital Awareness Vans (Jagrukta Raths) will travel across the state to reach even the most remote locations. These vans won’t just display government schemes. They’ll also serve as mobile feedback points.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportantly, the government wants to know:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat challenges women face in daily life How they perceive development What support they actually need\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat challenges women face in daily life\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow they perceive development\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat support they actually need\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRather than assuming, the government is asking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReal Problems, Real Voices, Real Solutions\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnlike many top-down awareness campaigns, Mahila Samvad believes in bottom-up change. Problems shared during these dialogues won’t stop at discussion. In fact, they will be recorded and forwarded to the respective district headquarters.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEventually, based on the insights gathered, custom solutions will be crafted for each locality. This ensures that feedback turns into actionable steps, not forgotten promises.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Muzaffarpur is a Key Focus\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInterestingly, Muzaffarpur will host the highest number of Mahila Samvad events. The region, known for its active women-led groups under Jeevika, has become a model for participatory development.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis strategic focus ensures that feedback from high-participation districts can guide other areas more effectively.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore Than a Dialogue—It’s a Movement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile this initiative may align with the upcoming election season, it also reflects a larger shift in governance. It represents active listening and community-centered leadership. And more importantly, it signals a government that wants to reach its people on their terms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen women from every background—farmers, homemakers, teachers, workers—get to voice their thoughts, the outcome is not just inclusive. It’s transformational.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour Voice Matters Too\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhether you live in a small village or in a city far from Bihar, stories like these inspire. They show what governance can look like when powered by listening, empathy, and action.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Want more real stories from the heart of Bihar?Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 11k+ strong global community that believes in people-first narratives.\u003c/p\u003e",
