        "id":  "bihars-unique-initiative-road-safety-slogans-and-wall-paintings-in-schools",
        "title":  "Bihar’s Unique Initiative: Road Safety Slogans and Wall Paintings in Schools",
        "summary":  "A Fresh Coat of Awareness: Bihar’s Colorful Push for Road Safety Imagine walking into a school where the walls speak. Not in words, but in powerful visuals and catchy slogans that teach",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA Fresh Coat of Awareness: Bihar’s Colorful Push for Road Safety\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine walking into a school where the walls speak. Not in words, but in powerful visuals and catchy slogans that teach every student how to be safe on the road. That’s exactly what the Bihar Government is now rolling out—a colorful and creative movement to turn every school wall into a canvas of safety and awareness.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Vision: Walls That Teach Life Lessons\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a bold move by the Bihar Transport Department, the upcoming campaign will feature impactful road safety slogans and artwork painted on the boundary walls of schools. These aren’t just decorative elements—they’re educational tools, crafted to ensure children grasp essential safety practices early in life.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThrough these wall paintings, students will learn:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe importance of wearing helmets and seat belts Why overspeeding is dangerous The risks of using mobile phones while walking or driving The rights of pedestrians How small decisions can prevent big tragedies\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe importance of wearing helmets and seat belts\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy overspeeding is dangerous\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe risks of using mobile phones while walking or driving\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe rights of pedestrians\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow small decisions can prevent big tragedies\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy engaging the Education Department, the Bihar Road Safety Council is set to ensure this initiative doesn’t remain just an idea but becomes an executed mission.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Meeting Table to School Walls: The Journey So Far\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis initiative took shape after a key decision during a recent meeting chaired by the Development Commissioner and led by the Bihar Road Safety Council. Following this, a formal request was sent to the Information and Public Relations Department, asking for standard painting and slogan-writing rates to implement the project uniformly across schools.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters: Building Habits That Save Lives\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChildren learn faster when they’re visually engaged—and Bihar knows that. This initiative isn’t just about painting walls, it’s about painting values onto young minds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimple, inspiring slogans like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Helmet pehno, zindagi chuno” “Road safety is self-respect” “Don’t text and walk—arrive alive” “Speed thrills but kills”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Helmet pehno, zindagi chuno”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Road safety is self-respect”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Don’t text and walk—arrive alive”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Speed thrills but kills”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese messages are easy to understand and impossible to ignore, especially when they’re part of a child’s daily school experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat’s Next: Monitoring, Execution \u0026 Community Involvement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo keep the momentum strong, a special monitoring committee will be established. Their goal? Timely execution and quality checks. More importantly, this campaign is a call for community involvement—students, teachers, and even parents can play a role in maintaining and spreading these messages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is not just talking about road safety—it’s showing it, painting it, and living it through its schools.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to see more such inspiring updates from Bihar?👉 Visit www.biharsay.com and be part of the growing 11,000+ strong global community that’s watching Bihar transform—one initiative at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
