        "id":  "bihar-becomes-indias-no-1-state-in-free-medicine-distribution",
        "title":  "Bihar Becomes India’s No.1 State in Free Medicine Distribution",
        "summary":  "Bihar Sets a New National Benchmark in Free Medicine Distribution Once known for its crumbling health infrastructure, Bihar has now emerged as India’s leader in free medicine supply—delivering over 611 essential medicines",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar Sets a New National Benchmark in Free Medicine Distribution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce known for its crumbling health infrastructure, Bihar has now emerged as India’s leader in free medicine supply—delivering over 611 essential medicines to patients across the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis remarkable transformation has brought affordable healthcare within reach of millions. And it’s not just a statistic; it’s a story of lives saved, families supported, and hope restored.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom 47 to 611: A Giant Leap in Medicine Availability\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn 2006, government hospitals in Bihar offered just 47 types of medicines. Today, the list includes 611 medicines and 132 medical consumables and devices, covering treatments from viral infections to cancer care.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese medicines are available across government hospitals and health centres—absolutely free of cost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis expansion means that patients no longer need to run to private pharmacies for critical medicines. Everything they need is often just a consultation away.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e10X Rise in Medicine Supply and Budget\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOver the last 20 years, the state’s budget for medicine supply has increased tenfold. From a modest beginning, the spending has now touched ₹762 crore in FY 2024–25.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs per official projections, it may reach ₹1100 crore by FY 2025–26. This investment has ensured uninterrupted supply, even of high-cost drugs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo Patient Left Behind: Medicines for All\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe goal is simple—every patient should receive the medicine they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom OPD to IPD, from urban hospitals to rural clinics, free medicine distribution ensures access to:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLife-saving emergency drugs Cancer, asthma, arthritis, and allergy medications Antibiotics and anti-viral treatments Blood-thinners and anti-allergic formulations\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLife-saving emergency drugs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCancer, asthma, arthritis, and allergy medications\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAntibiotics and anti-viral treatments\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBlood-thinners and anti-allergic formulations\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis coverage means patients don’t delay treatment due to cost. That’s a massive win for public health.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRanked No.1 in National Medicine Distribution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s performance has been recognised nationally. According to the DVDMS (Drug and Vaccine Distribution Management System) portal, Bihar has consistently ranked #1 in medicine supply and distribution for the past five months.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis ranking reflects the state’s efficiency in managing procurement, inventory, and timely delivery to health centres.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Gamechanger for Low-Income Families\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarlier, even a basic illness could push families into debt. Now, with free medicines readily available, patients no longer need to spend on costly prescriptions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis shift has made healthcare more inclusive. It’s no longer about who can afford treatment, but about who needs it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Timeline of Progress\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s how the journey unfolded:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2006: Only 47 medicines available. 2008: Expanded to 33 medicines for OPD and 112 for IPD patients. 2023: 611 medicines and 132 consumables listed under free distribution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2006: Only 47 medicines available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2008: Expanded to 33 medicines for OPD and 112 for IPD patients.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2023: 611 medicines and 132 consumables listed under free distribution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach phase of progress brought essential care to more people—and built trust in the public health system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA New Chapter in Bihar’s Healthcare Story\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s free medicine policy is more than a government initiative. It’s a public movement that’s improving health outcomes and saving lives.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt proves that focused reforms and consistent delivery can create change that touches every household.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant more such inspiring updates?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay tuned to www.biharsay.com for powerful stories that matter.Join our global community of 11,000+ readers who believe in Bihar’s rising story.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:Bihar Free Medicine Policy Bihar Health News Bihar Hospital Services Bihar Medicine Supply 2025 DVDMS Ranking Free Drugs Bihar Healthcare Access India Public Healthcare Bihar\u003c/p\u003e",
        "category":  "Education \u0026 Social",
