        "id":  "bihar-board-10th-topper-farmers-daughter-anshu-kumari-aces-with-98-aims-for-neet",
        "title":  "Bihar Board 10th Topper: Farmer’s Daughter Anshu Kumari Aces with 98%, Aims for NEET",
        "summary":  "Bihar Board 10th Topper: Farmer’s Daughter Anshu Kumari Aces with 98%, Aims for NEET Success! Bihar’s Brightest Star: Anshu Kumari’s Inspiring Journey West Champaran’s pride, Anshu Kumari, has scripted history by securing",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar Board 10th Topper: Farmer’s Daughter Anshu Kumari Aces with 98%, Aims for NEET Success!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Brightest Star: Anshu Kumari’s Inspiring Journey\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWest Champaran’s pride, Anshu Kumari, has scripted history by securing 98% marks in the Bihar Board 10th Exam. The daughter of a hardworking farmer, she now sets her sights on cracking NEET to become a doctor. Her unwavering determination and family’s support have fueled her success.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“I am overwhelmed with joy! Becoming a doctor has been my dream, and now I am one step closer to it. My elder sister has been my guiding force, and my parents never let financial constraints hinder my studies,” shared Anshu.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Board 10th Exam Results: A Look at the Toppers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnshu isn’t the only shining star. Alongside her, Sakshi Kumari from Samastipur and Ranjan Verma from Bhojpur also aced the exams, scoring 97.80% each. Moreover, Sakshi, the daughter of a carpenter, aspires to make a mark in the professional world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar School Examination Board (BSEB) announced an overall pass percentage of 82.11%. Out of 15,58,077 students, a staggering 4,52,302 secured first division, while 5,24,965 got second division, and 3,80,732 passed with third division.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBig Rewards for Big Achievers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo further encourage students, BSEB Chairman Anand Kishor has introduced double prize money for toppers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1st Rank: ₹2 lakh 2nd Rank: ₹1.5 lakh 3rd Rank: ₹1 lakh 4th-10th Rank: ₹20,000 each\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, all toppers will receive a laptop, certificate, and medal to recognize their outstanding performance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCM Nitish Kumar Applauds Bihar’s Young Achievers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Chief Minister Nitish Kumar personally congratulated the toppers, emphasizing the growing confidence of girls in academics. “Girls are making great strides in every field. Their success is inspiring and reflects Bihar’s progressive educational reforms.” Furthermore, he also lauded the Education Department and BSEB for timely results, ensuring students get ample time for further enrollment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat’s Next for Anshu?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith her NEET dream in focus, Anshu is gearing up for the next big challenge. Her story is a beacon of hope for students facing financial hardships. It proves that hard work, family support, and unwavering determination can conquer all odds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated with Bihar’s Top Achievers!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDo you want to read more inspiring stories? If yes, then follow www.biharsay.com for the latest updates and join our 10K+ strong community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
