        "id":  "bihar-school-news-govt-introduces-major-change-in-cycle-uniform-scheme",
        "title":  "Bihar School News: Govt Introduces Major Change in Cycle \u0026 Uniform Scheme",
        "summary":  "Bihar School News: Big Relief for Students! Find Out What’s Changed Education in Bihar just got a major boost! The state government has introduced significant changes to the Cycle and Uniform Scheme,",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eEducation in Bihar just got a major boost! The state government has introduced significant changes to the Cycle and Uniform Scheme, making it more accessible to students. Now, they will receive financial assistance at the beginning of the academic session. This decision, announced by Education Minister Sunil Kumar in the Legislative Council, marks a crucial step toward empowering students, especially those in rural areas.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey Announcements for Bihar’s School Students\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1. Cycle \u0026 Uniform Scheme Made More Accessible\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s Cycle and Uniform Scheme aims to support students studying in government schools. Previously, students had to meet certain criteria to qualify for financial assistance. However, with the latest changes, the process has become much simpler. As a result, students from distant villages who struggle with regular attendance will now benefit without complications.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2. 29,000 Schools to Get Computers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDigital education is no longer a dream! The Bihar government has announced that computers will be installed in 29,000 government schools, covering students from classes 6 to 8. Consequently, this initiative will bridge the technology gap and prepare students for a competitive future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3. Mid-Day Meal Scheme to Continue for Over 1 Crore Students\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNutrition is as important as education! More than one crore students in Bihar’s government schools will continue to receive nutritious meals under the Mid-Day Meal Scheme. Furthermore, the government remains committed to improving student health and attendance through this initiative.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4. Rapid Growth in Literacy \u0026 Female Education\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEducation Minister Sunil Kumar revealed some impressive literacy growth numbers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s literacy rate has jumped from 40% in 2001 to 80% today. Women’s literacy has increased from 34% to 74%, showcasing significant progress in female education. The state now has over 6 lakh teachers, with 44% of them being women. As a result, this has contributed to improved educational opportunities for girls.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e5. Education Budget Sees a Massive Boost\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar’s education sector is getting a major financial push. The budget for the education department has increased dramatically from ₹4,400 crore in 2005 to over ₹60,000 crore today. With this investment, infrastructure, teaching quality, and overall educational standards will see remarkable improvements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters for Bihar’s Students\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe recent changes in the Cycle and Uniform Scheme will encourage more students to attend school without fear of losing financial aid. Additionally, advancements in digital education, nutrition programs, and increased budget allocation indicate a promising future for Bihar’s education sector.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more such important updates on Bihar’s education sector, visit www.biharsay.com and become part of our growing 10K+ community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
