        "id":  "bihar-farmers-get-ready-government-to-start-wheat-procurement-from-april-1-check-msp-and-registration-details",
        "title":  "Bihar Farmers, Get Ready! Government to Start Wheat Procurement from April 1 – Check MSP and Registration Details",
        "summary":  "Big Opportunity for Bihar Farmers: Wheat Procurement Begins April 1 Great news for Bihar’s farmers! The government will start wheat procurement across the state from April 1. To ensure fair compensation, officials",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBig Opportunity for Bihar Farmers: Wheat Procurement Begins April 1\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreat news for Bihar’s farmers! The government will start wheat procurement across the state from April 1. To ensure fair compensation, officials have raised the Minimum Support Price (MSP) to ₹2,425 per quintal. Additionally, the process will take place online, making it more transparent and efficient.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow Can Farmers Sell Their Wheat?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe government has launched a digital portal for wheat procurement. Farmers must register online to sell their produce at government rates. This system eliminates middlemen and ensures quick direct payments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimple Online Registration: Farmers must sign up on the official portal before selling their wheat. Higher MSP for More Profit: This year’s MSP stands at ₹2,425 per quintal, an increase from last year. Direct Bank Payment: The government will deposit payments straight into farmers’ bank accounts, ensuring no delays.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere Will Wheat Procurement Take Place?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOfficials have set up dedicated procurement centers in every district of Bihar. These centers feature weighing machines and moisture testing devices to ensure fair pricing for farmers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey Updates for Farmers This Year\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe MSP has increased by ₹150, offering better earnings. Farmers no longer need intermediaries, simplifying the selling process. Government officials will monitor all procurement centers. The entire transaction will happen online, ensuring speed and reliability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportant Guidelines for Farmers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnly registered farmers can participate in procurement. Wheat must have a moisture level below 12% to qualify. Payments will arrive within 48 hours of procurement. Farmers must bring their Aadhaar card, bank passbook, and land records for verification.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAct Fast! Register Now for the Best Price\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince registration has already started, farmers should complete the process quickly. Delays might lead to missing out on selling wheat at the best government rates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e👉 Stay updated with the latest government schemes and agricultural news by following www.biharsay.com. Join our 10,000+ farmer community today!\u003c/p\u003e",
        "category":  "Education \u0026 Social",
        "categorySlug":  "education-social",
        "publishedDate":  "2025-03-21",
        "readingTimeMinutes":  2,
        "imageUrl":  "https://biharsay.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Bihar-Say-Website-4-2.png",
