        "id":  "good-news-for-bihar-travelers-16-special-trains-announced-for-delhi-mumbai-more",
        "title":  "Good News for Bihar Travelers: 16 Special Trains Announced for Delhi, Mumbai \u0026 More!",
        "summary":  "Holi Travel Alert: 16 Special Trains from Bihar to Delhi, Mumbai \u0026 More! Are you heading back to Delhi, Mumbai, or other metro cities after Holi? Here’s some great news! To manage",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eHoli Travel Alert: 16 Special Trains from Bihar to Delhi, Mumbai \u0026 More!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAre you heading back to Delhi, Mumbai, or other metro cities after Holi? Here’s some great news! To manage the post-Holi travel rush, Indian Railways has announced 16 special trains from Bihar. Now, you can book your tickets hassle-free and enjoy a smoother journey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpecial Trains from Bihar (March 17 – March 31)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo accommodate thousands of returning passengers, multiple trains will operate from Muzaffarpur, Darbhanga, Barauni, Jaynagar, Saharsa, Raxaul, and Sitamarhi to major destinations like Delhi, Mumbai, Hyderabad, Amritsar, and more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComplete Train List \u0026 Schedule:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur – Anand Vihar (Train No. 05283) – Every Friday until March 28 Muzaffarpur – Anand Vihar (Train No. 05219) – Every Saturday until March 29 Muzaffarpur – Anand Vihar (Train No. 04017) – March 21 (Friday) Muzaffarpur – Anand Vihar (Train No. 04029) – March 19 (Wednesday) Muzaffarpur – Anand Vihar (Train No. 05203) – Every Monday \u0026 Thursday until March 31 Muzaffarpur – Rishikesh (Train No. 04301) – March 18 (Tuesday) Muzaffarpur – Chervapalli (Train No. 07712) – March 17 (Monday) \u0026 March 22 (Saturday) Saharsa – New Delhi (Train No. 04065) – March 18 (Tuesday) Saharsa – Amritsar (Train No. 04601) – March 18 (Tuesday) Saharsa – Lokmanya Tilak (Train No. 05585) – March 21 (Saturday) Jaynagar – Anand Vihar (Train No. 04013) – March 18 (Tuesday) Jaynagar – Saharsa (Train No. 04501) – March 18 (Tuesday) Samastipur – Lokmanya Tilak (Train No. 01044) – March 19 (Wednesday) Raxaul – Lokmanya Tilak (Train No. 05557) – March 18 (Tuesday) Sitamarhi – Anand Vihar (Train No. 04015) – March 19 (Wednesday) Raxaul – Chervapalli (Train No. 07714) – March 21 (Saturday)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain Facilities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost of these special trains include AC, Sleeper, and General compartments to accommodate different budgets. So, whether you prefer comfort or affordability, you have options. Additionally, railway authorities have assured crowd control measures for a smoother travel experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRush Expected: Plan Your Journey Smartly\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDuring this peak travel season, railway stations like Muzaffarpur, Patna, Gaya, and Barauni will experience heavy footfall. It is advisable to book tickets in advance and arrive early at stations to avoid last-minute hassles. In case of an emergency, passengers can seek assistance from railway helplines and station officials.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated for More Travel Alerts!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis Holi season, make your return journey stress-free by planning ahead. Follow www.biharsay.com for real-time train updates and become part of our 10K+ community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
