        "id":  "from-jail-to-teacher-bihars-vipin-kumar-gets-government-job-while-in-handcuffs",
        "title":  "From Jail to Teacher: Bihar’s Vipin Kumar Gets Government Job While in Handcuffs",
        "summary":  "From Prison to Classroom: The Unbelievable Journey of a Bihar Man Who Became a Government Teacher A Scene That Shocked Everyone The image of a man in handcuffs walking onto a stage",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA Scene That Shocked Everyone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe image of a man in handcuffs walking onto a stage to receive his government teaching appointment letter left the audience in awe. The story of Vipin Kumar, a prisoner from Bihar’s Beur Jail, is unlike anything seen before. Despite being behind bars for 18 months under the POCSO Act, he successfully cleared the TRE-3 examination and secured a government teaching job.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVipin Kumar’s Struggles and Triumph\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVipin, a native of Airki village, Mohanpur block, Gaya, was once a respected teacher at a private coaching institute in Patna’s Saguna Mor. In 2023, he was accused under the POCSO Act and arrested. However, he has always claimed innocence, stating that rival coaching institutes framed him in a conspiracy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile waiting for justice, Vipin did not let his circumstances define him. Even in jail, he continued his studies, determined to build a future. His hard work paid off when he cleared Bihar’s Teacher Recruitment Exam (TRE-3) and became eligible for a government teaching position.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Moment That Stunned Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn March 9, 2025, during a grand ceremony at the Mahabodhi Cultural Center in Bodh Gaya, Bihar Government Minister Nitish Mishra personally handed over the appointment letter to Vipin Kumar. However, the sight of a prisoner receiving his appointment letter while in handcuffs left many speechless. For the first time in Bihar’s history, a jailed man officially became a government teacher.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith heavy security, Vipin was escorted from Beur Jail to Bodh Gaya for the event. As his name was announced, he walked onto the stage, still bound by chains. The hall filled with murmurs as people struggled to process the surreal moment. Was this a sign of justice, perseverance, or irony?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“I Want to Serve Society” – Vipin Kumar’s Emotional Words\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter receiving his appointment, Vipin spoke to the media. “I have always wanted to educate children and serve society. Even inside jail, I never gave up on my dreams. Once I am free, I will dedicate my life to teaching and shaping young minds,” he said.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHis words resonated with many. Should a person who has not been convicted yet be denied a chance at a better life? Minister Nitish Mishra emphasized that the Bihar government is committed to providing deserving candidates their due opportunities. He added that Vipin’s journey could inspire many others facing adversity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat’s Next for Vipin Kumar?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDespite securing the job, Vipin remains in judicial custody as his trial is still ongoing. His fate depends on the court’s verdict. If proven innocent, he will begin his teaching career. If found guilty, his appointment could be canceled.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe incident has sparked debates across Bihar. Can justice and opportunity coexist? Should someone accused, but not yet convicted, be given such an opportunity? Vipin’s story challenges traditional perspectives, making people rethink rehabilitation and second chances.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow Bihar’s Most Unbelievable Stories!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to stay updated on Bihar’s most extraordinary stories? Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 10K+ global community! Don’t miss out on stories that redefine success and resilience.\u003c/p\u003e",
        "category":  "Education \u0026 Social",
        "categorySlug":  "education-social",
        "publishedDate":  "2025-03-13",
        "readingTimeMinutes":  3,
        "imageUrl":  "https://biharsay.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Bihar-Say-Website-24.png",
        "author":  "Bihar Say Amrita",
        "authorName":  "Bihar Say Amrita",
        "url":  "https://biharsay.com/2025/03/13/from-jail-to-teacher-bihars-vipin-kumar-gets-government-job-while-in-handcuffs/",
        "isHero":  false,
