        "id":  "trains-from-bihar-to-prayagraj-cancelled-until-feb-23-full-list-updates",
        "title":  "Trains from Bihar to Prayagraj Cancelled Until Feb 23 | Full List \u0026 Updates",
        "summary":  "Trains from Bihar \u0026 Chhattisgarh to Prayagraj Cancelled Until Feb 23 – Check Full List \u0026 Updates! If you’re planning a trip to Prayagraj this week, you might need to rethink your",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eTrains from Bihar \u0026 Chhattisgarh to Prayagraj Cancelled Until Feb 23 – Check Full List \u0026 Updates!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you’re planning a trip to Prayagraj this week, you might need to rethink your travel plans. Indian Railways has canceled multiple trains from Bihar and Chhattisgarh due to a massive passenger rush for Mahashivratri. The cancellations will last until February 23, affecting thousands of travelers. Here’s everything you need to know.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFull List of Canceled Trains\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndian Railways has suspended several key trains, making travel to Prayagraj difficult for many passengers. Here are the affected trains:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDurg-Chhapra Sarnath Express (Train No. 15159/15160): Suspended from February 19 to February 21. Gorakhpur-Narkatiaganj Passenger (Train No. 55098/55097): Canceled until February 23. Gorakhpur-Patliputra Express (Train No. 15080): Not running until February 22.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese cancellations come as devotees from Bihar and Chhattisgarh flock to Prayagraj for religious events.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoute Changes \u0026 Alternative Options\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApart from cancellations, some trains will follow different routes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSwatantrata Senani Superfast Express (Jaynagar to New Delhi): This train will avoid Prayagraj until February 28 due to congestion at Prayagraj Jhunsi Railway Station.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTravelers should explore alternative routes or book special Mela trains to reach their destinations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Are These Trains Canceled?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe primary reason behind these disruptions is the overwhelming number of passengers heading to Prayagraj for Mahashivratri. The city is witnessing an unprecedented rush, making it difficult for regular trains to operate smoothly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat Should Passengers Do Now?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCheck Official Updates: Stay informed through Indian Railways’ official announcements. Plan Alternative Routes: Consider booking special Mela trains or opting for buses. Refunds: Passengers with reserved tickets will receive automatic refunds in their accounts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith these cancellations, planning ahead is crucial to avoid last-minute travel hassles.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay updated with real-time railway news! Follow www.biharsay.com for the latest train updates and be part of our 10K+ strong community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
