        "id":  "bihars-first-acute-stroke-care-unit-to-open-at-aiims-patna",
        "title":  "Bihar’s First Acute Stroke Care Unit to Open at AIIMS Patna",
        "summary":  "## “Every Second Counts”: AIIMS Patna Leads Bihar’s Fight Against Stroke with ‘Stroke Update 2025’   When every second decides between life and paralysis, **AIIMS Patna** is rewriting Bihar’s healthca...",
        "content":  "\u003ch2\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e“Every Second Counts”: AIIMS Patna Leads Bihar’s Fight Against Stroke with ‘Stroke Update 2025’\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen every second decides between life and paralysis, \u003cstrong\u003eAIIMS Patna\u003c/strong\u003e is rewriting Bihar’s healthcare story.\u003cbr /\u003eWith its bold step, \u003cstrong\u003e“Stroke Update 2025,”\u003c/strong\u003e the institute has launched a movement to bring \u003cem\u003espeed, science,\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003ehope\u003c/em\u003e to stroke patients across the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAIIMS Patna’s Landmark Initiative: Stroke Update 2025\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eAll India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) Patna\u003c/strong\u003e has introduced a transformative program to change stroke care in Bihar.\u003cbr /\u003eTitled \u003cstrong\u003e“Stroke Update 2025,”\u003c/strong\u003e the initiative focuses on \u003cem\u003erapid diagnosis, timely treatment,\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003ecollaboration between experts\u003c/em\u003e—three elements that can save lives when time is short.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJointly organized by the \u003cstrong\u003eDepartments of Neurology and Neurosurgery\u003c/strong\u003e, the event was inaugurated by \u003cstrong\u003eProf. (Brig.) Dr. Raju Agarwal\u003c/strong\u003e, Director of AIIMS Patna.\u003cbr /\u003eDuring the event, he announced the creation of a \u003cstrong\u003ededicated Acute Stroke Care Unit\u003c/strong\u003e—a specialized facility designed to deliver immediate, evidence-based care.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Timely intervention is the key to preserving life and neurological function,” said \u003cstrong\u003eProf. Agarwal\u003c/strong\u003e, urging hospitals to act faster than ever before.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAcute Stroke Care Unit: Where Time Meets Technology\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe upcoming \u003cstrong\u003eAcute Stroke Care Unit\u003c/strong\u003e will handle \u003cem\u003ethrombolysis\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003emechanical thrombectomy\u003c/em\u003e, two procedures that can reverse brain damage if done quickly.\u003cbr /\u003eThis development ensures that patients in Bihar receive world-class treatment without delays.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProf. Vikas Chandra Jha\u003c/strong\u003e, Head of Neurosurgery, shared crucial insights.\u003cbr /\u003eNearly \u003cem\u003e80% of strokes in India are ischemic\u003c/em\u003e and can be treated if addressed in time.\u003cbr /\u003eHe also pointed to the \u003cem\u003ealarming rise in strokes among younger adults\u003c/em\u003e, calling for stronger emergency systems and awareness campaigns.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUniting Experts for Faster Response and Better Recovery\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe event brought together more than \u003cstrong\u003e200 experts\u003c/strong\u003e, including neurologists, neurosurgeons, and general physicians from \u003cstrong\u003eAIIMS, PMCH, IGIMS,\u003c/strong\u003e and regional hospitals.\u003cbr /\u003eThrough discussions on \u003cem\u003eemergency triage, rehabilitation,\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eneurointervention\u003c/em\u003e, the program inspired collaboration across Bihar’s healthcare network.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, the speakers emphasized \u003cem\u003eambulance-based rapid response models\u003c/em\u003e and the need to expand \u003cem\u003estroke-ready hospitals\u003c/em\u003e throughout the state.\u003cbr /\u003eThe initiative also aligns with the \u003cstrong\u003eNational Health Programme’s mission\u003c/strong\u003e to strengthen critical care in every district.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBeyond Treatment: Building a Future of Compassion and Innovation\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor AIIMS Patna, this is not just a hospital project—it’s a \u003cem\u003epromise of progress\u003c/em\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003eThe institute aims to create a \u003cstrong\u003estatewide stroke network\u003c/strong\u003e, connecting rural and urban Bihar under one efficient care system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Stroke Update 2025 is a milestone in neurological care. It reflects AIIMS Patna’s commitment to innovation, compassion, and clinical excellence,” said \u003cstrong\u003eProf. Jha\u003c/strong\u003e, expressing hope for a healthier and more aware Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more inspiring stories that redefine Bihar’s growth in health, culture, and innovation —\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cstrong\u003efollow \u003ca href=\"https://www.biharsay.com\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ewww.biharsay.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e and join our \u003cstrong\u003e13k+ global community!\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLet’s celebrate the Bihar that heals, builds, and inspires the world. 🌍\u003c/p\u003e",
