        "summary":  "Patnaâ€™s Baghvani Mahotsav is creating a buzzâ€”literally and figuratively! This three-day event at Gandhi Maidan is changing the game for farmers, gardeners, and city dwellers alike. From empowering farmers to promoting urban gr...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatnaâ€™s Baghvani Mahotsav is creating a buzzâ€”literally and figuratively! This three-day event at Gandhi Maidan is changing the game for farmers, gardeners, and city dwellers alike. From empowering farmers to promoting urban green spaces, hereâ€™s why this festival is a must-visit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1. The Buzz Around Honey Production\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe festival kicked off with an exciting announcement: a new policy to boost honey production and marketing in Bihar. Agriculture Minister Mangal Pandey emphasized how this initiative will uplift landless farmers by training them in beekeeping. Crops like sunflower and moringa will play a vital role in this process. This move is not just about honeyâ€”itâ€™s about creating sustainable livelihoods.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2. Farmers Take Center Stage\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe festival features over 1,500 farmers from across Bihar. Together, they are showcasing 14,000 products, including honey, mushrooms, fox nuts (makhana), seeds, and ornamental plants. Visitors can explore 60 vibrant stalls, buy what they love, and connect with local farmers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3. Affordable Urban Gardening Kits\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to grow your own fruits and veggies? The rooftop gardening initiative offers an incredible deal. For just â‚¹2,250, you get 30 plants, pots, and six months of maintenance support. This is perfect for city dwellers looking to go green while saving money.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4. Innovation at Its Best\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA hybrid plant that grows both tomatoes and brinjals is stealing the show! Itâ€™s a testament to the power of modern farming techniques. Meanwhile, scientists are diving deeper into spice cultivation. Bihar, already a leader in turmeric production, is now aiming to grow more spices and boost farmersâ€™ income.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e5. A Boon for Biharâ€™s Economy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the last two decades, Biharâ€™s per capita income has grown from â‚¹7,500 to â‚¹66,000. Agriculture has played a key role in this transformation. With 13.50 lakh hectares of horticulture and an annual output of 286.45 lakh metric tons, the state is on the rise. The festival highlights ways to expand this growth even further.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy You Should Visit\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Baghvani Mahotsav is more than an eventâ€”itâ€™s a celebration of progress. From honey production to urban gardening, itâ€™s inspiring change for farmers and city residents alike.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t Miss Out!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHead to Gandhi Maidan to experience this revolution firsthand. For more updates, follow www.biharsay.com and join our 10K+ global community of changemakers.\u003c/p\u003e",
