        "id":  "ravi-kumar-yadav-bihars-bronze-medalist-at-national-fencing",
        "title":  "Bihar\u0027s Ravi Shines with Bronze at National Fencing Championship",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Rising Fencing Star Ravi Kumar Yadav, a talented fencer from East Champaran, has made Bihar proud by securing a bronze medal at the 19th Cadet (U-17) National Fencing Championship. The event, held in Rudrapur, Uttarakhan...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Rising Fencing Star\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRavi Kumar Yadav, a talented fencer from East Champaran, has made Bihar proud by securing a bronze medal at the 19th Cadet (U-17) National Fencing Championship. The event, held in Rudrapur, Uttarakhand, from January 8 to 11, 2025, saw fierce competition. Yet, Ravi stood out with his extraordinary skills and perseverance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Tournament to Remember\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCompeting in the Epee Individual category, Ravi showcased unmatched determination throughout the championship.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, he defeated Punjabâ€™s Prabhunoor Singh Sidhu with a decisive 15-10 score in the Top 64. Then, in the Top 32, he overcame Telanganaâ€™s Sanjay Kuthadi 15-11. Advancing further, he triumphed over Haryanaâ€™s Aryan Yadav 15-8 in the Pre-Quarterfinals. The tension rose in the Quarterfinals, where Ravi outperformed Maharashtraâ€™s Saiprasad Jangwad 15-11. Finally, in the Semifinals, Ravi narrowly lost to Haryanaâ€™s Prince Hooda with a close score of 14-15, earning the bronze medal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarly Beginnings and Hard Work\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRavi started fencing in 2019 in East Champaran, driven by his passion for the sport. Thanks to his consistent performances, he secured a place at the National Centre of Excellence (NCOE) in Guwahati, where he trains under the expert guidance of coach Lalit Kumar. Back home, he sharpens his skills at the District Fencing Training Centre in Motihari, with coach Vijay Kumarâ€™s support.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConsistent Excellence\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis bronze medal is not Raviâ€™s first national achievement. In November 2024, he claimed silver at the 68th National School Games in Jammu \u0026 Kashmir. Additionally, he has dominated state-level competitions, winning multiple gold medals and proving his mettle time and again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport System and Gratitude\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRavi credits his success to the unwavering support of his coaches, Vijay Kumar and Lalit Kumar, his family, and the Bihar Fencing Association. His father, Sajjan Kumar Yadav, a schoolteacher, has been a constant source of encouragement. The East Champaran community celebrates Raviâ€™s achievements with immense pride.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHonoring a Champion\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen Ravi returns to Motihari, the District Fencing Association will honor him for his stellar performance. Leaders, mentors, and sports enthusiasts have already extended their heartfelt congratulations to this young prodigy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Inspired\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more inspiring stories like Raviâ€™s, follow www.biharsay.com. Join our growing community of 10k+ readers and stay updated with the latest news and achievements from Bihar!\u003c/p\u003e",
