        "summary":  "A world-class cricket stadium in Rajgir, built with an investment of â‚¹350 crore, ready to host IPL and international matches. This architectural marvel, inspired by Sydneyâ€™s iconic stadium, is 75% complete and on track to tran...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA world-class cricket stadium in Rajgir, built with an investment of â‚¹350 crore, ready to host IPL and international matches. This architectural marvel, inspired by Sydneyâ€™s iconic stadium, is 75% complete and on track to transform Biharâ€™s sports landscape by July.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Rajgir International Cricket Stadium is not just a venue but a statement of Biharâ€™s growing prominence in the cricketing world. Designed to meet international standards, itâ€™s set to become a hub for national and global tournaments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey Highlights of Rajgirâ€™s Cricket Stadium\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ‚¹350 Crore Investment: Biharâ€™s largest cricket project to date. 39,400 Spectator Capacity: Ensuring an electrifying atmosphere for fans. Premium Playing Surface: Special grass sourced from Bengal for a superior ground experience. Well-Planned Access: Four entry gates dedicated to players, VIPs, and spectators for seamless movement. Massive Parking Facilities: Space for 2,000+ vehicles to accommodate large crowds. Modern Amenities: Cafeterias, drinking water stations, and restrooms for a comfortable spectator experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBCCIâ€™s Curators Step In\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Wednesday, January 14, BCCIâ€™s curators will visit Rajgir to inspect the pitch and ground. Their expertise will ensure the venue meets international standards, making it ready for IPL and other prestigious matches. This visit marks a significant milestone in the stadiumâ€™s development.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Vision to Reality: The Stadiumâ€™s Journey\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe dream of an international cricket stadium in Rajgir began in 2007, announced by Chief Minister Nitish Kumar. Construction officially started in 2018, with Shapoorji Pallonji Group overseeing the project across 72,843 square meters of land.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith 75% of the work completed, including major structural components, the remaining tasks focus on finishing touches. By July, the stadium is expected to be fully ready, setting the stage for Bihar to host its first international cricket match.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Rajgir Stadium is a Game-Changer for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis stadium isnâ€™t just about cricket; itâ€™s about ambition, growth, and putting Bihar on the global sports map. Modeled after Sydneyâ€™s stadium, it symbolizes the stateâ€™s potential to host world-class events.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar Cricket Association (BCA) is working closely with BCCI and other cricket bodies to ensure the venueâ€™s timely completion. Once operational, it will serve as a venue for IPL matches, international tournaments, and an inspiration for budding cricketers in the region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Connected for Regular Updates!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more updates on the Rajgir International Cricket Stadium and other developments in Bihar, visit www.biharsay.com. Join our community of over 10,000 readers and stay ahead with the latest news.\u003c/p\u003e",
