        "title":  "Bihar to Face Uttar Pradesh in a High-Stakes Ranji Trophy Match at Moin-ul-Haq Stadium",
        "summary":  "Patna is buzzing with excitement as Bihar takes on Uttar Pradesh in the Ranji Trophy 2024-25! The match will take place at the historic Moin-ul-Haq Stadium from January 23 to 26. Biharâ€™s cricket team, led by Veera Pratap Singh a...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna is buzzing with excitement as Bihar takes on Uttar Pradesh in the Ranji Trophy 2024-25! The match will take place at the historic Moin-ul-Haq Stadium from January 23 to 26.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s cricket team, led by Veera Pratap Singh and vice-captain Sakibul Gani, is gearing up for the challenge. Meanwhile, Uttar Pradeshâ€™s squad, captained by Aryan Juyal, features star players like Shivam Mavi, Saurabh Kumar, and Priyam Garg. Moreover, their team is guided by Sunil Joshi, a former Indian cricketer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Growing Cricket Aspirations\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOver the past few years, the Moin-ul-Haq Stadium has hosted several important matches. This season, it successfully held two Ranji Trophy games, paving the way for another thrilling encounter. Furthermore, Bihar Cricket Association (BCA) President Rakesh Tiwari has called this match a golden opportunity for Bihar to showcase its cricketing talent.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Bright Future for Bihar Cricket\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn December, the Bihar Government transferred the land registry of the Moin-ul-Haq Stadium to the BCA on a 30-year lease. Consequently, this move will allow the development of a state-of-the-art cricket facility. The planned upgrades include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA 40,000-seat capacity 76 corporate boxes and VIP accommodations for 250 guests Modern sports amenities like a swimming pool, badminton and volleyball courts, and more\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, the complex will feature a five-star hotel, a fully-equipped hostel for players, restaurants, and a clubhouse. These developments aim to transform Bihar into a hub for national and international cricket.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t Miss the Action\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearly, this match is more than just a game; itâ€™s a milestone in Biharâ€™s cricketing journey. From January 23 to 26, head to the Moin-ul-Haq Stadium and cheer for Bihar as they face Uttar Pradesh. Itâ€™s a spectacle you wonâ€™t want to miss!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ For more updates, visit www.biharsay.com. Join our 10k+ global community today!\u003c/p\u003e",
