        "title":  "Aurangabad Hosts Its First-Ever 13-Day Khadi Melaâ€”Discover Bihar\u0027s Hidden Craft Treasures!",
        "summary":  "Khadi Mela in Aurangabad: A Celebration of Biharâ€™s Rich Handicrafts and Local Entrepreneurs For the first time ever, Aurangabad district is hosting a vibrant 13-day Khadi Mela-cum-Entrepreneur Market, organized by the Bihar Stat...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eKhadi Mela in Aurangabad: A Celebration of Biharâ€™s Rich Handicrafts and Local Entrepreneurs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the first time ever, Aurangabad district is hosting a vibrant 13-day Khadi Mela-cum-Entrepreneur Market, organized by the Bihar State Khadi and Village Industries Board. This grand event, featuring 140+ stalls, brings together Khadi sellers and local entrepreneurs from across Bihar. It offers visitors a chance to explore unique handmade products, including authentic crafts and traditional textiles.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe mela is open from January 22 to February 2 and showcases the talent of over 100 Khadi and Village Industries institutions. Artisans and entrepreneurs from districts like Gopalganj, Madhubani, Bhagalpur, Siwan, and Gaya have gathered here to present their innovative creations. Clearly, this event is more than just a marketâ€”itâ€™s a celebration of Biharâ€™s culture and entrepreneurship.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat Makes This Mela Special?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis event offers a unique blend of traditional crafts, modern designs, and local entrepreneurship.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHandicrafts and Handlooms: A wide range of products, such as Tussar silk, Mithila paintings, Sujani sarees, silk bundis, and stylish jackets, are on display. Women Entrepreneurs: Many stalls feature items made under the Chief Minister Women Entrepreneur Scheme and Jeevika initiative, including papad, pickles, flaxseed laddoos, sattu, and home dÃ©cor. Local Pride: Products like carpets and durries from the Jalsa Kalin Dari Producer Company add to the charm. These items reflect the rich craftsmanship of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Should You Visit This Mela?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvents like this play a vital role in promoting Khadi and locally-made products. They inspire entrepreneurs, while also building awareness among customers. As Shatrughan Singh, Director of Jalsa Kalin Dari Producer Company, explains, â€œSuch events boost enthusiasm among entrepreneurs and connect people with handmade products.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Public Relations Officer Shweta Priyadarshini, the mela has three main goals. First, it aims to promote Khadi and village industries. Second, it offers local products a platform to reach new markets. Finally, it creates new employment opportunities, supporting the stateâ€™s economic growth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExperience the Spirit of Bihar!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t miss this chance to immerse yourself in Biharâ€™s traditional craftsmanship and entrepreneurial spirit. Visit the Khadi Mela in Aurangabad before February 2. Explore, shop, and support local artisans while enjoying the vibrant atmosphere.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more updates like this, visit www.biharsay.com and join our 10,000+ global community today!\u003c/p\u003e",
