        "title":  "Acharya Kishore Kunal: From IPS to Social Reformer | Padma Shree 2025 | #BiharKe7Ratna",
        "summary":  "Acharya Kishore Kunal: The IPS Officer Who Became Biharâ€™s Beacon of Social Change! A Life Dedicated to Service and Knowledge In the heart of Bihar, a luminary emerged whose lifeâ€™s work continues to inspire generations. Acharya...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eAcharya Kishore Kunal: The IPS Officer Who Became Biharâ€™s Beacon of Social Change!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Life Dedicated to Service and Knowledge\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the heart of Bihar, a luminary emerged whose lifeâ€™s work continues to inspire generations. Acharya Kishore Kunal, a name synonymous with dedication and service, left an indelible mark on society. His journey from a humble village in Muzaffarpur to becoming a revered social worker and scholar is a testament to his unwavering commitment to humanity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarly Life and Education\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBorn in 1950 in Baruraj village, Muzaffarpur district, Bihar, Kishore Kunal displayed exceptional academic brilliance from a young age. He completed his matriculation from his village high school, securing a prestigious scholarshipâ€”an achievement reserved for only a select few. Despite qualifying for engineering, he chose to pursue the arts at Patna College. In 1968, he secured the highest marks in Patna University, solidifying his academic excellence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDistinguished Career in Public Service\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn 1972, Kunal joined the Indian Police Service (IPS), serving with distinction across Gujarat, Bihar, and Jharkhand. His tenure was marked by integrity and dedication, leading to significant contributions in various capacities. Notably, he was appointed as the Officer on Special Duty (Ayodhya) by Prime Minister V. P. Singh. In this role, he mediated between conflicting parties during the Ayodhya disputeâ€”a responsibility he continued under subsequent administrations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTransition to Social Work and Philanthropy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter voluntarily retiring from the IPS in 2001, Kunal dedicated himself to social service. As the founder secretary of Patnaâ€™s Mahavir Mandir Trust, he established three charitable hospitals, offering affordable healthcare to the underprivileged. His efforts extended to empowering marginalized communities, including advocating for the employment of Dalit priests in Bihar temples.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLiterary Contributions and Scholarly Works\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond his administrative and social contributions, Kunal was a prolific writer. He authored several books, delving deep into historical and religious subjects. His writings reflect a profound understanding and commitment to promoting knowledge, interfaith harmony, and social justice.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHonors and Legacy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn recognition of his monumental contributions, the Government of India posthumously awarded him the Padma Shri in 2025. This prestigious honor underscores his lifelong dedication to social work, public service, and education. His legacy continues to inspire, reminding us of the power of selfless dedication.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Tuned for More Inspiring Stories\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the third installment in our #BiharKe7Ratna series. Join us tomorrow as we explore the life of another remarkable individual who has made significant contributions to society.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin Our Community\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more inspiring stories and updates, visit www.biharsay.com and become a part of our growing global community of over 10,000 members celebrating Biharâ€™s rich heritage.\u003c/p\u003e",
