        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eRajgir, a historic gem in Bihar, is now a year-round tourist hotspot! With stunning attractions like the Nature Safari, Zoo Safari, Glass Bridge, and Ghoda Katora, visitors keep coming back. The numbers speak for themselvesâ€”over 25 lakh tourists in 2024, even without the Malmas Mela!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecord-Breaking Tourist Footfall\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn 2024, Rajgir welcomed: âœ… 2,452,766 Indian tourists âœ… 102,042 foreign tourists\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDecember saw the highest footfall, with nearly 400,000 Indian and 18,000 foreign tourists. The month of November recorded the highest number of foreign visitors at 19,045. These numbers prove that Rajgir is now a must-visit destination in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNew Attractions Boosting Tourism\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe eight-seater ropeway to Vishwa Shanti Stupa has transformed the tourist experience. In 2024: ðŸš Over 7 lakh people rode the ropeway ðŸ’° â‚¹8 crore revenue generated\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe eco-friendly Ghoda Katora also saw over 3 lakh visitors, bringing in â‚¹25 lakh in earnings. With family-friendly closed cabins, the new ropeway is a favorite among children and seniors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpcoming Developments in Rajgir\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRajgir is gearing up for even bigger attractions, including: ðŸ› New Nalanda University ðŸŸ International Sports Stadium\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeepak Kumar, a local official, shared, â€œThese projects will bring even more visitors to Rajgir in the coming years.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMonthly Tourist Footfall in 2024\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith consistent growth, Rajgir is on its way to becoming a top travel destination in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“¢ Want more updates? Follow www.biharsay.com and be part of our 10K+ global community!\u003c/p\u003e",
