        "title":  "8th Pay Commission: Salary Set to Rise by 186%! Check How Much Bihar Govt Employees Will Earn Now!",
        "summary":  "The wait is finally over! With the central government announcing the formation of the 8th Pay Commission, every government employee in Bihar eagerly awaits the salary increase. If youâ€™re one of them, hereâ€™s everything you need...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eThe wait is finally over! With the central government announcing the formation of the 8th Pay Commission, every government employee in Bihar eagerly awaits the salary increase. If youâ€™re one of them, hereâ€™s everything you need to know about the upcoming salary hike and how to calculate it yourself.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e8th Pay Commission: Whatâ€™s Changing?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe 8th Pay Commission is expected to be implemented by 2026, benefiting nearly 50 lakh central government employees and 65 lakh pensioners across India. But the big question remainsâ€”which state will see the highest salary jump?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen a new pay commission is introduced, the central government provides guidelines for all states. The salary hike depends on two key factors:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFitment Factor (the multiplier applied to basic salary) Dearness Allowance (DA)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReports indicate that the fitment factor under the 8th Pay Commission could increase to 2.86, leading to a 186% rise in minimum basic salary. If Bihar follows this model, every government employee in the state will experience a significant boost in earnings.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow Much Will Your Salary Increase?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo understand the impact, letâ€™s take an example:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf your current basic salary is â‚¹22,000, After the 8th Pay Commission, applying the fitment factor of 2.86, your new basic salary will become â‚¹62,920.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThatâ€™s a massive jump! You can calculate your salary hike by simply multiplying your current basic salary by 2.86.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Employees: What to Expect?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen the 7th Pay Commission was introduced, the fitment factor stood at 2.57. Now, with the projected increase to 2.86, government employees in Bihar can expect: âœ… A significant rise in their take-home salary âœ… Higher pension benefits for retirees âœ… Improved living standards and financial security\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Hidden Treasure in Bihar: Son Bhandar Caves\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile discussing Bihar, letâ€™s talk about something fascinating! Son Bhandar Caves in Rajgir reportedly hold hidden gold treasures. British officers even bombarded the caves in search of gold but left empty-handed. Could this mystery be solved one day?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Next?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe countdown to the 8th Pay Commissionâ€™s implementation has begun. Since Bihar is likely to adopt the new recommendations, government employees should start preparing for a financial upgrade.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant more updates on Biharâ€™s latest news?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow www.biharsay.com and join our growing 10K+ global community!\u003c/p\u003e",
