        "title":  "Get Up to 80% Subsidy on 75 Agricultural Tools â€“ Donâ€™t Miss the Last Chance to Apply!",
        "summary":  "Transform Your Farming Experience with Subsidies on 75 Agricultural Tools! Are you a farmer in Bihar looking for a chance to upgrade your farming tools at an affordable rate? The governmentâ€™s Agricultural Mechanization Scheme of...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eTransform Your Farming Experience with Subsidies on 75 Agricultural Tools!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAre you a farmer in Bihar looking for a chance to upgrade your farming tools at an affordable rate? The governmentâ€™s Agricultural Mechanization Scheme offers massive subsidies on over 75 types of agricultural equipment, ranging from basic hand tools like khurpi, kudali, and hansua, to large machinery for advanced farming. The subsidy ranges from 40% to 80%, ensuring that both small and large farmers can benefit. Donâ€™t miss this golden opportunity to invest in your farmâ€™s future!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s On Offer?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnder the Agricultural Mechanization Scheme, farmers in Bihar can avail themselves of a variety of tools with significant subsidies. The government has laid out subsidies for 75 different types of agricultural equipment, ensuring that all farmers â€“ whether from rural villages or larger agricultural operations â€“ have access to affordable, quality machinery.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow Much Subsidy Can You Get?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe government is offering subsidies ranging from 40% to 80%, depending on the tool. Whatâ€™s even better is that the subsidy amounts differ for general caste and Scheduled Castes (SC), ensuring fairness and targeted support where needed. From small tools like hoes and sickles to larger, more sophisticated machinery, thereâ€™s something for every farmer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow to Apply?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo avail the benefits of the subsidy, farmers must apply on the Agriculture Departmentâ€™s official portal. The application process is open until 20th February, so time is running out!On 22nd February, after thorough verification, the department will carry out a lottery to select farmers and issue them approval letters for the tools they applied for. Itâ€™s crucial to complete your application before the deadline to avoid missing out on this excellent opportunity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey Tools Included in the Subsidy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis year, the government has added over 75 farming tools to the scheme. Whether youâ€™re looking to buy basic tools or modern machinery, this initiative has you covered. Some tools eligible for subsidies include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKhurpi (Hand Hoe) Kudali (Digging Hoe) Hansua (Sickle) Various large farming machinery\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese tools are essential for efficient and productive farming, and the subsidy will make them much more affordable for farmers across Samastipur and other regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy You Should Apply Right Now\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis scheme provides farmers the perfect opportunity to improve farming efficiency, reduce labor costs, and boost crop yields. With such high subsidies, you can upgrade your tools without breaking the bank. Whether you own a small farm or a large one, this scheme is for you.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow is the Process Conducted?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter you submit your application on the official Agriculture Department portal, the department will carry out an inspection. Verification of your application will occur, followed by a lottery-based approval process on 22nd February. If selected, you will receive an official approval letter to purchase the subsidized farming equipment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t miss your chance to get quality tools at unbeatable prices. Apply by 20th February and be part of the change in agriculture! For more updates and to stay informed on government schemes, visit www.biharsay.com. Join our 10K+ community of farmers and enthusiasts from around the world for more regular updates!\u003c/p\u003e",
