        "id":  "ancient-shiva-parvati-wedding-sculpture-found-in-bihar-rare-gupta-era-discovery",
        "title":  "Ancient Shiva-Parvati Wedding Sculpture Found in Bihar | Rare Gupta Era Discovery",
        "summary":  "The Untold Story of Ancient Bihar: A Shiv-Parvati Wedding Frozen in Time Bihar, the land of ancient heritage, has once again unveiled a rare archaeological marvelâ€” a terracotta sculpture depicting the divine wedding of Lord Shiv...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eThe Untold Story of Ancient Bihar: A Shiv-Parvati Wedding Frozen in Time\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar, the land of ancient heritage, has once again unveiled a rare archaeological marvelâ€” a terracotta sculpture depicting the divine wedding of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati. This exquisite piece, discovered in Chausa Garh, Buxar, dates back to the Gupta period (4th-5th century).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShiva-Parvatiâ€™s Wedding Depicted in a Rare Sculpture\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmong the numerous ancient sculptures found in Bihar, those associated with Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati stand out. However, the Kalyaan Sundar sculpture from Chausa Garh is unique. It intricately captures the divine wedding ceremony, an artistic representation rarely seen in terracotta.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBrahma as the Priest, Vishnu Performing Kanyadaan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis sculpture narrates a celestial taleâ€” Lord Brahma officiating the wedding rituals while Lord Vishnu, depicted in a rare posture, performs the Kanyadaan (the ritual of giving away the bride). Unlike many traditional sculptures where Lord Vishnu is accompanied by Goddess Lakshmi, this one solely focuses on his pivotal role in the marriage of Shiva and Parvati.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Masterpiece of Gupta Era Craftsmanship\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Dr. Shiv Kumar Mishra, a renowned sculpture expert, this terracotta idol is the oldest of its kind. It stands out as most previously discovered idols are stone-carved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe intricate details are mesmerizingâ€” Lord Shiva is depicted in Tribhanga Mudra, gracefully holding Goddess Parvatiâ€™s hand. She, adorned with stunning ornaments, mirrors his stance, creating an artistic symmetry that breathes life into this ancient relic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eParvatiâ€™s Divine Ornaments \u0026 Shivaâ€™s Iconic Posture\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eParvatiâ€™s jewelryâ€”a thick necklace, armlets, and waistbandsâ€”illustrates the finesse of Gupta-era craftsmanship. Meanwhile, Lord Shivaâ€™s firm yet elegant stance highlights his divine authority. The sacred fire, an essential part of Hindu wedding rituals, is also visible, making this sculpture a rare treasure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimilar Sculptures Across Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe discovery at Chausa Garh isnâ€™t isolated. Similar depictions have been found at Murli Pahad in Bhagalpur, Sultanpur, and various sites in Darbhanga and Nawada museums. The presence of such sculptures across Bihar indicates the regionâ€™s deep connection to Shaivism and its cultural significance in ancient times.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eElloraâ€™s Connection: A Pan-Indian Artistic Tradition\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExperts suggest that sculptures of this theme exist in Ellora Caves, Maharashtra. However, the Chausa Garh sculptureâ€™s terracotta medium makes it stand apart, emphasizing Biharâ€™s distinct artistic heritage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Timeless Legacy of Biharâ€™s Artistic Grandeur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith each discovery, Bihar cements its status as a treasure trove of ancient art and history. These sculptures arenâ€™t just relics; they are visual narratives of our glorious past, waiting to be explored.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more such fascinating discoveries, follow www.biharsay.com and join our 10K+ global community celebrating Biharâ€™s heritage.\u003c/p\u003e",
