        "title":  "Biharâ€™s 11% Electricity Consumption Surge â€“ A Power Revolution Unfolds!",
        "summary":  "Bihar has undergone an electrifying transformation! Once struggling with inadequate power supply, the state has now witnessed an 11-fold rise in electricity consumption, proving its rapid economic progress. The numbers tell a comp...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar has undergone an electrifying transformation! Once struggling with inadequate power supply, the state has now witnessed an 11-fold rise in electricity consumption, proving its rapid economic progress. The numbers tell a compelling story of change, development, and a brighter future for millions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eElectricity Consumption Skyrockets in Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBack in 2005, Bihar consumed only 700 megawatts of electricity. Fast forward to 2025, and this figure has surged to 8,005 megawatts, marking a historic jump. This growth highlights not just an increase in power supply but also rising demand due to industrial expansion, urbanization, and an improved standard of living.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey Infrastructure Developments Powering the State\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo meet this rising demand, Bihar has expanded its power infrastructure significantly:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrid Substations: From just 45 in 2005 to 170 in 2025, improving electricity distribution. Transmission Lines: Increased from 5,000 circuit kilometers to 20,393 circuit kilometers, ensuring better connectivity. Electricity Consumers: Grew from 1.7 million to a whopping 21.2 million, reflecting increased accessibility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese advancements have played a crucial role in ensuring a reliable power supply across the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Surge in Per Capita Electricity Usage\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe rise in power consumption isnâ€™t just about industries. It also signifies improved household access to electricity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2005 â€“ 70 units per capita 2012 â€“ 134 units per capita 2024 â€“ 363 units per capita\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearly, more people are benefiting from consistent power supply, transforming lifestyles and boosting productivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTop 10 Power-Consuming Districts in Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile the entire state has seen growth, some districts stand out due to their massive electricity usage:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna â€“ 647.6 crore units Gaya â€“ 240.2 crore units Muzaffarpur â€“ 165.6 crore units Rohtas â€“ 157.0 crore units Nalanda â€“ 151.4 crore units East Champaran â€“ 136.8 crore units Bhagalpur â€“ 130.1 crore units Aurangabad â€“ 112.2 crore units\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna leads the way with the highest electricity consumption, showcasing its urban growth and increased industrial activities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImproved Power Availability Across Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks to infrastructure upgrades, electricity supply has improved across the state:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUrban Areas â€“ Almost 24 hours of uninterrupted power Rural Areas â€“ Average of 22 hours of electricity daily\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuch improvements have fueled economic growth, enabling businesses, schools, and households to function smoothly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Energy Future: Whatâ€™s Next?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo sustain this momentum, the government is investing in further power capacity expansion:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpcoming 1,112 Megawatt Addition â€“ Set to strengthen the energy supply in the next fiscal year. Buxar Chausa Power Plant â€“ Two units of 660 megawatts each, with one unit expected to start operations soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese projects will provide long-term energy security, supporting Biharâ€™s ambitious growth plans.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated with Biharâ€™s Growth Story!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s transformation is far from over. With more power, better infrastructure, and rapid development, the state is moving towards a brighter future. Stay informed about Biharâ€™s progressâ€”follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates. Join our growing 10k+ global community and be a part of Biharâ€™s success story!\u003c/p\u003e",
