        "id":  "108-years-of-chanting-swami-santosh-anand-maharajs-mission-to-save-devagiri-mountain",
        "title":  "108 Years of Chanting: Swami Santosh Anand Maharajâ€™s Mission to Save Devagiri Mountain",
        "summary":  "The Fight to Protect Devagiri Mountain Begins Once a breathtaking range of mountains greeted travelers entering Shahkund, Bhagalpur. But rampant illegal mining destroyed most of them, leaving just a few behind. Among those who wit...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eThe Fight to Protect Devagiri Mountain Begins\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce a breathtaking range of mountains greeted travelers entering Shahkund, Bhagalpur. But rampant illegal mining destroyed most of them, leaving just a few behind. Among those who witnessed this devastation was Swami Santosh Anand Maharaj, a spiritual leader from Nepal. Seeing the environmental loss, he vowed to protect Devagiri Mountain by dedicating 108 years of uninterrupted chanting of â€˜Om Namah Shivayaâ€™. This mission, which began on May 27, 2010, is now a beacon of hope for environmental conservation and spiritual awakening.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Legacy Inspired by Devotion\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSwami Santosh Anand Maharajâ€™s journey started with inspiration from Pagal Baba Ashram, Jasidih, where a similar 108-year kirtan had begun. With limited resources, only five people joined him initially. But as the movement gained recognition, 20 permanent members took charge, organizing chanting sessions in three-hour shifts. Gradually, the initiative attracted devotees and environmentalists alike, transforming Devagiri into a center for both spirituality and conservation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Spiritual and Medicinal Treasure\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevagiri Mountain isnâ€™t just a site for kirtanâ€”it holds ancient medicinal secrets. Various rare herbs like Rudraksha, Kapoor, Long, Hing, Sindoor, Guggul, and Brahmi thrive here. With contributions from Swami Santosh Anand Maharaj and environmentalists like Shiromani, the mountain has become a natural pharmacy benefiting the local community.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Sacred Temples of Devagiri\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApart from being an environmental and spiritual hub, Devagiri Mountain boasts several ancient temples:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaa Kali Temple â€“ Located at the mountain peak, beside the chanting hall. Maa Bageshwari Temple \u0026 Durga Temple â€“ Situated a short distance away. Baba Girivarnath Temple â€“ A historically significant site, now protected by the Archaeological Department.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese temples, along with continuous chanting, make Devagiri a powerful spiritual energy center.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Sanctuary for Learning and Healing\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond spirituality, Swami Santosh Anand Maharaj has expanded his mission to social service.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYoga training is conducted at the center. Underprivileged children receive shelter and education. Local residents benefit from herbal treatments. The center also works to prevent further illegal mining.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVeterinarian Dr. Nirmal Kumar volunteers his time, teaching children, while dedicated disciples like Brahmachari Somanand, Om Didi, Shiv Prem, Babita, and Manoj Yadav serve selflessly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Monkâ€™s Journey to Devagiri\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBorn in Patratu, Jharkhand, Swami Santosh Anand Maharaj found his spiritual calling early. As a disciple of Swami Shivanand Tirth, he spent six years in Badrinathâ€™s Himalayan foothills, followed by time in Dhanbad and Nepalâ€™s Jetauranath. In 2010, he finally arrived in Shahkund, where he initiated the lifelong mission to save Devagiri.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin the Movement! Follow www.biharsay.com for more inspiring stories and become part of our 10K+ global community!\u003c/p\u003e",
