        "id":  "bhagalpurs-greenfield-airport-coming-soon-855-acres-in-sultanganj-approved-awaiting-final-nod",
        "title":  "Bhagalpurâ€™s Greenfield Airport Coming Soon! 855 Acres in Sultanganj Approved, Awaiting Final Nod!",
        "summary":  "Imagine catching a flight from Bhagalpurâ€™s very own airport, connecting seamlessly to major cities. That dream is turning into reality as the Bihar government has cleared the path for a Greenfield airport in Sultanganj, marking ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eImagine catching a flight from Bhagalpurâ€™s very own airport, connecting seamlessly to major cities. That dream is turning into reality as the Bihar government has cleared the path for a Greenfield airport in Sultanganj, marking a transformative step in the stateâ€™s aviation sector.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSultanganj Chosen for Bhagalpur Airport\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar government has identified 855 acres of land in Sultanganj for the project. The proposed location, strategically placed on Sultanganj-Deoghar Road, ensures seamless connectivity. The identified land is spread across multiple regions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMasdi â€“ 300 acres Nonsar â€“ 225 acres Rajganj â€“ 50 acres Kaswa â€“ 205 acres Sujapur â€“ 40 acres Manjhli â€“ 35 acres\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith its prime location and large-scale infrastructure planning, this airport is expected to revolutionize travel in eastern Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGovernmentâ€™s Push for Approval\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhagalpurâ€™s District Magistrate proposed two locationsâ€”Sultanganj and Goradihâ€”for the airport. After careful assessment, Sultanganj emerged as the top choice. Following this, Dr. S. Siddharth, Additional Chief Secretary, Civil Aviation, requested the Airports Authority of India (AAI) to conduct a technical feasibility assessment. The project now awaits final approval from the central government.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProposed Infrastructure and Runway Details\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRunway Length: 4,000 meters (northern end), 3,800 meters (southern end) Runway Width: 740 meters Terminal Size: 1,000 meters x 500 meters Distance from Bhagalpur Railway Station: 30 km\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConnectivity to Key Cities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe airportâ€™s location ensures accessibility to several major cities:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSultanganj: 6 km Bhagalpur: 30 km Munger: 34 km Banka: 57 km Jamalpur: 73 km Begusarai: 80 km Khagaria: 55 km Katihar: 120 km Godda: 88 km Deoghar: 126 km\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeputy CMâ€™s Vision for Biharâ€™s Aviation Growth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Deputy Chief Minister, Samrat Choudhary, previously announced the Greenfield Airport in Sultanganj, highlighting its role in boosting economic growth. He emphasized that this project will connect Tarapur and other eastern Bihar districts to national and international destinations, positioning Bhagalpur as a key aviation hub.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExcitement Among Local Residents\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe announcement has sparked excitement among locals. They believe the airport will enhance connectivity, boost tourism, and create jobs, ultimately leading to economic prosperity in the region. Now, all eyes are on the central governmentâ€™s final approval.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin the Conversation!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay updated on Biharâ€™s latest developments! Follow www.biharsay.com and join our 10,000+ global community today!\u003c/p\u003e",
