        "id":  "from-strangers-to-family-how-two-nurses-are-changing-the-lives-of-abandoned-elderly-in-bihar",
        "title":  "How Two Nurses Are Changing the Lives of Abandoned Elderly in Bihar!",
        "summary":  "A Heartwarming Story of Kindness Beyond Duty Imagine being abandoned by your own, left in an old age home to spend your days longing for love. Now, picture two young nurses, Anupriya and Nishu from SKMCH, stepping in to fill that ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA Heartwarming Story of Kindness Beyond Duty Imagine being abandoned by your own, left in an old age home to spend your days longing for love. Now, picture two young nurses, Anupriya and Nishu from SKMCH, stepping in to fill that voidâ€”not just as caregivers but as family. Their mission? To bring joy, health, and dignity back to the lives of those who have been cast aside. The Power of Selfless Service At a time when many see aged parents as burdens, Anupriya and Nishu have turned their nursing profession into a lifelong service to humanity. Every month, they visit old age homes in Muzaffarpur and Patna, offering medical care, companionship, and emotional warmth. These elderly souls, once rejected by their families, now find son-daughter-like love in these two young women. More Than Just Medical Care Their visits go beyond routine check-ups. They: Celebrate festivals with the elderly, ensuring they never feel left out. Cook homemade meals and personally serve them. Provide essential items like warm clothes in winter and summer essentials. Monitor health conditions, checking blood pressure, sugar levels, and ensuring prescribed medications are taken. Every act of kindness strengthens the bond between them and the elderly, proving that relationships built from the heart are stronger than blood ties. Listening to Stories, Sharing Smiles For Anupriya and Nishu, these visits are more than just volunteeringâ€”they are deeply personal. Sitting beside the elderly, listening to their life stories, and sharing heartfelt moments has become their way of giving back to a generation that once nurtured society. The wisdom, struggles, and triumphs they hear inspire them to continue their mission. â€œNo Elderly Should Feel Unlovedâ€ Nishu believes, â€œMany elders silently endure their pain. But when we sit with them, they open up, and we realize how a little care can change their world. If everyone contributed a little, no elderly person would feel abandoned.â€ The message is clearâ€”kindness can heal even the deepest wounds. Join the Movement This incredible story of compassion deserves to be heard. Be a part of this movement! Follow www.biharsay.com for more heart-touching updates and become a member of our 10K+ global community spreading love and positivity! Tags:Bihar news elderly care human kindness Inspirational Stories Muzaffarpur news nursing heroes old-age home SKMCH nurses\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Heartwarming Story of Kindness Beyond Duty\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine being abandoned by your own, left in an old age home to spend your days longing for love. Now, picture two young nurses, Anupriya and Nishu from SKMCH, stepping in to fill that voidâ€”not just as caregivers but as family. Their mission? To bring joy, health, and dignity back to the lives of those who have been cast aside.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Power of Selfless Service\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt a time when many see aged parents as burdens, Anupriya and Nishu have turned their nursing profession into a lifelong service to humanity. Every month, they visit old age homes in Muzaffarpur and Patna, offering medical care, companionship, and emotional warmth. These elderly souls, once rejected by their families, now find son-daughter-like love in these two young women.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore Than Just Medical Care\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir visits go beyond routine check-ups. They:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCelebrate festivals with the elderly, ensuring they never feel left out. Cook homemade meals and personally serve them. Provide essential items like warm clothes in winter and summer essentials. Monitor health conditions, checking blood pressure, sugar levels, and ensuring prescribed medications are taken.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery act of kindness strengthens the bond between them and the elderly, proving that relationships built from the heart are stronger than blood ties.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eListening to Stories, Sharing Smiles\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Anupriya and Nishu, these visits are more than just volunteeringâ€”they are deeply personal. Sitting beside the elderly, listening to their life stories, and sharing heartfelt moments has become their way of giving back to a generation that once nurtured society. The wisdom, struggles, and triumphs they hear inspire them to continue their mission.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œNo Elderly Should Feel Unlovedâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNishu believes, â€œMany elders silently endure their pain. But when we sit with them, they open up, and we realize how a little care can change their world. If everyone contributed a little, no elderly person would feel abandoned.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe message is clearâ€”kindness can heal even the deepest wounds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin the Movement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis incredible story of compassion deserves to be heard. Be a part of this movement! Follow www.biharsay.com for more heart-touching updates and become a member of our 10K+ global community spreading love and positivity!\u003c/p\u003e",
