        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eImagine a Bihar where women donâ€™t just support farmingâ€”they lead it. That future is here! With 52 lakh women farmers adopting modern agricultural techniques and 2,000 Jeevika Didis launching customer service centers, Bihar is setting new benchmarks in rural empowerment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWomen Farmers Shaping the Future of Agriculture\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s government has set an ambitious goal: by 2025, 52 lakh women farmers will integrate advanced farming techniques. This initiative will not only boost productivity but also improve their financial independence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo strengthen market access, authorities are linking these women with Farmer Producer Companies (FPCs). Additionally, they are establishing 85 organic farming clusters, promoting eco-friendly methods while ensuring a steady income for women farmers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBreaking Barriers: Women-Led Service Centers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor years, men dominated customer service centers in Bihar. But now, 2,000 Jeevika Didis will run these centers, delivering banking and digital services to rural communities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo support this shift, the government is facilitating â‚¹10,000 crore in bank loans for these women entrepreneurs. Deputy CM \u0026 Finance Minister Samrat Choudhary announced this financial push in the 2025-26 budget speech, underscoring Biharâ€™s commitment to womenâ€™s economic participation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpanding Livelihoods: Beekeeping \u0026 Dairy Farming\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond agriculture, Bihar is helping women gain financial independence in other sectors:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ Beekeeping Boom â€“ Over 11,789 women from Self-Help Groups (SHGs) are now beekeeping entrepreneurs, producing more than 2,724.7 tons of honey so far.ðŸ¥› Dairy \u0026 Animal Husbandry â€“ The government plans to connect 10 lakh families with dairy farming by 2025, increasing rural incomes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ‚¹150 Crore Boost for Women Entrepreneurs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is also investing in Self-Help Groups (SHGs) to expand financial opportunities. This year alone, the government is providing â‚¹150 crore in funding, supporting 1.03 lakh new SHGs and impacting 20 lakh families.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin the Movement!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s women are redefining agriculture and entrepreneurship. Stay informed and be part of this transformation! Visit www.biharsay.com for more updates and join our 10K+ global community celebrating Biharâ€™s progress!\u003c/p\u003e",
