        "id":  "kaimur-wildlife-sanctuary-to-become-bihars-largest-tiger-reserve-4x-bigger-than-valmiki",
        "title":  "Kaimur Wildlife Sanctuary to Become Biharâ€™s Largest Tiger Reserve | 4X Bigger Than Valmiki",
        "summary":  "# Kaimur Wildlife Sanctuary: Biharâ€™s Next Big Tiger Reserve, 4X Bigger Than Valmiki Bihar is set to witness a game-changing transformation in its wildlife conservation efforts! Kaimur Wildlife Sanctuary is on its way to becoming...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e# Kaimur Wildlife Sanctuary: Biharâ€™s Next Big Tiger Reserve, 4X Bigger Than Valmiki\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is set to witness a game-changing transformation in its wildlife conservation efforts! Kaimur Wildlife Sanctuary is on its way to becoming Biharâ€™s second Tiger Reserve, a title currently held only by Valmiki Tiger Reserve (VTR). The most striking part? It will be four times bigger than VTR, making it one of the largest tiger habitats in the region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBig Plans for Kaimur: Tigers to Arrive Soon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Central Government has initiated the process to officially designate Kaimur Wildlife Sanctuary as a Tiger Reserve. Starting in May 2025, authorities will relocate tigers from other reserves across India to Kaimur, ensuring a thriving population.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrently, VTR houses 54 tigers, but Kaimurâ€™s vast expanse will allow the population to grow significantly. The National Tiger Conservation Authority (NTCA) has developed strategic guidelines to protect and monitor these tigers effectively.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEco-Sensitive Zone: No More Industries Near Kaimur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure maximum conservation, the government will designate Kaimur as an Eco-Sensitive Zone (ESZ). Once implemented, the 10 km buffer zone will prevent industrial projects, preserving the sanctuaryâ€™s natural ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOfficials have marked 450 sq. km as the core zone, where human activities will be strictly prohibited. The buffer zone, spanning 1050 sq. km, will include Shergarh Fort, ancient temples, and historic villages, making it a significant eco-tourism hub.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA 300-KM Wildlife Corridor Connecting Four States\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKaimurâ€™s location plays a crucial role in tiger conservation! It connects with tiger reserves in Uttar Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh, and Jharkhand, forming a 300-km wildlife corridor. This link enhances tiger movement, reduces habitat isolation, and strengthens conservation efforts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNorth: Connects with Sonbhadra \u0026 Mirzapur (UP) leading to Dubri Tiger Reserve (MP) South: Extends towards Palamu Tiger Reserve \u0026 Garhwa Forests (Jharkhand)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis corridor will help maintain a healthy and diverse tiger population in the region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Proof: Tiger Sightings in Kaimur Since 2017\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTigers have roamed Kaimurâ€™s forests since 2017. In 2019, wildlife experts discovered tiger footprints and scat samples. Further confirmation came in 2020, when camera traps captured tigers moving through the sanctuary.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese findings accelerated conservation efforts, pushing authorities to take action.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVTR Tigers to be Relocated for Safety\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTigers often stray from Valmiki Tiger Reserve, leading to human-wildlife conflicts. Now, wildlife officials will rescue these tigers and relocate them to Kaimurâ€™s secure habitat, reducing such incidents.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Next? The Final Steps\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar government has ramped up efforts to finalize Kaimurâ€™s Tiger Reserve status. Officials will submit the proposal to declare it an Eco-Sensitive Zone to the Central Government by March 20, 2025. Once approved, tiger relocation and conservation programs will proceed without delay.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay updated with Biharâ€™s biggest wildlife stories! Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 10K-strong global community.\u003c/p\u003e",
