        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Skyward Surge: How Aviation is Redefining Connectivity in the State The skies over Bihar are buzzing like never before! In just two decades, the state has witnessed an unprecedented 17-fold surge in air travel. With new ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Skyward Surge: How Aviation is Redefining Connectivity in the State\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe skies over Bihar are buzzing like never before! In just two decades, the state has witnessed an unprecedented 17-fold surge in air travel. With new airports, expanded infrastructure, and booming passenger traffic, Bihar is soaring into a future of seamless connectivity and economic growth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Two Airports to a Sky Full of Possibilities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBack in 2005, Bihar had only two operational airportsâ€”Patna and Gaya. Today, the state is investing heavily in aviation, ensuring that no location is more than 200 km away from an airport. Chief Secretary Amrit Lal Meena confirmed that this ambitious plan is in full swing, transforming Bihar into a key aviation hub.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAviation Boom: Passenger and Aircraft Growth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s aviation landscape has evolved drastically over the last 20 years:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2005-06: 4,788 flights carried 2.48 lakh passengers. 2023-24: 29,614 flights transported 42.86 lakh travelers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThatâ€™s a 6x rise in flights and a 17x increase in passengersâ€”a staggering growth that highlights the stateâ€™s potential as a major air transit hub.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDarbhanga Airport: The Lifeline of North Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaunched on November 8, 2020, Darbhanga Airport quickly became one of Biharâ€™s busiest hubs:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2023-24: Over 3,335 flights took off, carrying 5.26 lakh passengers. The state has sanctioned â‚¹245 crore for a 90-acre expansion, setting the stage for international operations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpcoming and Expanding Airports in Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1ï¸âƒ£ Raxaul Airport\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLand Acquisition: 139 acres. Investment: â‚¹207 crore. Developed by: Airports Authority of India (AAI).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2ï¸âƒ£ Birpur (Supaul) Airport\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLand Acquisition: 88.83 acres. Investment: â‚¹42.37 crore. Part of the UDAN scheme to boost regional air travel.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3ï¸âƒ£ Purnia (Chunapur) Airport\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMajor Road Project: Four-lane road from Goasi to Chunapur. AAI Initiative: Civil enclave construction began in March 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4ï¸âƒ£ Bihta Airport: The Game Changer\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInvestment: â‚¹459.99 crore. Aircraft Capacity: A-321, B-737-800, A-320. Expected to decongest Patna Airport by 2027.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Future of Air Connectivity in Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar government is also planning to develop smaller airstrips in Bhagalpur, Valmikinagar, Madhubani, Munger, Saharsa, and Muzaffarpur under the UDAN scheme.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJanuary 13, 2025: State approval granted. February 19, 2025: The Civil Aviation Ministryâ€™s project evaluation committee gave the green light.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith massive investments, strategic expansions, and government backing, Biharâ€™s aviation future is brighter than ever. This growth will fuel tourism, business, and overall developmentâ€”bringing the state closer to global connectivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay ahead with the latest updates on Biharâ€™s aviation revolution! Follow www.biharsay.com and become a part of our 10k+ strong global community!\u003c/p\u003e",
