        "title":  "4 Years of \u0027Letâ€™s Inspire Bihar\u0027: Empowering Bihar, Transforming Lives",
        "summary":  "Letâ€™s Inspire Bihar: A Movement Towards a Developed Bihar In a grand celebration filled with hope and determination, â€˜Letâ€™s Inspire Biharâ€™ marked its fourth foundation day as the â€˜Viksit Bihar Sankalp Mahasabhaâ€™ on Mar...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eLetâ€™s Inspire Bihar: A Movement Towards a Developed Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a grand celebration filled with hope and determination, â€˜Letâ€™s Inspire Biharâ€™ marked its fourth foundation day as the â€˜Viksit Bihar Sankalp Mahasabhaâ€™ on March 22, 2025, at Bapu Sabhagar, Patna. More than just a commemoration, it was a collective resolution to transform Bihar into a developed and progressive state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Gathering of Visionaries\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOver 10,000 dedicated individuals attended this historic event, including intellectuals, academicians, spiritual leaders, university students, youth volunteers, entrepreneurs, and social activists. Attendees traveled from all districts of Bihar, across India, and even from abroad. Notably, Prashant Kumar, an entrepreneur from London, participated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe movement, led by renowned IPS officer Vikas Vaibhav, has gained immense traction. With a vision to revive Biharâ€™s civilizational roots in education, equality, and entrepreneurship, â€˜Letâ€™s Inspire Biharâ€™ has emerged as one of the most impactful non-political movements in the state. Since its inception in 2021, over 1,85,000 individuals have pledged to contribute to Biharâ€™s transformation by 2047.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Genesis of the Movement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe idea of â€˜Letâ€™s Inspire Biharâ€™ took shape on January 12, 2021, Swami Vivekanandaâ€™s birth anniversary. Inspired by interactions with Biharâ€™s youth, Vikas Vaibhav recognized the urgent need for an awakening to restore the stateâ€™s lost glory. On March 22, 2021, at Taramaá¹‡á¸al Sabhagar, Patna, the movement was officially launched with a mission to inspire every Bihari to rise above caste, creed, and ideology for the stateâ€™s progress.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVikas Vaibhavâ€™s Vision for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpeaking at Bapu Sabhagar, Vikas Vaibhav expressed pride in the movementâ€™s journey. He recalled the successful event at Bharat Mandapam, Delhi, which laid the foundation for Biharâ€™s development roadmap. Seeing thousands of determined individuals fill the venue, he confidently declared, â€œA new revolution has begun in Bihar. This is not just another movement; this is a historic call for educational, entrepreneurial, and social transformation.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVaibhav highlighted Biharâ€™s per capita monthly income of â‚¹5028, compared to â‚¹48000 in Sikkim and â‚¹32000 in Tamil Nadu. With a growth rate of 14.5%, Bihar needs a stronger push for sustainable progress. â€œIf we continue at this pace, our per capita income will only reach â‚¹20,000 in the next decade. Do we want Bihar to develop so slowly?â€ he asked. The audience responded with a resounding â€œNo!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Movement Beyond Politics\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne of â€˜Letâ€™s Inspire Biharâ€™sâ€™ key aspects is its non-political stance. Vikas Vaibhav reaffirmed that real change comes from societal awareness and action, not political affiliations. â€œIf politics could bring change, I would have joined it first. But true transformation happens through education, entrepreneurship, and equality,â€ he stated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe urged people to move beyond caste-based politics and strive for a meritocratic Bihar. Expressing concern over the negative perception of â€˜Bihariâ€™ in other states, he emphasized that this collective effort could restore the stateâ€™s dignity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOvercoming Challenges with Resilience\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVaibhav shared personal struggles, including a period of financial uncertainty when he received no salary for four months. His father supported him during this time. Despite challenges, his dedication to Bihar remained firm. â€œBihar is at a take-off stage. Now is the time to propel it forward. If we all contribute, nothing can stop this state from rising,â€ he asserted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWomen Empowerment \u0026 Education Initiatives\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHighlighting womenâ€™s role in Biharâ€™s transformation, Vaibhav praised the â€˜Gargi Chapterâ€™ of â€˜Letâ€™s Inspire Bihar,â€™ which runs 24 education centers across various districts. Women manage 19 of these centers, showcasing their growing leadership in the movement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe concluded by sharing his contact number with the audience, urging them to join the movement. â€œChange requires collective effort. Letâ€™s make this movement a peopleâ€™s revolution.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Road Ahead: A Collective Responsibility\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs Bihar stands at a turning point, initiatives like â€˜Letâ€™s Inspire Biharâ€™ offer hope. The state, known for its rich history and intellectual legacy, is witnessing a new era of awakening. The â€˜Viksit Bihar Sankalp Mahasabhaâ€™ was more than an eventâ€”it was proof of the power of unity, determination, and vision.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith thousands committed to the cause, Biharâ€™s journey toward development is no longer a distant dream but an achievable reality. The question remains: Will you be part of this historic transformation?\u003c/p\u003e",
