        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Mentha Boom: The Fragrant Revolution Set to Transform Agriculture Bihar is stepping up its game in aromatic farming! With mentha, khus, tulsi, and lemongrass cultivation expanding rapidly, farmers in the state are set to...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Mentha Boom: The Fragrant Revolution Set to Transform Agriculture\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is stepping up its game in aromatic farming! With mentha, khus, tulsi, and lemongrass cultivation expanding rapidly, farmers in the state are set to benefit from increased subsidies and investment. But what makes Biharâ€™s mentha and khus stand out? Letâ€™s dive into the details of this thriving industry.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Mentha and Khus: A Hidden Goldmine\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to the Central Medicinal Plant Research Institute, Bihar produces the highest quality mentha and khus in India. Their fragrance is 7% stronger than those grown in other states, making them highly sought after by processing companies. As a result, many firms now engage in contract farming with Biharâ€™s farmers, ensuring better prices and consistent demand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpanding Cultivation: The Governmentâ€™s New Plan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar agriculture department plans to increase the acreage of aromatic crops through structured planning and subsidies. Currently, the state grows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMentha: 5,000 hectares (Darbhanga, Siwan, Gopalganj, Chhapra, Saran, Muzaffarpur, Samastipur) Khus: 500 hectares (Saharsa, Rohtas, Aurangabad, Kaimur, Bhojpur, Samastipur, Begusarai) Tulsi: 100-150 hectares Lemongrass: 100 hectares\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith government support, these numbers will rise significantly, making Bihar a major hub for aromatic crop production.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRevival of the Mentha Market\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor years, mentha oil has been an essential ingredient in pain relief medicines, chewing gum, and toothpaste. While Uttar Pradesh leads in production, Bihar ranks second, contributing a significant share. However, when Chinese menthol entered the market, demand for Indian mentha dropped.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, companies are reinvesting in Biharâ€™s mentha farming, bringing back industry growth. Mentha oil currently sells at â‚¹1,000 per liter, making it a lucrative choice for farmers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Biharâ€™s Aromatic Farming is the Future\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGlobal Demand: With rising interest in natural and organic products, demand for mentha and khus continues to grow worldwide. Better Pricing: Contract farming guarantees assured payments and premium rates for farmers. Government Support: The state offers subsidies to encourage cultivation and expansion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s agricultural landscape is evolving, and aromatic crops are leading the way! If you want to stay updated on Biharâ€™s agricultural growth, innovations, and opportunities, follow www.biharsay.com and become a part of our 10k+ community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
