        "id":  "nandangarh-festival-2025-a-grand-revival-of-bihars-historic-legacy",
        "title":  "NandanGarh Festival 2025 â€“ A Grand Revival of Biharâ€™s Historic Legacy",
        "summary":  "The Grand Comeback of NandanGarh Mahotsav After nearly a decade, the much-anticipated NandanGarh Mahotsav is making a grand return! The historic town of Lauria-NandanGarh in Bihar is set to host an extraordinary cultural event. Di...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eThe Grand Comeback of NandanGarh Mahotsav\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter nearly a decade, the much-anticipated NandanGarh Mahotsav is making a grand return! The historic town of Lauria-NandanGarh in Bihar is set to host an extraordinary cultural event. District Magistrate Dinesh Kumar Rai and senior officials have meticulously planned the festival to captivate visitors once again. Minister Janak Ram will inaugurate the event at Sahu Jain High School Grounds on Sunday. The festivities will run from 4 PM to 9 PM.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAttendees will enjoy spectacular performances by local and state artists. They will also explore the historical significance of Lauria and NandanGarh. The administration has ensured strong security and seamless arrangements to make this festival memorable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Historical Significance of Lauria-NandanGarh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNandanGarh â€“ A Legacy of the Nanda Dynasty \u0026 Buddhist Era\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce a magnificent palace, NandanGarh stands as a symbol of the Nanda Dynasty and Buddhist heritage. Historians call Lauria the â€˜Mother of Historyâ€™, tracing its origins to Lohitya Nagar, mentioned in Shanti Awadheshâ€™s book on Pataliputra.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe ancient Nanda Empire, under Samrat Mahapadma Nanda, stretched from the Shivalik foothills to the Vindhya range. He expanded his kingdom and married Maurya, a young woman from Kushinagarâ€™s Rampur Janpad. Their son, Chandragupta Maurya, emerged as a warrior. As a young commander, Chandragupta led several significant battles, shaping his destiny and laying the foundation for the Mauryan Empire.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Buddhist Connection â€“ A Sacred Landmark\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLauria-NandanGarh holds deep Buddhist significance. According to Havaldar Tripathiâ€™s book â€˜Bhagwan Buddha and Biharâ€™, Gautam Buddha passed through this region while traveling to Kushinagar for Mahaparinirvana. Before crossing the Ganges and reaching Kesariya, Buddha stopped in Lauria. Here, he shaved his head and declared it his place of enlightenment. His sacred hair was enshrined in a mound, while his followers sent the remaining relics worldwide. Even today, Buddhist monks and devotees from across the world visit Sahu Jainâ€™s ancient mound, offering prayers and circumambulating the sacred site. They also revere the Ashoka Pillar and NandanGarh mound, where Buddhist monks practiced Vedic and Tantric rituals for centuries.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Cultural Extravaganza Awaits!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis yearâ€™s NandanGarh Mahotsav is more than historyâ€”it revives culture, traditions, and heritage. The festival will showcase soulful performances by regional and national artists, engaging the audience with music, dance, and theatrical acts. Visitors will also dive into Lauria-NandanGarhâ€™s glorious past, experiencing its rich cultural essence firsthand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t miss this once-in-a-decade celebration! Join this journey through history, culture, and legacy. For regular updates and to be part of our 10K+ global community, visit www.biharsay.com now!\u003c/p\u003e",
