        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Pride: Anushka Abhishek Heads to Russia for Karate World Cup Bihar is beaming with pride! Muzaffarpurâ€™s 13-year-old karate sensation, Anushka Abhishek, has secured her spot in the Indian team for the Karate World Cup 2...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Pride: Anushka Abhishek Heads to Russia for Karate World Cup\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is beaming with pride! Muzaffarpurâ€™s 13-year-old karate sensation, Anushka Abhishek, has secured her spot in the Indian team for the Karate World Cup 2025, set to take place in Moscow, Russia, from April 4 to April 8, 2025. Competing in the Under-14 Kumite Fight (45kg category), Anushka is all set to showcase her skills on the global stage!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Historic Feat for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnushka is Biharâ€™s first-ever karateka to compete in the Karate World Cup, making her selection a monumental achievement for the stateâ€™s sports community. The news has sparked excitement among karate enthusiasts, coaches, and fellow athletes. Her parents, Annu Abhishek and Preeti Kumari, along with her trainers and supporters, are overwhelmed with joy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYears of Dedication and Hard Work\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnushka has been training rigorously for the past four years at RAS World Martial Arts Academy, under the expert guidance of Sensei Suraj Pandit. Her commitment, discipline, and relentless spirit have propelled her to this level. She has fought through intense competition to earn this golden opportunity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Role of Coaches and Mentors\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBehind every great athlete is a mentor who guides them to success. Anushkaâ€™s selection wouldnâ€™t have been possible without the support of her head coach Shihan E. Rahul Srivastava, who will also be accompanying Team India to Russia. Under his leadership, the team is expected to deliver an outstanding performance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFederationâ€™s Support and Sponsorship\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe India Zen Do Shin Karate Federation, led by Shihan Shilpi Sonam, has played a key role in Anushkaâ€™s journey. They officially handed over her selection letter and provided her with a full sponsorship kit to support her in this prestigious tournament.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Wave of Support Across Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe entire Bihar sports community is celebrating Anushkaâ€™s achievement. Messages of congratulations and best wishes are pouring in from across the state. This milestone is a significant boost for martial arts in Bihar, inspiring young athletes to pursue karate at an international level.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoad to Glory in Moscow\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith only days left for the tournament, Anushka is intensifying her training, aiming to bring home a medal and make India proud. As she prepares to take on the worldâ€™s best, Bihar stands firmly behind her, cheering her on!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated with More Bihar Sports News\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow www.biharsay.com for the latest updates on Biharâ€™s sports stars, and become part of our 10,000+ strong community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
