        "title":  "Railway Ministry Approves Rs 6.78 Crore Underpass Project",
        "summary":  "Finally, a Victory for Tankuppa Residents! Railway Ministry Approves Rs 6.78 Crore Underpass Project A Long-Awaited Breakthrough for Tankuppa After years of relentless campaigning and protests, the people of Tankuppa in Biharâ€™s ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eFinally, a Victory for Tankuppa Residents! Railway Ministry Approves Rs 6.78 Crore Underpass Project\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Long-Awaited Breakthrough for Tankuppa\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter years of relentless campaigning and protests, the people of Tankuppa in Biharâ€™s Gaya district have achieved a major victory. The Railway Ministry has sanctioned Rs 6.78 crore for the construction of an underpass near Jianbigha, adjacent to Tankuppa Station. This long-overdue project will finally ease traffic congestion and improve safety for commuters.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Role of Union Minister Jitan Ram Manjhi\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis milestone wouldnâ€™t have been possible without the persistent efforts of Union Minister Jitan Ram Manjhi. The residents had been demanding either an overbridge or an underpass for years. However, their requests were repeatedly overlooked. Frustrated by the inaction, they even boycotted voting in past elections as a form of protest.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eManjhi had promised during the Lok Sabha elections that he would address this pressing issue if elected. Staying true to his word, he took the matter to Railway Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw, leading to the long-awaited approval of the underpass project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResidentsâ€™ Struggles and Protests Pay Off\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Gaya Dhanbad Grand Cord Railway Sangharsh Samiti, led by President E Nandlal Manjhi, played a crucial role in this movement. Over the years, the community submitted multiple petitions to authorities, yet their appeals were ignored. The struggle intensified when residents staged protests and escalated their demands through various platforms.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, in a meeting last month, a delegation from the Sangharsh Samiti met Jitan Ram Manjhi and formally presented a memorandum. Recognizing the urgency, he took immediate action, pushing for the projectâ€™s approval.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Next for Tankuppa?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the funding secured and approvals in place, the focus now shifts to execution. The underpass will significantly improve connectivity, reduce travel time, and enhance safety for pedestrians and motorists. The exact timeline for construction is yet to be announced, but locals are hopeful that work will begin soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMembers of the Sangharsh Samiti, including Vinod Singh, Vijay Yadav, Jhalak Singh, Rajkumar Sao, Mohd. Rizwan, Dilip Singh, Kapil Yadav, Munna Pandey, Dilip Yadav, Umesh Das, and Sudhir Sao, have expressed their gratitude to Jitan Ram Manjhi for fulfilling his commitment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay updated with real-time Bihar news! Visit www.biharsay.com and become part of our 10k+ global community.\u003c/p\u003e",
