        "title":  "Bihar Announces Cheaper Electricity for Smart Prepaid Meter Users from April 1!",
        "summary":  "Are you a smart prepaid meter user in Bihar? If yes, hereâ€™s some fantastic news! The Bihar State Electricity Regulatory Commission (BSERC) has announced new electricity rates effective from April 1, 2025. This means you will enj...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eAre you a smart prepaid meter user in Bihar? If yes, hereâ€™s some fantastic news! The Bihar State Electricity Regulatory Commission (BSERC) has announced new electricity rates effective from April 1, 2025. This means you will enjoy cheaper electricity bills and additional benefits.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLower Electricity Rates for Smart Prepaid Meter Users\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new tariff brings significant relief for prepaid meter consumers. Specifically:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou will save 25 paise per unit if you use a smart prepaid meter. Rural consumers will benefit from a 54 paise per unit discount. For six months after installation, there will be no penalty for exceeding load.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you live in a rural area and have installed a smart prepaid meter, you can enjoy a total benefit of 79 paise per unit on your electricity consumption.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRelief for Rural \u0026 Industrial Consumers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new tariff benefits extend beyond just prepaid users. Additionally:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRural consumers using over 50 units per month will now pay 54 paise less per unit. The government rejected a proposed electricity tariff hike for industrial consumers, ensuring stable rates. Industrial users making digital payments will receive up to â‚¹50,000 in discounts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCold Storage \u0026 Agriculture Sector Gains\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo support the agricultural sector, the Bihar government has introduced a separate category for cold storage facilities. Consequently, this ensures fair electricity rates for storing perishable agricultural produce.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCold storages with a contract demand of up to 74 kW now fall under LT-IAS. For HT cold storage (11 kV), a new category has been introduced for facilities ranging from 50 kVA to 1500 kVA.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Electricity Rates from April 1, 2025\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHereâ€™s a quick look at the revised electricity rates:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith these changes, electricity will become more affordable across Bihar, benefiting millions of users.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ’¡ Want to stay updated on more such policy changes and benefits? Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 10K+ strong community!\u003c/p\u003e",
