        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Mega Road Project: 5400 KM in 365 Days â€“ A Game Changer! ðŸš§ Bihar is witnessing a historic transformation! The state government has set an ambitious targetâ€”building 5400 KM of roads within a year. This initiative a...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Mega Road Project: 5400 KM in 365 Days â€“ A Game Changer! ðŸš§\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is witnessing a historic transformation! The state government has set an ambitious targetâ€”building 5400 KM of roads within a year. This initiative aims to improve rural connectivity, boost development, and enhance accessibility across thousands of villages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMission: Pothole-Free Roads by June!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Rural Works Department has launched a massive initiative. Within the next three months, it plans to make all rural roads pothole-free. To achieve this, the government has allocated â‚¹20,626 crore for the project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s in the Plan?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAuthorities will repair 13,452 roads spanning 23,541 KM. Workers are already constructing 7518 KM of roads. Under Mukhyamantri Gram Sampark Yojana, the government will invest â‚¹6000 crore to connect 2500 new habitations. Engineers will renovate 31,031 KM of roads that have exceeded their repair period. Construction crews will build 700 new bridges with an investment of â‚¹3000 crore.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Road Revolution: The Journey So Far\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore 2005, Biharâ€™s rural connectivity was in a dire state. The lack of infrastructure hindered economic growth. However, Chief Minister Nitish Kumarâ€™s leadership has driven massive road expansion:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2005: Bihar had only 8,000 KM of rural roads. Now: The network stretches over 1,17,913 KM. The Rural Works Department has developed 83% of Biharâ€™s roads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBetter roads lead to faster transportation, improved access to markets, enhanced healthcare facilities, and more job opportunities. Farmers can transport goods easily, children can reach schools safely, and rural businesses can grow rapidly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Road Ahead: 2025 \u0026 Beyond\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy March 2026, authorities plan to complete the surface layer of these newly built roads. This project is a stepping stone to transforming Bihar into a state with world-class connectivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay tuned for more updates! Follow www.biharsay.com for regular insights and become part of our 10K+ global community!\u003c/p\u003e",
