        "title":  "Biharâ€™s Big Leap in Connectivity: Over 6 Railway Over Bridges (ROB) to Be Completed in 2025",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Big Leap in Connectivity: 6+ Railway Overbridges Set to Launch This Year! Biharâ€™s Connectivity Revolution Is On Track â€” Literally Bihar is all set to receive a long-awaited infrastructure boost in 2025. With over hal...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Big Leap in Connectivity: 6+ Railway Overbridges Set to Launch This Year!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Connectivity Revolution Is On Track â€” Literally\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is all set to receive a long-awaited infrastructure boost in 2025. With over half a dozen Railway Over Bridges (ROBs) nearing completion, daily commuting in several districts is about to become faster, safer, and significantly more convenient.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor decades, waiting at railway crossings has been a frustrating part of everyday life. However, with these ROBs coming into existence, that is about to change dramatically. The state is now stepping into a new era of road-rail integration and public convenience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere Are These ROBs Coming Up?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLetâ€™s take a closer look at the major ROBs under construction and their current status:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChausa-Gahmar ROB (Buxar):The rail section is complete. Meanwhile, the Bihar State Bridge Construction Corporation (BSBCC) is building the approach road, which is expected to be completed by June 2025. Buxar-Baruna ROB:Construction work is actively underway and, notably, it is on track to finish by mid-2025. Karbhandia-Mughalsarai ROB (Rohtas):While the railway portion is progressing, the approach road is also under construction. The full structure is likely to be completed by the end of this year. Gangoli-Deoria-Pahleja ROB (Rohtas):In this case, BSBCC is working on the access roads, and the deadline for completion remains set for 2025. Pusauli-Muthani ROB (Kaimur):Since the railway structure is already complete, the focus is now on finalizing the approach road. Progress is steady and in line with projections. Parsauni-Sitamarhi ROB (Sitamarhi):Although the railway portion is still ongoing, the approach road is expected to be completed by December 2025. Naugachhia-Katoria ROB (Bhagalpur):Fortunately, this ROB is close to full completion and is slated to be ready by year-end.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChausa-Gahmar ROB (Buxar):The rail section is complete. Meanwhile, the Bihar State Bridge Construction Corporation (BSBCC) is building the approach road, which is expected to be completed by June 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuxar-Baruna ROB:Construction work is actively underway and, notably, it is on track to finish by mid-2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKarbhandia-Mughalsarai ROB (Rohtas):While the railway portion is progressing, the approach road is also under construction. The full structure is likely to be completed by the end of this year.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGangoli-Deoria-Pahleja ROB (Rohtas):In this case, BSBCC is working on the access roads, and the deadline for completion remains set for 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePusauli-Muthani ROB (Kaimur):Since the railway structure is already complete, the focus is now on finalizing the approach road. Progress is steady and in line with projections.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eParsauni-Sitamarhi ROB (Sitamarhi):Although the railway portion is still ongoing, the approach road is expected to be completed by December 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNaugachhia-Katoria ROB (Bhagalpur):Fortunately, this ROB is close to full completion and is slated to be ready by year-end.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy These ROBs Matter to Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese overbridges are more than just infrastructure projects. In fact, they offer real, measurable benefits that touch lives daily.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSmoother traffic flow:No more waiting for trains to pass; vehicles will move seamlessly. Fewer road accidents:As crossings get replaced, the risk of mishaps will reduce significantly. Saved travel time:Time saved on the road translates to more productivity and less stress. Boosted local economy:Faster, safer travel means better access to goods, jobs, and education.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSmoother traffic flow:No more waiting for trains to pass; vehicles will move seamlessly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFewer road accidents:As crossings get replaced, the risk of mishaps will reduce significantly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSaved travel time:Time saved on the road translates to more productivity and less stress.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoosted local economy:Faster, safer travel means better access to goods, jobs, and education.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, the completion of these ROBs sends a strong message that Bihar is finally catching up on long-pending infrastructure promises.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhoâ€™s Making It Happen?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese projects fall under a joint effort â€” the Cost Sharing Scheme between Indian Railways and the Government of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Railway Ministry takes care of the primary bridge structure. Meanwhile, the Bihar State Bridge Construction Corporation (BSBCC) is tasked with building and completing the approach roads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Railway Ministry takes care of the primary bridge structure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMeanwhile, the Bihar State Bridge Construction Corporation (BSBCC) is tasked with building and completing the approach roads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis strong collaboration is a reflection of effective public sector coordination â€” one that prioritizes public safety and convenience over delays and red tape.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Next for Biharâ€™s Infrastructure?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile these ROBs are a significant achievement, theyâ€™re only a piece of the puzzle. As Bihar continues to grow, such developments pave the way for further progress in transportation, logistics, and urban mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, the commitment to completing these projects within this year reflects a focused approach to governance. Clearly, Bihar is not just planning for the future â€” itâ€™s building it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated With the Voice of Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant real updates that matter to you and your community? Interested in tracking development stories before they make national headlines? Looking to join a fast-growing, engaged audience?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant real updates that matter to you and your community?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInterested in tracking development stories before they make national headlines?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLooking to join a fast-growing, engaged audience?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Visit www.biharsay.com and become part of our 10,000+ global community. Stay informed. Stay empowered.\u003c/p\u003e",
