        "title":  "Patna Metro Speeds Up: Bihar Deploys 397 Engineers for Urban Projects",
        "summary":  "Patna Metro Gets a Boost: 397 Engineers Join to Transform Urban Bihar When promises turn into action, cities rise. Thatâ€™s exactly whatâ€™s happening in Bihar right now. In a significant move aimed at accelerating infrastructure ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna Metro Gets a Boost: 397 Engineers Join to Transform Urban Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen promises turn into action, cities rise. Thatâ€™s exactly whatâ€™s happening in Bihar right now.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a significant move aimed at accelerating infrastructure development, the Bihar Government has deployed 397 Junior Engineers (JEs) across multiple urban departments. This includes Patna Metro Rail Corporation (PMRC), BUIDCO, the Bihar Housing Board, and several municipal bodies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese engineers are not just numbers. They represent a focused mission to build faster, smarter, and stronger cities across the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFast-Tracking Patna Metro: 19 Engineers Deployed\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo speed up the ambitious Patna Metro project, 19 Junior Engineers have joined the PMRC. Among them, 11 are from the civil stream, while 4 each belong to the mechanical and electrical branches. These professionals will work on realigning timelines, coordinating departments, and ensuring seamless implementation of the metroâ€™s priority corridor, which the government aims to launch by 15 August 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks to this strategic deployment, the metro now has a better shot at becoming a functioning reality rather than an unfinished dream.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUrban Development Projects Finally Gain Momentum\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond the metro, these engineers will actively support critical urban projects throughout Bihar. Their duties range from improving road networks to enhancing water supply, from managing sewage systems to overseeing public building construction.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUrban Development and Housing Minister Jivesh Kumar stated that the deployment of these engineers will significantly boost work under key schemes such as the Jal Jeevan Hariyali Mission and accelerate progress on facilities like the Samrat Ashok Bhawan.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs a result, citizens across Bihar will begin to notice visible improvements in civic services and urban infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTransparent Recruitment and Immediate Joining Orders\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar Technical Services Commission (BTSC) conducted the hiring for these engineering roles. Hereâ€™s how the deployment breaks down:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e350 Civil Engineers 35 Mechanical Engineers 12 Electrical Engineers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e350 Civil Engineers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e35 Mechanical Engineers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e12 Electrical Engineers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach engineer has been instructed to report to their designated department within one week, carrying their original documents and verification proof. This immediate onboarding ensures thereâ€™s no delay in project execution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDepartments like BUIDCO, municipal corporations, and the Bihar Housing Board are now equipped with fresh talent ready to drive change on the ground.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis Move Signals a Real Shift in Biharâ€™s Urban Future\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor years, development in Bihar has been discussed more than delivered. But this time, it feels different. This isnâ€™t just about policy â€” itâ€™s about presence. The presence of trained, on-ground professionals ready to put plans into action.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom roads to rails, Biharâ€™s cities are now entering an era of visible transformation. This step may not fix everything overnight, but it undeniably puts progress back in motion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay in the Know, Stay AheadFor real-time, on-ground updates about Biharâ€™s growth stories, follow www.BiharSay.com.Join a global community of over 10,000 informed readers who believe in Biharâ€™s bright future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t just watch change happen â€” be a part of it.\u003c/p\u003e",
