        "id":  "30-salary-hike-for-ministers-of-state-rank-in-bihar-allowance-surge-and-26000-new-posts-announced",
        "title":  "30% Salary Hike for Ministers of State Rank in Biharâ€”Allowance Surge and 26,000 New Posts Announced",
        "summary":  "30% Salary Boost for Ministers of State Rank in Bihar The Bihar cabinet, under the leadership of Chief Minister Nitish Kumar, has approved a 30% hike in the monthly salary for individuals holding the Minister of State and Deputy M...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e30% Salary Boost for Ministers of State Rank in Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar cabinet, under the leadership of Chief Minister Nitish Kumar, has approved a 30% hike in the monthly salary for individuals holding the Minister of State and Deputy Minister rank.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, these office-bearers will earn â‚¹65,000 per month, marking a clear increase from the previous â‚¹50,000. This decision is expected to enhance financial parity among key administrative roles across departments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRevised Allowances Bring Further Gains\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot only have the salaries increased, but a complete allowance revision has also been rolled out. This includes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal Allowance: Increased from â‚¹55,000 to â‚¹70,000 Daily Allowance: Now â‚¹3,500 (previously â‚¹3,000) Hospitality Allowance (Minister of State Rank): Revised to â‚¹29,500 from â‚¹24,000 Hospitality Allowance (Deputy Minister Rank): Now â‚¹29,000, up from â‚¹23,500\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal Allowance: Increased from â‚¹55,000 to â‚¹70,000\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDaily Allowance: Now â‚¹3,500 (previously â‚¹3,000)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHospitality Allowance (Minister of State Rank): Revised to â‚¹29,500 from â‚¹24,000\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHospitality Allowance (Deputy Minister Rank): Now â‚¹29,000, up from â‚¹23,500\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese changes benefit not only ministers but also other officials who hold posts equivalent to these ranks. This includes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhips in both the Legislative Assembly and Council Chairpersons and members of state commissions and boards Deputy Chairmen and Deputy Chief Whips\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhips in both the Legislative Assembly and Council\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChairpersons and members of state commissions and boards\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeputy Chairmen and Deputy Chief Whips\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince they perform crucial functions, aligning their remuneration with evolving responsibilities helps improve morale and accountability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo Active Ministers of Stateâ€”Yet the Benefits Apply\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInterestingly, Bihar currently has no appointed Ministers of State or Deputy Ministers. Every member of the present cabinet holds the cabinet minister rank.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, since the status-based allowance system covers a wide range of functionaries with similar responsibilities, the revised salary and perks still apply to many officials throughout the stateâ€™s governance structure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e26,000+ New Government Posts Cleared Across Departments\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to salary changes, the cabinet has approved the creation of over 26,000 posts, significantly strengthening Biharâ€™s administrative capacity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe key highlights include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThree New Directorates within the Health Department: Public Health Directorate Health Services Directorate Medical Education Directorate 20,016 posts created under these directorates 3,306 translator posts sanctioned in the Urdu Directorate Launch of the Bihar Education Administration Cadre Rule-2025 to enhance school-level monitoring and administration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThree New Directorates within the Health Department:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePublic Health Directorate Health Services Directorate Medical Education Directorate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePublic Health Directorate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHealth Services Directorate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMedical Education Directorate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e20,016 posts created under these directorates\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3,306 translator posts sanctioned in the Urdu Directorate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaunch of the Bihar Education Administration Cadre Rule-2025 to enhance school-level monitoring and administration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis step not only addresses workforce shortages but also aligns with the stateâ€™s long-term goals for better public service delivery.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Move Toward Strengthening Public Infrastructure\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy focusing on both financial reform and workforce expansion, the Bihar cabinet demonstrates a clear intent to modernize its administrative ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDepartments like health and education are poised to benefit from increased manpower, while updated pay structures are expected to attract and retain experienced personnel across levels.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe decisions taken during the cabinet meeting are likely to improve governance processes, create employment opportunities, and streamline state-level functions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more updates on Biharâ€™s growth, reforms, and announcements, follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 10,000+ strong community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
