        "id":  "he-was-just-a-worker-from-bihar-until-gujarat-called-him-a-lifesaver",
        "title":  "He Was Just a Worker from Bihar â€” Until Gujarat Called Him a Lifesaver",
        "summary":  "â€œEk Bihari Sau Par Bhariâ€ â€“ One Manâ€™s Final Act Saved Six Lives Across State Borders When tragedy strikes, very few leave behind a legacy that lights up lives beyond their own.This is the story of Chamak Lal, a humble cran...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œEk Bihari Sau Par Bhariâ€ â€“ One Manâ€™s Final Act Saved Six Lives Across State Borders\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen tragedy strikes, very few leave behind a legacy that lights up lives beyond their own.This is the story of Chamak Lal, a humble crane operator from Bhagalpur, Bihar, whose final act of kindness in Gujarat became a tale of rare humanity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Life Interrupted, But Not in Vain\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn March 28, while working in Surat, Chamak Lal suffered a serious fall from a crane. He was rushed to the hospital, but his condition worsened. On April 1, doctors declared him brain dead.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut that wasnâ€™t where his story ended.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Bold Decision That Touched Lives\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepresentatives from Donate Life, an organization promoting life-saving choices, approached his family. Despite being overwhelmed with grief, they made a powerful decision â€” one that changed six lives.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSoon after, a green corridor was swiftly created between Surat and Ahmedabad. In just two hours, his body reached Ahmedabad, where his heart, kidneys, liver, and eyes helped patients in critical need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Son Honoured in Gujarat\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBack in Bhagalpur, Dadhichi Deh Dan Samitiâ€™s Vimal Jain took charge of bringing Chamak Lalâ€™s remains home. The Samiti didnâ€™t stop there. They pledged to support the education of his three sons:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNitish, a first-year B.A. student at TNB College Sanjeev, in Class 10 Jaikant, in Class 9\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNitish, a first-year B.A. student at TNB College\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSanjeev, in Class 10\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJaikant, in Class 9\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis support ensures his children donâ€™t have to pause their dreams while coping with loss.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond Geography, Beyond Grief\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis tale is more than just a story of loss. Itâ€™s a reminder of how one personâ€™s decision can ripple across states and hearts. Chamak Lal may have left Gujarat physically, but he remains present through six lives that now breathe easier because of him.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe may have been a worker. But in those final moments, he became a symbol of something bigger â€” unity, humanity, and the strength of selflessness.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the Bihar we donâ€™t talk about enough.This is the India we should celebrate more often.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more powerful stories like this â€” stories that go beyond headlines and highlight hope â€”Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our growing community of over 10,000+ readers across the world.\u003c/p\u003e",
