        "summary":  "Flyover News in Bihar: This City Is Quietly Racing Aheadâ€”6 Flyovers Incoming! Youâ€™ve heard about Patna. But what if we told you another city in Bihar is gearing up to become the next flyover capital? With six new flyovers and ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eFlyover News in Bihar: This City Is Quietly Racing Aheadâ€”6 Flyovers Incoming!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYouâ€™ve heard about Patna. But what if we told you another city in Bihar is gearing up to become the next flyover capital? With six new flyovers and ROBs on the cards, this transformation promises to redefine how the city moves, grows, and connects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile most still guess which city it is, preparations are already underway. Officials have completed land surveys, identified government land, and finalized estimates. Now, private land acquisition is the final step before construction begins.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePeople Demanded, The Government Responded\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe momentum began with repeated appeals from locals in Manpurâ€™s Patwatoli area, backed strongly by social and weaver communities. For years, traffic congestion choked the cityâ€™s daily life.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInstead of turning a blind eye, the state government acted swiftly. After granting approval, they launched technical surveys and finalized the Detailed Project Report (DPR) without delay. The result? A transformation plan ready to roll.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSix Flyovers That Will Reshape the City\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHereâ€™s how the cityâ€™s roadmap will change:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA major flyover will connect Manpurâ€™s six-lane bridge directly to the Gayaâ€“Nawada Road near Mehta Petrol Pump. Another stretch will run 700 meters from Mufassil Mode to Khijarsarai Road. A third section will link the new Jagjivan College building on Sitakund Road.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA major flyover will connect Manpurâ€™s six-lane bridge directly to the Gayaâ€“Nawada Road near Mehta Petrol Pump.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnother stretch will run 700 meters from Mufassil Mode to Khijarsarai Road.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA third section will link the new Jagjivan College building on Sitakund Road.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe total estimated cost is â‚¹350 crore, and construction starts by May 2025, according to DM Dr. Tyagarajan S.M..\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy These Flyovers Matter\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond easing traffic, these flyovers are expected to boost tourism. The city will become more accessible from Rajgir, Bodh Gaya, and Vishnupad Temple, making travel easier for both locals and visitors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, shorter commutes will reduce fuel consumption, stress, and pollutionâ€”a win for both people and the planet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWork Already in Motion\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLand measurement is already complete for the ROB at Bageshwari Gumti and the Ghughritand flyover. Officials have marked government lands first to avoid delays. Now, theyâ€™re moving forward with private land acquisition.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis time, the administration isnâ€™t waiting for things to fall into placeâ€”theyâ€™re making it happen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t Miss What Happens Next\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom city makeovers to rising tourism hubs, Bihar is evolving faster than ever. And this story is just one part of the bigger picture.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want updates that cut through the noise? Follow www.biharsay.com for verified, in-depth coverage and become part of our 10K+ strong global community. Bihar is risingâ€”stay ahead of the story.\u003c/p\u003e",
