        "title":  "Jur Sital 2025: How Mithila Welcomes the New Year!",
        "summary":  "Jur Sital 2025: A Festival Where Sattu Meets Soul and Water Becomes Worship In a world chasing modernity, Mithila quietly turns the page to a new yearâ€”not with noise, but with nourishment, prayers, and a splash of water on a chi...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eJur Sital 2025: A Festival Where Sattu Meets Soul and Water Becomes Worship\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a world chasing modernity, Mithila quietly turns the page to a new yearâ€”not with noise, but with nourishment, prayers, and a splash of water on a childâ€™s forehead. Welcome to Jur Sital, the traditional Maithil New Year, where age-old customs create memories that last a lifetime.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat Makes Jur Sital So Special?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery year, as Vaishakh begins, Jur Sital arrives like a breeze of nostalgia in the heartland of Mithilanchal, located in North Bihar. Itâ€™s not just another date on the calendarâ€”itâ€™s a celebration of health, harmony, and heritage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFamilies begin their day early. Before sunrise, mothers and grandmothers pour cool water on childrenâ€™s heads, offering silent blessings for good health and a long life. This act is more than ritualâ€”itâ€™s love, passed down through generations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSattu, Aam ki Chutney \u0026 The No-Chulha Rule\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe kitchen too observes the festival in its unique way. No fire burns on the stove. Instead, sattu and raw mango chutneyâ€”prepared a day beforeâ€”are served with devotion. This traditional fare is not just about taste; it symbolizes coolness, simplicity, and prosperity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe belief goes: If you eat sattu on this day, your stomach stays cool and your home stays blessed for the rest of the year.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Two-Day Ritual: From Satuaan to Dhurkhel\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJur Sital unfolds over two culturally rich days. The first day is Satuaan, dedicated to prayers and sattu. On the second day, people celebrate Dhurkhel, where children play with mud and water, reminiscent of a Holi of Earth and Joy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t merely playâ€”itâ€™s about reconnecting with nature, touching the soil, and respecting the elements. In Mithila, even games teach lessons of sustainability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Festival Rooted in Love for Children and Nature\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile the rituals are followed by all, children remain at the heart of Jur Sital. From water blessings to cold meals, everything is designed around their well-being. Itâ€™s a gentle reminder that festivals arenâ€™t only about the divineâ€”theyâ€™re about the future generation, too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJust like Chhath Puja honors the sun, Jur Sital honors water and earth. And in doing so, it blends environmental awareness with spiritual depth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant more such beautiful stories of Biharâ€™s vibrant culture and untold traditions?ðŸŒ Follow www.biharsay.com and become a part of our growing 10K global community thatâ€™s proud to say: We belong to Bihar!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant more such beautiful stories of Biharâ€™s vibrant culture and untold traditions?ðŸŒ Follow www.biharsay.com and become a part of our growing 10K global community thatâ€™s proud to say: We belong to Bihar!\u003c/p\u003e",
