        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Railway Revolution: Amrit Bharat Express Set to Transform Travel!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is about to experience a railway revolution! The Amrit Bharat Express will soon offer a faster, more efficient travel experience for people across the state. This Wednesday, the historic speed trial of the Amrit Bharat Express took place between Saharsa and Jhanjharpur.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpeed Trial and New Rail Link\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Wednesday, the Amrit Bharat Express underwent its crucial speed trial. It ran from Saharsa to Saraigarh and then from Saraigarh to Jhanjharpur. During the trial, experts closely monitored the Kosi Rail Mahasetu using drone surveillance. This ensured a smooth and safe journey for the train.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePM Modi to Launch Amrit Bharat Express\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePrime Minister Narendra Modi will flag off the Amrit Bharat Express in Jhanjharpur on April 24. The train will then begin its regular service. It will travel from Saharsa to Saraigarh Junction, passing through Darbhanga, Ayodhya, and Varanasi, before reaching Anand Vihar in Delhi.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Train Matters for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amrit Bharat Express will significantly reduce travel times across Bihar. It will make travel quicker, more comfortable, and more accessible. By connecting various key regions, this train will boost tourism and local economies. Itâ€™s not just a train; itâ€™s a new era for Biharâ€™s infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe introduction of this service is a part of a bigger plan to improve connectivity across the state. Biharâ€™s railway system is evolving, and this express train is one of the milestones.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGet the Latest Updates on Biharâ€™s Infrastructure\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay updated with the latest news on Biharâ€™s railway developments, infrastructure projects, and more. Visit www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become a part of our 11,000-strong global community!\u003c/p\u003e",
