        "id":  "smart-id-cards-for-farmers-in-bihar-pilot-kisan-registry-project-launched",
        "title":  "Bihar\u0027s 5 Crore Farmers to Get Aadhaar-like IDs",
        "summary":  "5 Crore Farmers, 1 Identity: Bhojpur Joins Centreâ€™s â‚¹2817 Cr Digital Mission with Aadhaar-like ID Cards â€œà¤•à¤¿à¤¸à¤¾à¤¨à¥‹à¤‚ à¤•à¥‹ à¤®à¤¿à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾ à¤…à¤ªà¤¨à¤¾ à¤†à¤§à¤¾à¤° à¤œà¥ˆà¤¸à¤¾ ID â€“ à¤…à¤¬ à¤¯à¥‹à¤œà¤¨à¤¾ à¤...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e5 Crore Farmers, 1 Identity: Bhojpur Joins Centreâ€™s â‚¹2817 Cr Digital Mission with Aadhaar-like ID Cards\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œà¤•à¤¿à¤¸à¤¾à¤¨à¥‹à¤‚ à¤•à¥‹ à¤®à¤¿à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾ à¤…à¤ªà¤¨à¤¾ à¤†à¤§à¤¾à¤° à¤œà¥ˆà¤¸à¤¾ ID â€“ à¤…à¤¬ à¤¯à¥‹à¤œà¤¨à¤¾ à¤•à¤¾ à¤²à¤¾à¤­ à¤¸à¥€à¤§à¥‡ à¤”à¤° à¤¸à¤°à¤²!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndiaâ€™s farmers are stepping into a new era.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo boost income and simplify access to government schemes, the Government of India has launched a â‚¹2817 crore Digital Agriculture Mission. At the heart of this mission is a game-changing initiative: Aadhaar-like ID cards for farmers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy March next year, the government aims to register 5 crore farmers under this program. Interestingly, Bhojpur in Bihar has already emerged as an early leader by participating in the pilot phase.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Farmer ID Cards Could Change Everything\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese new farmer IDs will provide a unique digital identity, functioning much like Aadhaar. With this, farmers can easily access:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMinimum Support Price (MSP) benefits Crop insurance claims Government subsidies Farmer Credit Cards And all future agri-schemes\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMinimum Support Price (MSP) benefits\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCrop insurance claims\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGovernment subsidies\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFarmer Credit Cards\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd all future agri-schemes\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Agriculture Secretary Devesh Chaturvedi, the digital ID will reduce verification delays and improve transparency. Notably, the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmersâ€™ Welfare is executing this initiative with technical support from ICAR.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo far, 19 states have agreed to participate in the rollout. Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh, and now Bhojpur (Bihar) have already started pilot implementations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhojpurâ€™s Ground-Level Push: 18,000+ Farmers Registered\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the ground in Bhojpur, the pilot is making strong progress:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e28 villages across 14 blocks have seen registration camps Farmers provide Aadhaar, a mobile number, and revenue receipts Revenue officers upload land ownership details to a central portal Farmers receive a unique ID linked to their land\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e28 villages across 14 blocks have seen registration camps\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFarmers provide Aadhaar, a mobile number, and revenue receipts\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRevenue officers upload land ownership details to a central portal\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFarmers receive a unique ID linked to their land\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConsequently, this digital â€œland biodataâ€ simplifies scheme eligibility checks. Already, over 18,000 PM-Kisan beneficiaries have been enrolled in the pilot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNext, the process will cover joint landholders and farmers lacking direct land receipts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eList of Bhojpur Blocks Covered\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVillages in these 14 blocks are part of the pilot:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAra: Bhakura, Mahuli Barhara: Babura, Bakhorapur Bihiya: Kateya, Kamariyaw Charpokhari: Semraw, Nagari Garhani: Baligaon, Garhani Jagdishpur: Ayr, Dalippur Koilwar: Beerampur, Khanaganj Piro: Tar, Chaurhijangal Mahal Sahar: Perhap, Guljarpur Sandesh: Bhatauli, Chilaus Shahpur: Bariswan, Isarpura Tarari: Karth, Badkagaon Agiaon: Narayanpur, Agiaon Udwantnagar: Udwantnagar, Piyania\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAra: Bhakura, Mahuli\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBarhara: Babura, Bakhorapur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihiya: Kateya, Kamariyaw\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCharpokhari: Semraw, Nagari\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGarhani: Baligaon, Garhani\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJagdishpur: Ayr, Dalippur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKoilwar: Beerampur, Khanaganj\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePiro: Tar, Chaurhijangal Mahal\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSahar: Perhap, Guljarpur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSandesh: Bhatauli, Chilaus\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShahpur: Bariswan, Isarpura\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTarari: Karth, Badkagaon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAgiaon: Narayanpur, Agiaon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUdwantnagar: Udwantnagar, Piyania\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearly, the effort is widespread and inclusive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDocuments Required for Kisan ID Registration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo join the program, farmers must bring the following:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAadhaar card Linked mobile number Revenue receipt (Jamabandi)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAadhaar card\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLinked mobile number\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRevenue receipt (Jamabandi)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRegistration is simple and fast. In fact, most verification happens on the spot at the camp. This eliminates long waits and reduces paperwork hassles.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDigital Tools for Digital Farmers: AI Chatbots Next\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe mission doesnâ€™t end with ID cards. The government is also developing AI-powered chatbots to guide farmers. These bots will provide:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eScheme-related information in regional languages Personalized assistance Help with filling out online applications\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eScheme-related information in regional languages\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePersonalized assistance\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHelp with filling out online applications\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs a result, farmers will no longer depend on middlemen or agents for scheme access.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat It Means for Farmers Nationwide\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis pilot, though small in scale for now, has national implications. With the government targeting 5 crore farmers by March, India is preparing for a digitally unified agri-network.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s more, the initiative empowers farmers with verified identity, fast-tracked benefits, and real-time assistance. Itâ€™s a strong step toward building an efficient, transparent, and farmer-friendly system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the long run, this shift could redefine rural development and boost farmer income across the board.\u003c/p\u003e",
