        "title":  "Rajgir to host Women\u0027s Kabaddi World Cup 2025",
        "summary":  "à¤œà¤¬ à¤¬à¤¿à¤¹à¤¾à¤° à¤¬à¥‹à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾â€¦ à¤¦à¥à¤¨à¤¿à¤¯à¤¾ à¤¸à¥à¤¨à¥‡à¤—à¥€!Get ready, sports lovers! The vibrant city of Rajgir, Bihar, is about to script history again. From June 1 to 10, the 2025 Womenâ€™s Kabaddi World ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eà¤œà¤¬ à¤¬à¤¿à¤¹à¤¾à¤° à¤¬à¥‹à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾â€¦ à¤¦à¥à¤¨à¤¿à¤¯à¤¾ à¤¸à¥à¤¨à¥‡à¤—à¥€!Get ready, sports lovers! The vibrant city of Rajgir, Bihar, is about to script history again. From June 1 to 10, the 2025 Womenâ€™s Kabaddi World Cup will electrify the State Sports Academy, bringing together 14 powerhouse teams from across four continents!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKabaddiâ€™s Grand Return to Bihar: A Moment of Pride\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter a glorious first hosting in 2012 at the Patliputra Sports Complex, Bihar is once again in the global spotlight. Thanks to the combined efforts of the Amateur Kabaddi Federation of India (AKFI) and the International Kabaddi Federation (IKF), Rajgir will welcome countries like India, Iran, Nepal, Bangladesh, Thailand, Netherlands, and many more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot just fans from Bihar, but millions around the world will tune in to witness one of Indiaâ€™s most ancient yet dynamic sports.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhoâ€™s Coming to Battle for Glory?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe participating nations are:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndia Iran Nepal Bangladesh Thailand Netherlands Poland Hungary Japan Germany Argentina Uganda Kenya\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndia\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIran\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNepal\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBangladesh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThailand\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNetherlands\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoland\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHungary\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJapan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGermany\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArgentina\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUganda\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKenya\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis diverse lineup shows Kabaddiâ€™s booming popularity beyond Asia. Especially with countries like Argentina and Uganda stepping onto the kabaddi mat, the excitement levels are sky-high!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndia: The Team to Beat\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndiaâ€™s Womenâ€™s Kabaddi team is riding high on confidence. After clinching victory against Iran (32-25) in the recent Asian Womenâ€™s Kabaddi Championship in Tehran, they are entering the tournament as defending champions. In the last World Cup final, Team India toppled Iran 25-19, while Thailand and Japan shared the third place.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLed by fierce captain Sonali Vishnu and her deputy Pushpa Rana, Team Indiaâ€™s dominance looks unshakable. However, with new challengers emerging, fans can expect edge-of-the-seat matches!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePreparations in Full Swing for the Big Battle\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt a grand signing ceremony in Patna, AKFIâ€™s Secretary General Ravindran Shankaran and official Jitendra Thakur sealed the eventâ€™s final confirmations. Speaking passionately, Shankaran said:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œIt is a matter of great joy and pride for Bihar to host the Womenâ€™s Kabaddi World Cup in Rajgir. Due to the governmentâ€™s commitment to developing sports, Bihar is gaining the honour of hosting several national and international competitions.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo sharpen their skills, the Indian squad will undergo a rigorous 15-day training camp. This intense preparation will ensure that they are ready to defend their crown when the whistle blows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Rajgir? Why Now?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRajgir, with its lush landscape and rich cultural backdrop, offers a perfect setting for an international kabaddi fiesta. The governmentâ€™s focus on making Bihar a sporting hub is finally paying off. This event not only strengthens Biharâ€™s sporting infrastructure but also places it firmly on the global sports map.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom colorful opening ceremonies to nail-biting matches, Rajgir promises an unforgettable celebration of spirit, strength, and strategy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Donâ€™t miss a beat! For real-time updates, thrilling match previews, and behind-the-scenes scoops on the Womenâ€™s Kabaddi World Cup, follow www.biharsay.com and become a proud part of our 11k+ strong community worldwide!\u003c/p\u003e",
