        "title":  "SepakTakraw Takes Over Bihar â€“ Growth, Success \u0026 Future Opportunities",
        "summary":  "The Phenomenal Rise of SepakTakraw in Bihar Imagine a game that blends football, volleyball, and acrobatics. Thatâ€™s SepakTakraw. Itâ€™s a sport thatâ€™s gaining rapid popularity in Bihar. Following the World Cup held in Patna in...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eThe Phenomenal Rise of SepakTakraw in Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine a game that blends football, volleyball, and acrobatics. Thatâ€™s SepakTakraw. Itâ€™s a sport thatâ€™s gaining rapid popularity in Bihar. Following the World Cup held in Patna in March 2025, SepakTakraw is now one of the stateâ€™s most exciting sports.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Daily Wage Workers to Gold Medalists\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn Patliputra Indoor Stadium, Sahil Kumar, a 16-year-old from Bihar, is training for the Khelo India Youth Games. For Sahil, SepakTakraw is more than a sportâ€”itâ€™s a way out of poverty. With support from the government, he and others are pushing themselves toward greatness.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSahilâ€™s family comes from humble beginnings. Yet, thanks to SepakTakrawâ€™s low-cost equipment and the opportunities available, he is now able to dream of a better future. Unlike cricket, which requires expensive gear, SepakTakraw is accessible for many.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Governmentâ€™s Role in Boosting SepakTakraw\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s SepakTakraw players are making waves nationally. Over 600 active players are now competing. Thanks to the creation of the Bihar State Sports Authority (BSSA) in 2023, SepakTakraw is now a priority sport in the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is making significant investments in facilities. These developments will help players reach their full potential. Additionally, the sportâ€™s inclusion in the Asian Games further strengthens its status.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Medal-Lao Naukri Pao Scheme\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Medal Lao Naukri Pao scheme is changing the game. It offers A-grade government jobs to athletes who win medals at national and international events. In 2024, 71 athletes received jobs under this scheme. Itâ€™s a breakthrough for players like Aarti Kumari and Rashmi Kumari, who now see a brighter future through sports.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNational Success: Bihar Leads the Way\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s teams are excelling at the national level. In the 2024 Junior National Championship, the boysâ€™ team won the national title. The sub-junior girls team secured a bronze medal. This success is setting the stage for future glory.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, players from across Patna, Muzaffarpur, Nalanda, and Saran are signing up in growing numbers. Karunesh Kumar, an international-level player, believes the state is becoming a force to be reckoned with.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Historic Victory at the World Cup\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s biggest triumph came when the menâ€™s SepakTakraw team won Indiaâ€™s first-ever gold medal at the World Cup in March 2025. The victory catapulted Bihar into the global spotlight. Bobby Kumar, from Saran, was one of the key players.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePrime Minister Narendra Modi and Union Sports Minister Mansukh Mandaviya congratulated the team. They praised the players for their exceptional performance. This win marks a new era for SepakTakraw in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSepakTakraw: A Future for Everyone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe sport is growing rapidly in Bihar. More players are joining every day. In fact, 18 players from Bihar are competing in the upcoming Khelo India Youth Games. Players like Aarti, who dreams of representing India, are paving the way for the future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is also improving its sports infrastructure. New academies and programs are being introduced. With these developments, the future of SepakTakraw looks bright in Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin the Movement!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is becoming the hub for SepakTakraw in India. The stateâ€™s athletes are showing the world what they can achieve. Want to stay updated? Follow www.biharsay.com. Join our growing community and get the latest updates on Biharâ€™s sports scene!\u003c/p\u003e",
