        "title":  "Patna to Get 150 New Electric Buses by August",
        "summary":  "150 Electric Buses Coming to Patna: Biharâ€™s Green Revolution Hits the Road by August! Patna, Tayyar Ho Jao! Ab Safar Hoga Harit, Shahar Hoga Smart! Green wheels are about to change Patnaâ€™s traffic storyâ€”one electric bus at a...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e150 Electric Buses Coming to Patna: Biharâ€™s Green Revolution Hits the Road by August!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna, Tayyar Ho Jao! Ab Safar Hoga Harit, Shahar Hoga Smart!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreen wheels are about to change Patnaâ€™s traffic storyâ€”one electric bus at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatnaâ€™s E-Bus Surge: A Clean Commute Revolution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a bold move towards sustainable mobility, Patna is all set to welcome 150 brand-new electric buses by August 2025. These zero-emission buses will soon roll out on 14 major city routes, replacing traditional CNG models and giving the capital a much-needed breath of fresh air.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut thatâ€™s not allâ€”this green upgrade is just one part of a larger electrification wave sweeping across Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters: Clean Energy, Cleaner Air\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna has long grappled with rising pollution and chaotic public transport. These e-buses are a direct response to those challenges. Unlike fossil-fuel-driven buses, electric buses emit zero tailpipe emissions, drastically reducing urban carbon footprints.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, electric buses cost less to run, require less maintenance, and offer smoother rides. That means cleaner air and a better commuting experience for thousands of residents every day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Bigger Plan: 400 Electric Buses Statewide\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis transformation is not just Patnaâ€™s story. The capital city is part of a statewide green transport initiative, under which Bihar will receive 400 electric buses to operate across multiple cities including Muzaffarpur, Gaya, Bhagalpur, and more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe initiative reflects a long-term commitment by the Bihar government to make public transport both eco-friendly and efficient. And for Patna, this is just the beginning.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e14 Key Routes Set to Go Electric\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom bustling Gandhi Maidan to the crowded lanes of Kankarbagh and Danapur, these buses will serve major routes that carry the bulk of the cityâ€™s daily traffic. The strategic route planning ensures maximum impactâ€”helping reduce congestion, boost convenience, and cut emissions where it matters most.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Road Ahead\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatnaâ€™s shift to electric buses isnâ€™t just a transport update. Itâ€™s a green promise. A promise to lead by example, fight climate change, and build a better future for the next generation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay tuned as the city takes a giant leap toward smart urban mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to stay ahead of such powerful updates from Bihar?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change. With over 11,000 followers, top LinkedIn impressions for Bihar-focused content, and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar.Its flagship podcast and video series, BiharCast, dives deep into untold storiesâ€”spotlighting changemakers, traditions, and rising voices from the heart of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
