        "title":  "Blackout Mock Drill Tomorrow in 6 Cities of Bihar!",
        "summary":  "â€œBlackout Alert: Bihar Cities to Pause for 2 Minutes on May 7 â€“ Hereâ€™s Why You Should Careâ€ Bihar to Hit Pause: Sirens, Silence, and a Blackout Across Key Cities Imagine the city going completely dark.No traffic. No lights...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œBlackout Alert: Bihar Cities to Pause for 2 Minutes on May 7 â€“ Hereâ€™s Why You Should Careâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar to Hit Pause: Sirens, Silence, and a Blackout Across Key Cities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine the city going completely dark.No traffic. No lights. Just a chilling siren that pierces through the silence. On May 7th, this will be reality across Patna, Begusarai, Barh, Barauni, and Purnia, as Bihar prepares for one of its largest-ever mock drills.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnder the Ministry of Home Affairsâ€™ directive following the Pahalgam terror attack, these drills aim to test disaster response systems and public readiness in case of emergencies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Going to Happen on May 7th?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt exactly 6:58 PM, loud sirens will echo across 80 different locations in Patna alone. Within seconds, electricity will be cut off, throwing the city into complete darkness for 10 minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSoon after, police vehicles and fire brigades will drive around with sirens blaring at key junctions like the Secretariat, Patna University, NIT, and the Reserve Bank, where fixed siren systems are already installed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸš« Traffic will be halted.ðŸ”Œ Power will be disconnected.ðŸš¨ Siren will signal the start and end.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEven though this sounds intense, officials urge people not to panic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Drill Matters More Than Ever\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to District Magistrate Dr. Chandrashekhar Singh and SSP Avkash Kumar, this exercise isnâ€™t just protocol â€” itâ€™s preparedness for potential terror threats.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith rising geopolitical tension between India and Pakistan, this mock drill acts as a simulation of a real-world emergency scenario. It will allow authorities to monitor public behavior, response time, and system coordination â€” crucial elements in saving lives during real attacks or disasters.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut the drill wonâ€™t just test the government.It will test us all.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWill people cooperate? Will citizens help each other? Will panic override patience?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow You Can Help â€“ Or Hurt â€“ the Drill\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe success of this mock drill depends not on officials, but on the citizens of Bihar. Hereâ€™s what YOU should do:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâœ… Stay indoors between 6:50 PM and 7:10 PMâœ… Donâ€™t call emergency numbers unless itâ€™s a real emergencyâœ… Spread awareness in your housing society or localityâœ… Avoid social media panic or misinformationâœ… Cooperate with police and traffic control units\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not a curfew. Itâ€™s a commitment to collective safety.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Bihar is in the National Spotlight\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe drill across Bihar is part of a nationwide preparedness strategy. Yet Biharâ€™s participation stands out â€” especially Patna, with its wide-scale involvement and logistical readiness.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd itâ€™s not just about today.This is about building a culture of responsiveness for tomorrow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say â€” the digital voice of Bihar â€” will continue bringing such unfiltered, real, and relevant stories from the heart of our state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“£ Donâ€™t miss another important update from Bihar.Follow www.biharsay.com now and become part of our 11k+ global community that celebrates Biharâ€™s culture, courage, and change â€” one story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change. With over 11,000 followers, top LinkedIn impressions for Bihar-focused content, and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar. Its flagship podcast and video series, BiharCast, dives deep into untold stories, spotlighting changemakers, traditions, and rising voices from the heart of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
