        "id":  "construction-agency-to-work-for-free-at-sitamarhi-janaki-temple",
        "title":  "Construction agency to work for free at Sitamarhi Janaki Temple",
        "summary":  "After Ayodhya, Now Sitamarhi! Janaki Temple to Be Built for Free â€” A Historic Gift to Bihar A Temple Built with Devotion, Not Charges In an announcement that left the crowd in awe, Deputy Chief Minister Vijay Kumar Sinha declare...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eAfter Ayodhya, Now Sitamarhi! Janaki Temple to Be Built for Free â€” A Historic Gift to Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Temple Built with Devotion, Not Charges\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn an announcement that left the crowd in awe, Deputy Chief Minister Vijay Kumar Sinha declared something incredible. The agency that built Ayodhyaâ€™s Ram Mandir will now construct the Janaki Temple in Sitamarhiâ€™s Punaura village â€” completely free of charge.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo bills. No contracts. Only devotion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe revealed this during the Janaki Navami Mahotsavâ€™s grand opening night. The air buzzed with chants, cheers, and cultural pride.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlans to Expand: 50 Acres for Punaura Dham\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo support this spiritual revival, the state government will soon acquire 50 acres around Punaura village. This land will be developed into a vast spiritual corridor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis move isnâ€™t just about religion. Itâ€™s a part of Biharâ€™s plan to become a major religious tourism hub in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd yes, the funds have already been allocated. The commitment is real.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Mahotsav Like Never Before\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis yearâ€™s Janaki Navami Mahotsav saw record-breaking pilgrim numbers in Sitamarhi and even in Janakpur Dham, Nepal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom spiritual chants to star-studded performances, the atmosphere stayed magical.The evening featured stunning acts by:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSona Mahapatra (Singer) Maithili Thakur (Folk Star) Soma Mandal (Bharatanatyam Icon)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSona Mahapatra (Singer)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaithili Thakur (Folk Star)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSoma Mandal (Bharatanatyam Icon)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir energy turned the event into an unforgettable cultural memory.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSitamarhiâ€™s Sacred Makeover: Biharâ€™s Bold Spiritual Statement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat Ayodhya did for Ram, Sitamarhi is now doing for Sita. With no construction fee, national talent, and dedicated land, the Janaki Temple project will reshape Biharâ€™s spiritual identity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd most importantly, it proves something deeperâ€”faith still drives change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t miss Biharâ€™s transformation story!Follow www.biharsay.com for real stories, real heroes, and real pride.ðŸ’¬ Be part of our growing #BiharSay family of 11K+ readers worldwide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change. With over 11,000 followers, top LinkedIn impressions for Bihar-focused content, and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIts flagship podcast and video series, BiharCast, dives deep into untold stories, spotlighting changemakers, traditions, and rising voices from the heart of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
