        "title":  "Biharâ€™s 6 Karate Stars to Represent India at Nepal\u0027s Mount Everest International Championship",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Karate Powerhouse! | 6 Young Warriors to Represent India in Nepalâ€™s Mount Everest International Karate Championship ðŸ‡®ðŸ‡³ Biharâ€™s Karate Champs Set to Make History in Nepal! Once again, Biharâ€™s sons and daughter...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Karate Powerhouse! | 6 Young Warriors to Represent India in Nepalâ€™s Mount Everest International Karate Championship ðŸ‡®ðŸ‡³\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Karate Champs Set to Make History in Nepal!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce again, Biharâ€™s sons and daughters are ready to make the nation proud! Six dynamic karatekas from Bihar have been selected to represent Team India at the prestigious Mount Everest International Karate Championship in Kathmandu, Nepal, happening from May 16 to 20, 2025. Their fists carry not just strength, but the hope and pride of an entire state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese selections mark a thrilling chapter in Bihar Sports News and speak volumes about the talent emerging from the heartland of India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMeet the Real Champions of Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom local dojos to international arenas, these young stars have shown unstoppable grit. The selected athletes include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNitin, Paridhi, and Ankit from Muzaffarpur Vansh from Sheohar Akash Raja and Saurav from Vaishali\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNitin, Paridhi, and Ankit from Muzaffarpur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVansh from Sheohar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAkash Raja and Saurav from Vaishali\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith their unwavering discipline and rigorous training, these six have earned their place on the Indian squad through a high-stakes national trial hosted by the India Zen-Do-Shin Karate Federation. Out of 60 participants, only these six stood out â€” a testament to Biharâ€™s rising dominance in martial arts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow the Selection Unfolded\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe road to Nepal wasnâ€™t easy. Athletes had to push their limits in a national-level trial organized by the India Zen-Do-Shin Karate Federation, where performance, agility, and skill were closely evaluated. From that intense trial, Biharâ€™s six heroes emerged victorious.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir selection isnâ€™t just a personal win â€” itâ€™s a victory for every aspiring athlete across Bihar. It shows whatâ€™s possible with dedication, even without big city infrastructure or hype.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLeading the Squad â€“ A Mentor From Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdding to the pride, Shihan E. Rahul Srivastav, a well-respected figure in Indian Karate, will lead the national team as head coach. His guidance will surely boost the teamâ€™s performance and morale in Nepal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHis presence is a reminder that Bihar not only produces players â€” it also produces leaders, mentors, and icons in the sports world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Championship Matters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Mount Everest International Karate Championship is no ordinary event. It draws elite competitors from across the globe, providing an international platform for young talent. This will be the 11th edition of the event, making it a legacy tournament for martial artists worldwide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Biharâ€™s athletes, this is more than a tournament â€” itâ€™s a global stage. Theyâ€™re not just representing Bihar or India â€” theyâ€™re telling the world that talent knows no boundaries.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Sporting Spirit is Rising\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn recent years, Biharâ€™s youth have stepped into the spotlight in cricket, football, athletics â€” and now, karate. With minimal resources but maximum passion, theyâ€™re breaking barriers and shattering stereotypes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlatforms like Bihar Say have consistently amplified such achievements, celebrating every unsung hero and changemaker.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ”¥ Want more such inspiring sports updates?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin our growing global community of 11K+ followers.ðŸ‘‰ Visit www.biharsay.com for regular stories that go beyond headlines and bring you closer to Biharâ€™s soul â€” from grassroots sports to cultural legends.Be a part of Biharâ€™s most vibrant storytelling movement â€” Bihar Say, the digital voice of Bihar!\u003c/p\u003e",
