        "title":  "Bihar Tops PMFME Scheme Implementation in 2025",
        "summary":  "â€œFrom Fields to Factories: How Biharâ€™s Micro Food Units Are Leading Indiaâ€™s Entrepreneurial Chargeâ€ â€œBihar ne phir sabit kiya hai â€“ sapne chhote ho sakte hain, lekin iraade bade hote hain!â€In a powerful win for grass...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œFrom Fields to Factories: How Biharâ€™s Micro Food Units Are Leading Indiaâ€™s Entrepreneurial Chargeâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œBihar ne phir sabit kiya hai â€“ sapne chhote ho sakte hain, lekin iraade bade hote hain!â€In a powerful win for grassroots entrepreneurship, Bihar has clinched the No. 1 spot nationwide in the implementation of the PMFME (Pradhan Mantri Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises) scheme for the year 2024â€“25. The announcement was made by Industries Minister Nitish Mishra, who credited this success to Biharâ€™s consistent push for self-reliance, local empowerment, and industry-focused growth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Big Leap: 10,000+ Entrepreneurs Empowered\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnder the PMFME scheme, Bihar approved loans for 10,296 applicants and successfully disbursed funds to 6,589 micro food processing unitsâ€”achieving a remarkable 63% implementation rate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut this isnâ€™t just a number game. Each loan represents a local dream turned reality, a family business revived, or a rural youth choosing entrepreneurship over migration. Minister Nitish Mishra rightfully called it a step toward promoting small-scale industries and employment at the heart of the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow PMFME Works: A Game-Changer for Local Units\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnlike traditional subsidy schemes, PMFME is sharply focused on decentralized and micro-level food processing. Hereâ€™s what makes it different:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndividual Units get a credit-linked subsidy of 35% (up to â‚¹10 lakh), provided they contribute at least 10% of the project cost. The scheme also covers working capital and infrastructure, allowing even small setups to compete and scale.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndividual Units get a credit-linked subsidy of 35% (up to â‚¹10 lakh), provided they contribute at least 10% of the project cost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe scheme also covers working capital and infrastructure, allowing even small setups to compete and scale.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut thatâ€™s not all.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond Individuals: FPOs, SHGs \u0026 Co-ops Benefit Too\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFarmer Producer Organisations (FPOs), Self-Help Groups (SHGs), and Cooperatives arenâ€™t left behind. They too receive:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e35% subsidy on project costs (up to â‚¹3 crore) for establishing Common Facility Centres. The goal? To provide shared spaces, tools, and processing supportâ€”lowering the cost burden and increasing productivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e35% subsidy on project costs (up to â‚¹3 crore) for establishing Common Facility Centres.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe goal? To provide shared spaces, tools, and processing supportâ€”lowering the cost burden and increasing productivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis collaborative model is already transforming community-driven enterprises, especially in agrarian districts of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWho Can Apply? This Scheme Is for Everyone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne of the strongest aspects of the PMFME scheme is its inclusivity. Whether youâ€™re:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn individual entrepreneur A private limited company A proprietorship or partnership firm An NGO A cooperative Or a women-led SHGâ€¦\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn individual entrepreneur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA private limited company\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA proprietorship or partnership firm\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn NGO\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA cooperative\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOr a women-led SHGâ€¦\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThereâ€™s a path for you. With this, Bihar is bridging the gap between traditional practices and modern market needs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Bihar Topped: Leadership, Vision \u0026 Local Spirit\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo what helped Bihar beat larger states? A combination of policy commitment, community mobilization, and on-ground implementation. Local governance and awareness programs played a vital role in reaching remote regions and marginalized entrepreneurs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMinister Nitish Mishraâ€™s proactive approach also helped accelerate loan approvals, ensure transparency, and minimize delays.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Is Not Just Growing, Itâ€™s Leading\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe success of PMFME in Bihar reflects a deeper shift â€” a new era of entrepreneurship led by rural changemakers. It proves that with the right support, even small ventures can become engines of big change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s not just a policy win â€” itâ€™s a victory for the people of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s not just a policy win â€” itâ€™s a victory for the people of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ For more stories like this â€“ real stories of change, hope, and Biharâ€™s rise â€“ follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our growing global community of 11,000+ changemakers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s narrative through inspiring tales of culture, business, and transformation. Stay updated, stay inspired.\u003c/p\u003e",
