        "id":  "apple-cultivation-in-bihar-farmer-grows-apples-at-44c-and-breaks-climate-myths",
        "title":  "Apple Cultivation in Bihar: Farmer Grows Apples at 44Â°C and Breaks Climate Myths",
        "summary":  "Apple Grows in Bihar Heat! Farmer Lalit Kumar Turns 44Â°C into a Sweet Success Story! An Apple Grows in Bihar: How One Farmer Made the Impossible, Possible â€œThey said apples need snow. I proved they can bloom in Bihar.â€Thatâ€™...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eApple Grows in Bihar Heat! Farmer Lalit Kumar Turns 44Â°C into a Sweet Success Story!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn Apple Grows in Bihar: How One Farmer Made the Impossible, Possible\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œThey said apples need snow. I proved they can bloom in Bihar.â€Thatâ€™s not a movie dialogueâ€”itâ€™s the real voice of change from Lalit Kumar, a farmer from Masaurhi, Patna. In a state better known for rice, wheat, and lentils, Lalit is defying climate norms and rewriting Biharâ€™s farming narrative. And yes, weâ€™re talking about real, juicy applesâ€”ripening in a place where summer temperatures soar to 44Â°C!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Man Behind Biharâ€™s First Apple Breakthrough\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLalit Kumar isnâ€™t new to farming. For over two decades, he has nurtured plants across 12 bighas of land. But recently, he planted something revolutionaryâ€”apple trees. Not in Himachal or Kashmir, but right here in Bihar. With just 10 plants of the â€˜Hariman 99â€™ and â€˜Goldenâ€™ varieties, Lalit has managed to get sweet, market-ready fruit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd no, this isnâ€™t a one-off experiment. Itâ€™s a taste of the future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œPeople laughed when I said Iâ€™d grow apples. Now theyâ€™re tasting them,â€ says Lalit with pride.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œPeople laughed when I said Iâ€™d grow apples. Now theyâ€™re tasting them,â€ says Lalit with pride.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Himachal to Patna: The Journey of the Sapling\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe story began when Lalit brought apple saplings from Hariman, Himachal Pradesh. These were not ordinary varieties. â€˜Hariman 99â€™ and â€˜Goldenâ€™ are specially developed for warm climates. Whatâ€™s more surprising? These apples donâ€™t just surviveâ€”they thrive at 44Â°C, a temperature that would make regular varieties wilt.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith his deep-rooted love for horticulture, Lalit gave these plants everything they neededâ€”soil care, consistent watering, and patience. Today, the same red fruits that define Shimla are now adding a new colour to Biharâ€™s soil.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Climate + Right Varieties = Sweet Apples\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile many still think apple farming needs cold weather, Lalit believes itâ€™s time to break that myth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWeâ€™ve always believed apples canâ€™t grow here. But the truth is, right variety + right care = right results,â€ he explains.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWeâ€™ve always believed apples canâ€™t grow here. But the truth is, right variety + right care = right results,â€ he explains.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese apples are not just growingâ€”theyâ€™re bearing fruit with remarkable taste and quality. With rising demand for local produce, Lalit sees no reason why Bihar apples canâ€™t sell at â‚¹200/kg just like their Himachal cousins.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMarket-Ready and Future-Proof\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s exciting? Lalitâ€™s apples are already market-ready. No transportation cost from the hills. No long storage. Just fresh, sweet apples grown right hereâ€”ready to be sold locally or across India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just about farming. Itâ€™s a quiet agricultural revolution in a state thatâ€™s ready to innovate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters for Biharâ€™s Farming Future\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLalit Kumarâ€™s success shows what happens when tradition meets innovation. In a time when farmers across India are struggling, Bihar has a new hope growingâ€”literallyâ€”in its soil. This is more than a story. Itâ€™s a signal to every farmer whoâ€™s ever been told â€œyou canâ€™t.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause now, even apples bow down to Biharâ€™s resilience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want more real stories from the heart of Bihar?Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become a part of our 11K+ global community. Bihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through real stories of grit, culture, and grassroots change\u003c/p\u003e",
