        "title":  "Bihar Launches 6 New Government Bus Routes â€“ Full List \u0026 Impact",
        "summary":  "New Bus Routes Unlocked! Bihar Commutes Just Got a Major Upgrade â€“ Hereâ€™s What You Need to Know Biharâ€™s Roadways Revolution: 6 Brand-New Bus Routes Launched, Commute Made Easier Than Ever Imagine starting your day knowing a ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eNew Bus Routes Unlocked! Bihar Commutes Just Got a Major Upgrade â€“ Hereâ€™s What You Need to Know\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Roadways Revolution: 6 Brand-New Bus Routes Launched, Commute Made Easier Than Ever\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine starting your day knowing a reliable government bus will now take you from Bairgania to Patna without the chaos of unregulated travel. This isnâ€™t a dreamâ€”itâ€™s Biharâ€™s newest reality.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar State Road Transport Corporation (BSRTC) has officially flagged off six brand-new government-run bus routes, aimed at connecting remote towns to the state capital and beyond. This initiative, backed by the arrival of 30 new buses at the Muzaffarpur depot, is more than just a transport upgradeâ€”itâ€™s a step toward bridging mobility gaps across Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHereâ€™s Whatâ€™s Changing â€“ The New Routes in Focus\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStarting this weekend, BSRTC will operate buses on the following freshly approved routes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBairgania â€“ Patna Adapur â€“ Patna Bettiah â€“ Siwan Gahiri â€“ Patna Sikta â€“ Patna Narkatiaganj â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBairgania â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdapur â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBettiah â€“ Siwan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGahiri â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSikta â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNarkatiaganj â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd thatâ€™s just the beginning. According to Regional Manager Ashish Kumar, who is overseeing the transition, these additions are part of a wider plan. Some of these routes had no BSRTC service before. Now, thatâ€™s changingâ€”permanently.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot Just New Routes â€“ More Buses on Existing Lines Too\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the six new routes, the government will increase the number of buses on several busy corridors. This includes popular routes like:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAreraj â€“ Patna Shivhar â€“ Patna Muzaffarpur â€“ Patna Sitamarhi â€“ Patna Maharajganj â€“ Patna Punauli â€“ Patna Aurai â€“ Patna Kataiya â€“ Patna Daroli â€“ Patna Bettiah â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAreraj â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShivhar â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSitamarhi â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaharajganj â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePunauli â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAurai â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKataiya â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDaroli â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBettiah â€“ Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, whether youâ€™re a daily commuter, student, or trader, youâ€™ll now have more optionsâ€”and more reliabilityâ€”than ever before.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters â€“ A Human-Centric View\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis update isnâ€™t just about buses and permitsâ€”itâ€™s about people. For thousands of citizens, a smoother journey means more punctual jobs, affordable travel, timely medical appointments, and easier education access.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTake Seema Devi, a homemaker from Areraj. She says, â€œEarlier, I had to wait hours for a private bus to Patna. With the new government service, it feels like weâ€™re finally visible on the transport map.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuch stories echo across Bihar. By expanding reach and capacity, BSRTC is making public transport feel personalâ€”and powerful.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBehind the Scenes: How It All Came Together\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter acquiring 30 new buses, the Muzaffarpur depot was selected as the central hub for launching these services. The Regional Transport Authority has already granted permits, and late Friday night, all buses were successfully transferred from Patna to Muzaffarpur.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOperations may begin as early as Saturday, according to officials. If all goes smoothly, this could be the start of a new era for Biharâ€™s public transportation system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinal Word? Noâ€”Just Your Next Step\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just a transport update. Itâ€™s a signal. Bihar is movingâ€”faster, smarter, and stronger.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸš¨ Want to stay ahead with Biharâ€™s most impactful news?ðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and join our growing family of 11,000+ global followers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical storytelling platform, reshaping the narrative of the state. From grassroots change to business insights, our stories travel from Patna to the world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecome a part of the change.Become a part of #BiharSay.\u003c/p\u003e",
