        "title":  "Bihar Metro Update 2025: Patna Launches on August 15, 4 More Cities by 2029",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Big Leap: Patna Metro from August 15 \u0026 4 More Cities on Track by 2029! Metro Magic Begins in Bihar: 5 Cities Gear Up for a Modern Transport Revolution! Imagine boarding a sleek metro train in Patna on Independence Day â€...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Big Leap: Patna Metro from August 15 \u0026 4 More Cities on Track by 2029!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMetro Magic Begins in Bihar: 5 Cities Gear Up for a Modern Transport Revolution!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine boarding a sleek metro train in Patna on Independence Day â€” no more chaotic roads or endless traffic jams. This is not just a dream. Itâ€™s Bihar stepping into the future with bold urban mobility plans. With Patna leading the charge, five major cities â€” Patna, Gaya, Muzaffarpur, Darbhanga, and Bhagalpur â€” are all set to welcome metro services as part of an ambitious infrastructure transformation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis visionary project isnâ€™t just about metros; itâ€™s about momentum, modernity, and making Bihar future-ready.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‡®ðŸ‡³ Independence Day Ride: Patna Metro to Roll Out on August 15, 2025\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe countdown has already begun. Patna Metro is slated for launch on August 15, 2025, marking a milestone for Biharâ€™s capital city. The construction work is progressing at full speed. Patnaâ€™s residents can soon expect seamless commutes, quicker travel, and cleaner transport â€” all within city limits.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is Biharâ€™s biggest urban mobility upgrade in decades, reflecting Chief Minister Nitish Kumarâ€™s long-term development vision for the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNext in Line: Gaya, Bhagalpur, Muzaffarpur \u0026 Darbhanga\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is not stopping at Patna. Metro projects in four other cities are in the pipeline:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe longest proposed metro route â€” 36 kilometers. Divided into two corridors with 28 metro stations planned.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe longest proposed metro route â€” 36 kilometers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDivided into two corridors with 28 metro stations planned.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhagalpur:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo be developed in two phases. Phase 1: 12 km stretch from Saidpur to Champanagar (12 stations). Phase 2: Extension from Bhagalpur Station to Champanagar and Vastu Vihar (10 more stations).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo be developed in two phases.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePhase 1: 12 km stretch from Saidpur to Champanagar (12 stations).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePhase 2: Extension from Bhagalpur Station to Champanagar and Vastu Vihar (10 more stations).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCorridor 1: 13.85 km from Harpur Bakhri to Ramdayalu (13 stations). Corridor 2: 7.4 km from SKMCH to Muzaffarpur Junction (7 stations).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCorridor 1: 13.85 km from Harpur Bakhri to Ramdayalu (13 stations).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCorridor 2: 7.4 km from SKMCH to Muzaffarpur Junction (7 stations).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDarbhanga:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDetailed Project Report (DPR) in progress. Final blueprint expected to be unveiled soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDetailed Project Report (DPR) in progress.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinal blueprint expected to be unveiled soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach cityâ€™s DPR is being handled by RITES (Rail India Technical and Economic Service), ensuring the planning meets global transit standards.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFunding the Future: A Global Investment in Biharâ€™s Growth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe financial model is robust and inclusive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCentre \u0026 Bihar Government: Will each contribute 20% of the cost. International Lending Agencies: The remaining 60% will be financed by institutions like the Asian Development Bank and World Bank.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCentre \u0026 Bihar Government: Will each contribute 20% of the cost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInternational Lending Agencies: The remaining 60% will be financed by institutions like the Asian Development Bank and World Bank.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis mixed-funding strategy not only ensures financial stability but also opens Bihar to global infrastructure partnerships.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Metro Mission Matters to Every Bihari\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just about trains. Itâ€™s about:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBetter job opportunities Cleaner air and fewer emissions Improved urban connectivity A new image for Bihar on the national development map\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBetter job opportunities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCleaner air and fewer emissions\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImproved urban connectivity\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA new image for Bihar on the national development map\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is not waiting for change â€” itâ€™s creating it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLetâ€™s Track the Future Together\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar Metro is more than a project. Itâ€™s a movement. A movement toward smart cities, efficient public transport, and a more progressive Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Donâ€™t just watch it unfold â€” be part of it. Follow www.biharsay.com for real-time updates, powerful stories, and local insights that truly matter.ðŸŒ Join our global community of 11,000+ changemakers.ðŸ“¢ #BiharSay is Biharâ€™s digital voice â€” bold, apolitical, and future-facing.\u003c/p\u003e",
