        "summary":  "Patna Shines Bright: Khelo India Youth Games 2025 Conclude with Grand Ceremony Yesterday! â€œKal Patna Mein Sirf Khel Nahi, Itihaas Likha Gaya!â€Yesterday, Patna witnessed a moment that will be remembered for years. The 15th Khel...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna Shines Bright: Khelo India Youth Games 2025 Conclude with Grand Ceremony Yesterday!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œKal Patna Mein Sirf Khel Nahi, Itihaas Likha Gaya!â€Yesterday, Patna witnessed a moment that will be remembered for years. The 15th Khelo India Youth Games 2025 came to a spectacular end at the Pataliputra Sports Complex, Kankarbagh, lighting up the city with joy, pride, and pure athletic spirit. From May 4th to May 15th, Bihar hosted this mega youth sporting event with unmatched energy and elegance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatnaâ€™s Power-Packed Farewell to Indiaâ€™s Youth Athletes\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt exactly 6:30 PM yesterday, the stadium erupted in cheers as the closing ceremony began. The electrifying performances, fireworks, and proud moments gave a fitting goodbye to Indiaâ€™s young athletes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDignitaries including Union Minister of State for Youth Affairs and Sports Raksha Nikhil Khadse and Biharâ€™s Deputy CM Samrat Choudhary graced the stage, applauding the talents who lit up this edition of the Games.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt wasnâ€™t just a closing eventâ€”it was Biharâ€™s declaration that itâ€™s ready to lead Indiaâ€™s sporting future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMedal Tally Recap: Maharashtra Dominates, Haryana Pushes Hard\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaharashtra clinched the overall title, finishing with an impressive 149 medalsâ€”including 56 gold and 45 silver. Their consistent performance across sports like athletics, wrestling, and swimming showed their sporting depth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHaryana, ever a strong contender, gave a tough fight and secured 107 medals, with 35 gold and 26 silverâ€”earning second place overall.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRajasthan bagged third place, ending their campaign with 55 medals, including 22 goldsâ€”shining in sports like fencing and shooting.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinal Day Thrillers: Basketball, Wrestling, Fencing\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYesterdayâ€™s final matchups were intense.In boysâ€™ basketball, Tamil Nadu stormed past Delhi to grab bronze.Meanwhile, Punjabâ€™s girls stunned Maharashtra and added a bronze to their tally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the girlsâ€™ basketball final, Karnataka defeated Haryana and took home the gold, showing brilliance in teamwork and strategy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimultaneously, wrestling and fencing medal matches played out in Patna and Rajgir, keeping spectators on edge till the very last moment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸŽ¯ The Games might be over, but their impact will echo across Bihar and beyond. From hosting elite events to nurturing grassroots talent, Bihar is no longer on the sidelinesâ€”itâ€™s taking centre stage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want to keep witnessing Biharâ€™s rise?Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and join our 11K+ global community thatâ€™s reshaping how the world sees Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is your go-to platform for powerful stories on culture, changemakers, entrepreneurship, and youth power. Our flagship series, BiharCast, is changing conversations, one story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
