        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eJo Patna ke nets mein dikhta hai, wo India ke field tak ja sakta hai!â€ â€” Ghavri \u0026 Ankola Discover Biharâ€™s Raw Bowling Power\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSomething extraordinary happened at Moin-ul-Haq Stadium this Friday. More than 400 young bowlers turned up with one dreamâ€”to make it big. Under the sharp eyes of former Indian cricketers Karsan Ghavri and Salil Ankola, Bihar witnessed a glimpse of its cricketing future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e76 Talents Chosen, But The Real Game Starts Now\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOut of over 400 aspirants, 76 bowlers earned their spot on Day 1 of the second phase of the â€œSearch for Bowlersâ€ trials, hosted by the Bihar Cricket Association (BCA). The numbers included 65 boys and 11 girls, each showcasing their unique style, strength, and spin.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile most trials usually go unnoticed, this one stood out. The scale, the energy, and above all, the level of raw talentâ€”everything felt like a shift in Biharâ€™s cricket narrative.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGhavri Gets Real: â€œTalent Is Not Enoughâ€”Match Performance Mattersâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCricket legend Karsan Ghavri, who played 39 Tests for India, observed closely and offered honest insights.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œItâ€™s not just 20 kids with potential. Many can go far if they work on discipline, play matches, and stay consistent,â€ he said with conviction.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œItâ€™s not just 20 kids with potential. Many can go far if they work on discipline, play matches, and stay consistent,â€ he said with conviction.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe reminded everyone that net practice doesnâ€™t make a match-winner. Pressure situations define a real player. According to him, BCAâ€™s effort could become the foundation for Biharâ€™s bowling dominance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, he felt that trials like this reduce dependency on outside talent. â€œIf you build your own talent pipeline, you donâ€™t need to look elsewhere,â€ he added.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnkolaâ€™s Flashback: â€œWe Had Nothingâ€”These Kids Have Everythingâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFormer fast bowler Salil Ankola brought both nostalgia and wisdom. He recalled how hard it was back in the 80s.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWe didnâ€™t know what professional training meant. We chopped wood and figured things out the hard way,â€ he laughed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWe didnâ€™t know what professional training meant. We chopped wood and figured things out the hard way,â€ he laughed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, he quickly turned serious. â€œThese bowlers now have coaches, infrastructure, and access. But thatâ€™s only useful when matched with hustle,â€ he stressed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe urged the youngsters to learn from every chance, show up with intent, and stay readyâ€”because opportunity never knocks twice.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinal Trial Awaits: The Race Isnâ€™t Over Yet\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe final trial round will take place on Saturday. Earlier, it was postponed for safety reasons after the India-Pakistan conflict following the Pahalgam terror attack. The decision came to protect players, staff, and everyone involved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, as conditions improve, the selectors are all set to see who rises under pressure. With spots still open, expectations are sky-high.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis Is More Than a Trial. Itâ€™s Biharâ€™s Moment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat we saw in Patna wasnâ€™t just bowlingâ€”it was belief. It was Biharâ€™s sons and daughters declaring they belong on the big stage. With the right push, they can wear the blue jersey someday.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd if you want to witness this riseâ€”not just in cricket but across culture, business, and grassroots transformationâ€¦\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com for powerful, apolitical stories that change how the world sees Bihar.Join our 11K+ global community of thinkers, dreamers, and changemakers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading storytelling platform, known for its flagship podcast BiharCast, and top-performing Bihar-focused content across LinkedIn, DailyHunt, and more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:BCA Search for Bowlers Bihar Cricket Talent Bihar Cricket Trials bihar say Bihar sports news Karsan Ghavri Patna Moin-ul-Haq Stadium Patna Salil Ankola Bihar\u003c/p\u003e",
