        "title":  "Biharâ€™s Madhepura Engine Factory to Export 4500 HP Locomotives to Africa",
        "summary":  "à¤—à¤°à¥à¤µ à¤¸à¥‡ à¤•à¤¹à¥‹ â€“ à¤®à¤¢à¤¼à¥Œà¤°à¤¾ à¤šà¤²à¤¾à¤à¤—à¤¾ à¤…à¤«à¥à¤°à¥€à¤•à¤¾ à¤•à¥€ à¤°à¤«à¥à¤¤à¤¾à¤°! A Revolution on Railsâ€”Born in Bihar, Bound for Africa What if we told you that an engine crafted in the hea...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eà¤—à¤°à¥à¤µ à¤¸à¥‡ à¤•à¤¹à¥‹ â€“ à¤®à¤¢à¤¼à¥Œà¤°à¤¾ à¤šà¤²à¤¾à¤à¤—à¤¾ à¤…à¤«à¥à¤°à¥€à¤•à¤¾ à¤•à¥€ à¤°à¤«à¥à¤¤à¤¾à¤°!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Revolution on Railsâ€”Born in Bihar, Bound for Africa\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat if we told you that an engine crafted in the heart of Bihar will soon roar through the landscapes of Africa? Thatâ€™s not a dreamâ€”itâ€™s happening right now in Madhura, Saran.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe WLPL Madhura Locomotive Plant, a collaborative venture between Wabtec Corporation (USA) and the Indian Railways, is scripting history. This advanced locomotive factory is all set to export 4500 HP diesel engines to the African nation of Guinea. The first batch will roll out by end of June 2025, powering Guineaâ€™s Simandou Project, a major mining and rail development effort.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is more than just a trade dealâ€”itâ€™s Bihar stepping onto the global manufacturing stage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWLPL Madhura: From Silent Fields to Global Headlines\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocated on 270 acres of land with a 70-acre production facility, this factory was launched on 17th September 2018. In less than seven years, it has transformed into Indiaâ€™s most advanced diesel locomotive manufacturing plant.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith over 600 skilled engineers and technicians, it has already delivered 700 engines to Indian Railways, and the momentum is only growing. These engines are known not just for their power, but for their eco-friendly performance, meeting international emission standards.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut this Africa-bound shipment changes everythingâ€”it signals Make in Bihar going truly Global.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGuinea Orders 100 Engines from Bihar: What It Means\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Government of Guinea has placed an order for 100 locomotives. According to Biharâ€™s Industry Minister Nitish Mishra, this is a major leap forward for India-Africa cooperation. The engines will be used to transport iron ore across Guineaâ€™s rugged terrain.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe first batch will be dispatched by June end, but before that, a grand naming ceremony is scheduled for 26th May at the plant. Itâ€™s a moment loaded with pride, anticipation, and global visibility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecently, Sandeep Selot, MD (South and Southeast Asia) of Wabtec Corporation, met with Minister Mishra to discuss this high-impact project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut Where Is Madhuraâ€™s Name?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDespite this historic achievement, locals in Madhura feel an emotional pinch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEngines built here often carry the names of cities like Gandhidham (Gujarat), Roza (U.P.), or Putti (Andhra Pradesh). The people of Madhura want to see their townâ€™s name etched onto the very engines they build.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal leaders including MLA Jitendra Kumar Rai and several farmer groups have formally requested the Ministry to name the new Guinea-bound engines after Madhura. The naming ceremony on 26th May could finally give them that long-overdue recognition.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause after all, if an engine is made in Madhura, why shouldnâ€™t the world know?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters for Biharâ€™s Future\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis story is not just about enginesâ€”itâ€™s about employment, innovation, and global trust in Biharâ€™s industrial capacity. It highlights how a once-quiet town can become the hub of international trade, thanks to vision, skill, and strategic partnerships.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s also about the image transformation of Biharâ€”from being tagged as â€œbackwardâ€ to being known for engineering excellence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want to hear more such inspiring stories from Bihar?Follow www.biharsay.com and be part of the 11K-strong global community!Bihar Say is not just a media platformâ€”itâ€™s Biharâ€™s digital heartbeat. Through its flagship series BiharCast, it showcases the soul of Biharâ€”from changemakers to culture, from grassroots to global.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t miss out on the next big story. Be a part of Biharâ€™s narrativeâ€”reshaped by stories, not stereotypes.\u003c/p\u003e",
