        "id":  "gaya-a-spiritual-world-heritage-site-is-now-renamed-as-gaya-ji-like-ganga-ji",
        "title":  "Gaya, a spiritual world heritage site is now renamed as GAYA JI like GANGA JI",
        "summary":  "Gaya Ji: Why This Ancient City Is Not Just a Place, But a Portal to the Divine Not Just a Cityâ€”A Sacred Calling: Welcome to Gaya Ji Some lands arenâ€™t just placesâ€”theyâ€™re portals to the divine.Gaya Ji, the ancient soul of B...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eGaya Ji: Why This Ancient City Is Not Just a Place, But a Portal to the Divine\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot Just a Cityâ€”A Sacred Calling: Welcome to Gaya Ji\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome lands arenâ€™t just placesâ€”theyâ€™re portals to the divine.Gaya Ji, the ancient soul of Bihar, is one such land. Recently renamed officially by the Bihar government, this sacred city now carries the reverence it always deserved. And itâ€™s not just about namesâ€”itâ€™s about spiritual truth, inherited faith, and the yearning for moksha.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Vishnupad Mandir to the Mahabodhi Temple, every corner of Gaya Ji whispers stories of gods, pilgrims, and salvation-seekers from centuries past.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVishnupad Mandir: Where Lord Vishnu Left His Mark\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt the heart of Gaya Ji lies the Vishnupad Mandir, where a 13-inch footprint of Lord Vishnu is believed to be enshrined in stone.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilt by Ahilyabai Holkar in 1787, this temple is not only an architectural marvel but a cornerstone of Vaishnav devotion. According to sacred texts, this footprint marks the spot where Vishnu subdued the demon Gayasura, granting salvation to generations that follow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePilgrims from every part of the country come here to perform Pind Daanâ€”rituals that bring peace to their ancestors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePind Daan: Where Memory Meets Moksha\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy do millions visit Gaya Ji during Pitru Paksha?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause here, Lord Rama himself performed Pind Daan for his father, King Dasharatha.This ancient ritualâ€”deeply woven into the Sanatan belief systemâ€”symbolizes the eternal connection between the living and the departed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNowhere else in India does this practice hold such gravity and historical depth. The Falgu River, often dry but spiritually alive, watches over these rituals like a silent witness to centuries of devotion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Shared Pilgrimage: From Sanatan to Buddhism\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJust a few kilometers from Vishnupad lies Mahabodhi Templeâ€”where Gautam Buddha attained enlightenment under the Bodhi Tree.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis UNESCO World Heritage Site connects seekers from India, Nepal, Sri Lanka, Thailand, and beyond. For Buddhists, Gaya Ji is a pilgrimage of truth. For Hindus, itâ€™s a quest for ancestral peace.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn both journeys, the soul finds light.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is what makes Gaya Ji a spiritual crossroad for humanityâ€”where nirvana and moksha meet under the same sacred sky.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom â€˜Gayaâ€™ to â€˜Gaya Jiâ€™: A Name with Meaning\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy the shift from â€˜Gayaâ€™ to â€˜Gaya Jiâ€™?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause places like these deserve honor in every syllable.Just like we say Kashi Vishwanath Ji, Ganga Ji, or Yamuna Ji, itâ€™s time we speak of Gaya Ji with equal reverence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe movement for this change began over 55 years ago. Religious communities, especially the Gayapal and Panda Samaj, led the charge. And now, thanks to the Nitish Kumar government, the name finally mirrors the soul of the city.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just political reformâ€”itâ€™s cultural resurrection.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShakti, Vishnu, and the Feminine Divine\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya Ji is also home to one of the 51 Shaktipeethsâ€”the revered Mangla Gauri Temple.Perched on the Bhsmakoot hill, this temple draws thousands of devotees, especially during Navratri, when faith overflows in the form of songs, lamps, and offerings.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilt in 1350 AD, it is a reminder that Gaya Ji isnâ€™t a placeâ€”itâ€™s a living testament to divine femininity and eternal devotion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya Ji: A Legacy We Must Speak Loudly About\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen we say Gaya Ji, we donâ€™t just invoke a nameâ€”we invoke a legacy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s where myth, memory, and moksha live together.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s a sacred geography where the past isnâ€™t forgottenâ€”itâ€™s performed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo next time you speak of this land, say it the way our ancestors did:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya Jiâ€¦\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“² For more such soul-stirring stories, insights, and updates from the heart of Bihar, visit www.biharsay.com and become part of our growing 11k+ global community.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical storytelling platformâ€”reshaping the stateâ€™s image, one powerful story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:Bihar Tourism Gautam Buddha Gaya Ji Gaya Ji Pitru Paksha Gaya Ji Renaming News Mahabodhi Temple Mangla Gauri Temple Moksha Pind Daan Pitru Paksha Sanatan Dharma Shaktipeeth Spiritual Places in India Vishnupad Mandir\u003c/p\u003e",
