        "id":  "bihar-to-launch-500-gov-buses-to-6-states",
        "title":  "Bihar to Launch 500 Gov. Buses to 6 States",
        "summary":  "6 States, 500 Buses, 1 Bihar: Indiaâ€™s Heartland Rolls Ahead This Festive Season!â€ Biharâ€™s Big Bus Boom: 500 Inter-State Rides Approved Before Puja Season What if your festive journey from Bihar to Delhi, Punjab, or Bengal be...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003e6 States, 500 Buses, 1 Bihar: Indiaâ€™s Heartland Rolls Ahead This Festive Season!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Big Bus Boom: 500 Inter-State Rides Approved Before Puja Season\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat if your festive journey from Bihar to Delhi, Punjab, or Bengal became smoother, faster, and more affordable?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar State Road Transport Corporation (BSRTC) has dropped a massive update. By Durga Puja 2025, over 500 buses will roll out from Bihar to six major states â€” Delhi, Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan, West Bengal, Punjab, and Haryana.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes, you read that right. The long wait for a better inter-state travel network is finally over.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Survey to Sanction: The Journey of This Game-Changing Decision\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTransport officers didnâ€™t rush the decision. Months of route analysis, passenger demand surveys, and inter-departmental coordination went into finalizing this rollout.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe transport secretaries of the six states have already greenlit the plan. Now, final agreements are being drafted to cement these partnerships. Every move has been backed by data and public demand, ensuring long-term viability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere Will the Buses Start? All Eyes on 6 Division Headquarters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuses will operate from six key cities in Bihar:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna Gaya Bhagalpur Purnia Muzaffarpur Darbhanga\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhagalpur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePurnia\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDarbhanga\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese division headquarters will act as ISBT (Inter-State Bus Terminal) hubs. Many of these already run limited inter-state services. For example, Darbhanga to UP, Bhagalpur to Jharkhand, and Purnia to Bengal are existing routes that will now scale up.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePublic-Private Push: The PPP Model Makes it Bigger\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure efficiency and quality, buses will run under both government and PPP (Public-Private Partnership) models.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s more exciting? Operators joining the PPP model will receive a â‚¹20 lakh grant per bus. This support is expected to attract serious players and improve passenger experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, not only will buses be more frequent, but theyâ€™ll also be cleaner, faster, and better maintained.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters: A Shift from Costly Reroutes to Direct Access\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrently, passengers heading from Bihar to other states often travel via indirect train routes. They spend extra time and money reaching state capitals first, then boarding buses to their final destination.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this rollout, theyâ€™ll save both time and money. And more importantly, theyâ€™ll travel in dignity during the festive rush â€” no more overcrowded trains or long waits.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to BSRTC estimates, 3â€“7 lakh passengers travel to these six states annually during festival seasons. This plan is crafted to meet that spike without chaos.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Darbhanga to Delhi â€“ Bihar is on the Move\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just about transport. Itâ€™s about connection, accessibility, and pride. Bihar is no longer a waiting room for developmentâ€”itâ€™s becoming the launchpad.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd while this initiative doesnâ€™t carry celebrity names, itâ€™s backed by the untiring work of public servants and transport planners who listened to people first.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸŒ Want to stay updated on Biharâ€™s transformation stories?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become part of our 11,000+ global community!Join the movement. Celebrate Biharâ€™s progress. Amplify its voice.\u003c/p\u003e",
