        "title":  "Bihar\u0027s GI Products Now on Postage Stamps â€“ Shahi Litchi, Makhana, Magahi Paan Featured",
        "summary":  "Shahi Litchi to Makhana: Biharâ€™s GI Tag Heroes Now Shine on â‚¹5 Postal Stamps â€“ A Proud Moment for Muzaffarpur Biharâ€™s Shahi Litchi Steals the Spotlight on â‚¹5 Postal Stamp If youâ€™re from Bihar or love stories of regiona...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eShahi Litchi to Makhana: Biharâ€™s GI Tag Heroes Now Shine on â‚¹5 Postal Stamps â€“ A Proud Moment for Muzaffarpur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Shahi Litchi Steals the Spotlight on â‚¹5 Postal Stamp\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf youâ€™re from Bihar or love stories of regional pride, hereâ€™s a refreshing update you should not miss.India Post has unveiled a set of â‚¹5 postage stamps featuring four of Biharâ€™s most iconic GI-tagged products. And they look absolutely stunning.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLeading the spotlight is Muzaffarpurâ€™s globally loved Shahi Litchi, showcased in vibrant red hues, capturing its freshness and flavor in every detail.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4 GI-tagged Products, 1 Historic Tribute\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis special stamp series pays tribute to four of Biharâ€™s top GI products:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhagalpurâ€™s Zardalu Mango Mithilaâ€™s Makhana Magadhâ€™s Magahi Paan Muzaffarpurâ€™s Shahi Litchi\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBhagalpurâ€™s Zardalu Mango\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMithilaâ€™s Makhana\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMagadhâ€™s Magahi Paan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpurâ€™s Shahi Litchi\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach stamp uses bold, distinctive colors to reflect the character of the produce. The Zardalu Mango features rich greens, the Makhana glows in pure white, and the Magahi Paan appears in deep green. However, the Shahi Litchiâ€™s bright red cluster has become a true eye-catcher. It not only represents Bihar but also offers a visual delight for stamp collectors and cultural enthusiasts alike.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Landmark First in Indian Postal History\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Acharya Chandrakishore Parashar, President of the North Bihar Philatelist Society, this marks the first time in 150 years of Indian postal history that multiple GI-tagged products from a single state have received such recognition simultaneously.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBack in 2023, the Shahi Litchi had already represented Bihar in a mini-sheet of GI fruits released as part of the Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav. That was significant, but this is an even more prominent leap. Now, Bihar doesnâ€™t just represent â€” it dominates the GI narrative on postage stamps.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Identity Travels Global â€” One Stamp at a Time\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese stamps are currently available at the Muzaffarpur Head Post Office and philatelic bureaus across India. They have already caught the attention of collectors and cultural curators.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut more than that, they act as cultural messengers. Every letter sent with these stamps carries a piece of Biharâ€™s identity to the world. It is a bold visual statement of the stateâ€™s growing legacy in agriculture, sustainability, and traditional excellence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis Is More Than a Stamp\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat India Post has done isnâ€™t just a postal update. Itâ€™s a cultural reset. A moment where Biharâ€™s local excellence gets national honor and global reach. These four products arenâ€™t just economic assets â€” theyâ€™re symbols of heritage, livelihoods, and flavor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor thousands of farmers, artisans, and local communities, this gesture means recognition. It places them and their work on a prestigious platform and assures them that their stories matter.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLooking for more such inspiring updates from Bihar?Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates, powerful stories, and real change from the grassroots.Join our 11,000+ global community and become a part of Biharâ€™s digital renaissance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through stories that spotlight culture, grassroots innovation, and business. With top LinkedIn impressions and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, Bihar Say is the digital voice of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
