        "id":  "1200-cr-new-terminal-at-jayprakash-narayan-airport-now-operational",
        "title":  "1,200 Cr New Terminal at Jayprakash Narayan Airport Now Operational!",
        "summary":  "Patna Takes Off in Style: New Terminal at Jayprakash Narayan Airport Now Operational! Bihar just unlocked a new gateway to the skiesâ€”modern, magnificent, and deeply rooted in its heritage. A Historic Day for Biharâ€™s Aviation T...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna Takes Off in Style: New Terminal at Jayprakash Narayan Airport Now Operational!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar just unlocked a new gateway to the skiesâ€”modern, magnificent, and deeply rooted in its heritage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Historic Day for Biharâ€™s Aviation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday, June 3, marks a proud milestone for Bihar. The new terminal at Patnaâ€™s Jayprakash Narayan International Airport is now live and fully operational from 7 AM onwards. From longer queues and cramped spaces to world-class comfort and cutting-edge efficiency, flyers from Patna are stepping into a new era.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInside the Terminal: Where Tradition Meets Technology\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpread across 65,150 sq. meters, the state-of-the-art terminal now handles 3,000 passengers during peak hours and features:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFive aerobridges 11 boarding gates 64 check-in counters 9 ATRS machines for smooth security Digi Yatri gates for contactless travel 4 baggage conveyor belts in the arrivals zone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFive aerobridges\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e11 boarding gates\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e64 check-in counters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e9 ATRS machines for smooth security\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDigi Yatri gates for contactless travel\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4 baggage conveyor belts in the arrivals zone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePassengers stepping in today experienced not just infrastructure, but a showcase of Biharâ€™s soulâ€”from Nalanda-inspired architecture to traditional murals and carvings that turn every journey into an immersive cultural moment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eParking \u0026 Entry Upgraded Too!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReaching the terminal? Itâ€™s easier now. A dedicated flyover leads directly to the departure level, while arrivals exit from the ground floor.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Multi-Level Car Park (MLCP) is also open from today with space for 1,100 vehicles, maintaining the same budget-friendly parking fees. Commuters will also benefit from a designated pick-up zone with clear time limits to avoid congestion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFlight Movement: The Numbers Today\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith 98 aircraft movements already managed today, the airport is operating smoothly under the new system. Air India Express flights to Hyderabad and Guwahati were among the first to operate from the new terminal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeputy General Manager Uma Shankar confirmed that while no international routes have been announced yet, airlines are expected to ramp up domestic services soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Next?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe old terminal will soon be demolished, making way for more parking bays and four additional aerobridge bases. Once completed, the apron will support 11 aircraft, pushing Patna Airportâ€™s capacity to an all-new high.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis expansion raises the annual passenger capacity from 25 lakh to 1 crore, a fourfold jump that reflects Biharâ€™s rising importance in Indiaâ€™s air traffic map.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“£ Be Part of Biharâ€™s Growth Journey\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTodayâ€™s terminal launch is not just about flightsâ€”itâ€™s about pride, progress, and global connectivity. Itâ€™s Bihar telling the world: weâ€™re ready for take-off.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com for real-time updates, inspiring stories, and positive news from across Bihar. Join our 11K+ global community reshaping how the world sees our state.\u003c/p\u003e",
