        "title":  "Ganga Water to Irrigate South Bihar Farm",
        "summary":  "When Rivers Answer the Call of the Fields: Biharâ€™s Ganga Water Revolution Imagine a parched land where hopes of harvest flicker with every dry gust. Now picture that same land revivedâ€”green, nourished, and full of promise. Tha...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eWhen Rivers Answer the Call of the Fields: Biharâ€™s Ganga Water Revolution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine a parched land where hopes of harvest flicker with every dry gust. Now picture that same land revivedâ€”green, nourished, and full of promise. Thatâ€™s the vision Bihar is turning into reality.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a historic move, the government has decided to extend the reach of Ganga water beyond householdsâ€”to the farms of South Bihar. The first drops of this transformation will soon irrigate the soil of districts like Nalanda, Gaya, and Nawada.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Drinking to Drip: Ganga Water to Fuel Irrigation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUntil now, surplus water from the Ganga River was primarily used for drinking water schemes. But with irrigation capacity in several regions dropping by up to 80%, the state has acted decisively.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSantosh Kumar Mall, Principal Secretary of Biharâ€™s Water Resources Department, announced that Gangaâ€™s surplus monsoon water will now travel through pipelines to reach even the long-thirsty Belhar-based Badua reservoir in Banka district.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters: Fighting Drought with Vision\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMany water bodies, even during monsoon, remain underfilled. The Badua reservoir, for instance, has seen its capacity drop significantly due to erratic rainfall. By redirecting Ganga water, not only will this reservoir fill, but the surrounding areas will benefit from expanded irrigation facilities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis initiative is part of the broader Jal Jeevan Hariyali Abhiyan, which emphasizes smart water use, conservation, and climate resilience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot Just Irrigation: Drinking Water Projects on the Horizon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe transformation doesnâ€™t stop at agriculture. Plans are underway to supply treated surface water from the Son River to cities like Aurangabad, Dehri, and Sasaram. Additionally, Kaimurâ€™s Bhabhua and Mohania towns will soon receive water from the Durgawati reservoir.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs per officials, several other dormant reservoirs like Morve, Jalkot, Bascot, and Garhi will also be recharged using Ganga water, ensuring a steady and sustainable water table.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Call for Collective Responsibility\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChief Engineer Awadhesh Kumar emphasized that true prosperity depends on the coexistence of life and greenery. Climate change has made water conservation more urgent than ever. Under this mission, ponds across the state are being cleared of encroachments and restored to store rainwater and boost groundwater levels.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just an infrastructure projectâ€”itâ€™s a moral mission. Every pipeline laid is a promise to the farmers, every drop saved is a step towards Biharâ€™s sustainable future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to see more such bold stories of transformation from Bihar? âž¡ï¸ Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become part of the 11K+ strong global community. Bihar Say is the voice of a changing Biharâ€”unfiltered, apolitical, and unapologetically real.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e#Bihar #GangaWater #Irrigation #WaterManagement #ClimateChange #SouthBihar #SantoshKumarMall #JalJeevanHariyali #Agriculture #WaterCrisis #SustainableDevelopment #Nalanda #BaduaReservoir #BiharSay\u003c/p\u003e",
