        "summary":  "Two Champions, One Dream: Biharâ€™s Rising Fencing Stars Shine Bright In a landmark moment for Bihar, two young athletes from Motihariâ€”Keshar Raj and Ravi Kumar Yadavâ€”have been selected as Khelo India Athletes under the presti...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eTwo Champions, One Dream: Biharâ€™s Rising Fencing Stars Shine Bright\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a landmark moment for Bihar, two young athletes from Motihariâ€”Keshar Raj and Ravi Kumar Yadavâ€”have been selected as Khelo India Athletes under the prestigious scheme of the Sports Authority of India. The recognition is not just a personal milestone, but a testament to Biharâ€™s growing presence in national sports.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Big Announcement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRavindran Shankaran, Director General and CEO of Bihar State Sports Authority, announced the selection. According to him, the Khelo India Talent Identification Committee has chosen eight exceptional fencing talents from across Indiaâ€”two of whom are proudly from Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKeshar Raj will represent in the Foil category, while Ravi Kumar Yadav will compete in the Ã‰pÃ©e event. Starting June 4, 2025, both athletes will begin receiving full-time residential training, health insurance, sports gear, and top-notch coaching under the Khelo India scheme.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAchievements That Paved the Way\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese selections are far from random. Ravi Kumar Yadav recently clinched a bronze medal in the Ã‰pÃ©e event at the Khelo India Youth Games 2025 in Rajgir. He also won a silver at the 68th School Games National Fencing Championship in Jammu and Kashmir and a bronze at the U-17 National Fencing Championship in Rudrapur, Uttarakhand. Impressively, he also represented India in the Cadet World Championship and Asian Championship.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMeanwhile, Keshar Raj has been equally outstanding. She won gold in the U-14 Foil event at the 68th School Games in Jammu and Kashmir, and a bronze at the National U-14 Fencing Championship in Cuttack, Odisha. Her crowning achievement this year was a gold at the Khelo India Asmita League.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Motihari to the National Spotlight\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth athletes started their journey at the District Fencing Training Center located at Khel Bhawan, Motihari. They now train at the National Centre of Excellence in Guwahati, a place where dreams begin to look real.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir discipline, dedication, and achievements showcase what Biharâ€™s youth can achieve with the right support and platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Story of Biharâ€™s Sporting Evolution Continuesâ€¦\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant more such stories of grit and glory from Bihar?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow www.biharsay.com for inspiring updates that reshape Biharâ€™s image. Be a part of the 11K+ global community following Bihar Say, the stateâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e#BiharNews #KheloIndia #FencingIndia #YouthAthletes #SportsDevelopment #BiharSay #Motihari #BiharPride #BiharAthletes #RisingStars\u003c/p\u003e",
