        "id":  "bihars-rural-connectivity-milestone-1843-roads-852-bridges-now-complete",
        "title":  "â‚¹991 Crore Boost Builds 1843 Roads, 852 Bridges Across Rural Bihar",
        "summary":  "Bihar Builds Ahead: 1843 Roads and 852 Bridges Redefine Rural Connectivity Bihar is not just building roads; it is building futures. In a groundbreaking push for rural infrastructure, the Bihar Government has completed 1,843 roads...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar Builds Ahead: 1843 Roads and 852 Bridges Redefine Rural Connectivity\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is not just building roads; it is building futures. In a groundbreaking push for rural infrastructure, the Bihar Government has completed 1,843 roads and 852 bridges across the stateâ€”a bold move reshaping access and opportunity in its villages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMassive Budget, Bigger Impact\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnder the Rural Infrastructure Development Fund (RIDF), the state earmarked a substantial â‚¹991 crore for the 2025-26 fiscal year. This fund was dedicated to accelerating the pace of road and bridge construction across multiple districts. As a result, over 4,818 kilometers of roads now improve rural mobility, and hundreds of villages are no longer cut off during critical times.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDistrict-Wise Progress Sparks Transformation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach division made notable progress. For example:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna Division (including Patna, Nalanda, Bhojpur, and others) completed 493 roads and 159 bridges. Tirhut Division (including Muzaffarpur and Champaran districts) delivered 266 roads and 152 bridges. Purnia Division built 102 roads and a staggering 148 bridges, with Kishanganj completing all 21 approved roads. Magadh Division (Gaya, Jehanabad, Arwal, and others) wrapped up 248 roads and 93 bridges.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuch district-wise execution not only showcases administrative efficiency but also highlights the governmentâ€™s inclusive development approach.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRural Life: Connected and Thriving\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen villages get roads, change follows. With new connectivity:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFarmers reach markets faster. Children attend schools without walking through mud. Patients access healthcare without delays. Local entrepreneurs find new supply chains.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe ripple effect is undeniable. Whether itâ€™s promoting local trade, enhancing educational access, or improving emergency response, rural connectivity fuels social and economic growth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoads to a Stronger Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese infrastructural milestones arenâ€™t just numbersâ€”they are a reflection of Biharâ€™s intent to rise. The strategic focus on rural infrastructure ensures that no part of the state is left behind. With continued efforts, Biharâ€™s villages can evolve into self-sufficient, thriving communities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ For more inspiring updates on Biharâ€™s transformation, follow www.biharsay.com and become a part of our growing 11K+ global community! Bihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through powerful narratives on culture, development, and grassroots heroes.\u003c/p\u003e",
