        "summary":  "After years of delay, the Sultanganj-Aguwani Ghat Bridge is back in action It once symbolised hope. Then it became a reminder of failure. Now, the Sultanganjâ€“Aguwani Ghat bridge, after long delays and a partial collapse, is fina...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eAfter years of delay, the Sultanganj-Aguwani Ghat Bridge is back in action\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt once symbolised hope. Then it became a reminder of failure. Now, the Sultanganjâ€“Aguwani Ghat bridge, after long delays and a partial collapse, is finally being rebuilt. And this time, thereâ€™s a deadline: 18 months.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe broken section between Pier 9 and Pier 13 had shaken public trust. Now, under the direct orders of the High Court, reconstruction has resumed â€” not just with urgency, but also with improved design, revised engineering, and clear accountability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCourt Orders, Government Moves â€” And A New Push for Progress\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar State Bridge Construction Corporation Ltd. (BSBCCL) is handling the repair of the collapsed portion. Itâ€™s not just patchwork â€” the entire stretch is undergoing a structural rethink.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs part of the first phase, the roadway (approach path) is being built immediately. This is to ensure that traffic movement can restart as soon as possible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMihir Kumar Singh, Additional Chief Secretary of the Road Construction Department, confirmed that a series of engineering changes are also underway. For instance, composite girders are being fabricated as per fresh blueprints in an approved workshop.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, experts from IIT Roorkee are offering technical consultation for modifications in the superstructure. Based on their recommendations, reinforcement in the foundation is already in progress.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Bridge Is More Than Just Steel and Cement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe bridge connects Sultanganj in Bhagalpur to Aguwani Ghat in Khagaria. For thousands of commuters, farmers, and traders, this route means shorter travel time, reduced costs, and direct access to markets.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the past year, the collapsed section forced people to take longer, costlier detours. Not to mention, it became a symbol of what goes wrong when public infrastructure fails.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut now, with the bridge work resuming and timelines declared upfront, a sense of faith is returning. If completed on schedule, it can restore much more than just connectivity â€” it can rebuild trust in Biharâ€™s governance and project execution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow Bihar Say for More Stories That Matter\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese are the stories that often fade from the headlines after a few days. But they shape the lives of people on the ground for years. Thatâ€™s why Bihar Say is committed to following every update â€” to keep you informed, engaged, and inspired.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Visit www.biharsay.comJoin our global community of 11,000+ readers and listeners. From stories of change to voices from the ground â€” weâ€™re building Biharâ€™s most credible, apolitical media network.\u003c/p\u003e",
