        "title":  "Travel to Patna from Any Corner of Bihar in 3.5 Hours!",
        "summary":  "Want to Reach Patna in Just 3 Hours? This Bihar Transport Revolution Will Shock You!â€ â€œà¤…à¤¬ à¤ªà¤Ÿà¤¨à¤¾ à¤¹à¤° à¤•à¥‹à¤¨à¥‡ à¤¸à¥‡ à¤¸à¤¿à¤°à¥à¤« à¤¤à¥€à¤¨ à¤˜à¤‚à¤Ÿà¥‡ à¤®à¥‡à¤‚!â€ The Bihar government has secured a hist...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eWant to Reach Patna in Just 3 Hours? This Bihar Transport Revolution Will Shock You!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œà¤…à¤¬ à¤ªà¤Ÿà¤¨à¤¾ à¤¹à¤° à¤•à¥‹à¤¨à¥‡ à¤¸à¥‡ à¤¸à¤¿à¤°à¥à¤« à¤¤à¥€à¤¨ à¤˜à¤‚à¤Ÿà¥‡ à¤®à¥‡à¤‚!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar government has secured a historic win. The Railway Ministry just approved 223 Road Over Bridges (ROBs). As a result, anyone across Bihar can now reach Patna within 3Â½ hours. This massive connectivity milestone is already reshaping travel and transit statewide\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNational Approval and Local Thanks\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTransport Minister Nitin Naveen expressed deep gratitude to the Center and the Railway Ministry. Furthermore, he highlighted Biharâ€™s full technical and administrative backing to ensure smooth progress\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow This Plan Takes Shape\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA review meeting chaired by top officialsâ€”like Mihir Kumar Singh (ACS, Roads) and Naveen Gulati (Railway Board)â€”led to DPR approval for 12 ROBs/RUBs across key districts These include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSaharsa (104B1) Chhapra (47spl) Sitamarhi (55C/3) Gaya (39/C/T, 8/C) Lakhisarai (24/A/E, 27/B/T) Jamui (36) Munger (17/A/E) Aurangabad (28/B, 23/C/T) Muzaffarpur (123)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSaharsa (104B1)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChhapra (47spl)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSitamarhi (55C/3)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGaya (39/C/T, 8/C)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLakhisarai (24/A/E, 27/B/T)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJamui (36)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMunger (17/A/E)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAurangabad (28/B, 23/C/T)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur (123)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDPR Pipeline \u0026 NOCs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDPRs for another 48 ROBs are ready and pending approval by next month. Teams are working on 112 more DPRs simultaneously From March to May, Bihar secured NOCs for all 223 railway crossings. It also covered 236 of 259 LC crossings under various departments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDPRs for another 48 ROBs are ready and pending approval by next month.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTeams are working on 112 more DPRs simultaneously\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom March to May, Bihar secured NOCs for all 223 railway crossings. It also covered 236 of 259 LC crossings under various departments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCountdown to 3.5â€‘Hour Patna Rides\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMinister Naveen made it clear: once these 223 ROBs are ready, travel time to Patna from any district will reduce to under 3 hours 30 minutes. Consequently, traffic jams at level crossings will vanishâ€”making road travel faster and safer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEfficiency boost: Less waiting time at railway gates means faster commutes. Road safety: Overpasses eliminate dangerous clashes between trains and vehicles. Economic uplift: Better connectivity drives trade, business, and mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEfficiency boost: Less waiting time at railway gates means faster commutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoad safety: Overpasses eliminate dangerous clashes between trains and vehicles.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEconomic uplift: Better connectivity drives trade, business, and mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTogether, these projects mark a major transformation in Biharâ€™s transportation landscape.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ For more updates like this, follow www.biharsay.com. Join the 11Kâ€‘strong global community reshaping Biharâ€™s narrative.Bihar Say is Biharâ€™s apolitical storytelling hubâ€”bringing culture, business, grassroots change to the forefront.ðŸŽ™ï¸ Donâ€™t miss BiharCastâ€”our podcast and video series sharing untold stories from Biharâ€™s heart.\u003c/p\u003e",
