        "id":  "six-new-airports-to-come-up-in-bihar",
        "title":  "Bihar Approves â‚¹150 Cr for 6 New Airports",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Sky is Rising! 6 New Airports Coming Up â€” See Where and Why This is Big Bihar to Get 6 Brand-New Airports â€” A Game-Changer for Connectivity \u0026 Growth Biharâ€™s wings are spreading wide â€” literally.In a landmark deci...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Sky is Rising! 6 New Airports Coming Up â€” See Where and Why This is Big\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar to Get 6 Brand-New Airports â€” A Game-Changer for Connectivity \u0026 Growth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s wings are spreading wide â€” literally.In a landmark decision that could redefine connectivity in the state, the Bihar Cabinet has greenlit the development of six new airports. This decision, taken just months ahead of the state assembly elections, is more than a vote-winning move â€” itâ€™s a massive push toward regional growth and infrastructure development.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLetâ€™s dive into what this means for everyday Biharis, businesses, and dreamers waiting for takeoff.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere Are These New Airports Coming Up?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese airports are part of the Central Governmentâ€™s UDAN scheme (Ude Desh Ka Aam Nagrik), aimed at boosting regional air connectivity. Hereâ€™s where the runways are about to roll out:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMadhubani Birpur (Supaul) Munger Valmiki Nagar (Bettiah) Muzaffarpur Saharsa\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMadhubani\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBirpur (Supaul)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMunger\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eValmiki Nagar (Bettiah)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSaharsa\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach of these regions, rich in culture and human potential, has long awaited easier access to national hubs. This move could not only improve travel but also unlock tourism and business opportunities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCost and Execution â€” How Much, Who, and How?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe total budget sanctioned for the project is â‚¹150 crore.Each airport will receive â‚¹25 crore for its development.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) has been approved between Biharâ€™s Directorate of Aviation and the Airports Authority of India (AAI). This ensures the right expertise is in place, without delay.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Additional Chief Secretary S. Siddharth, the agreement is a timely move in sync with Biharâ€™s growth narrative.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt Doesnâ€™t Stop There â€” Patna Gets 5-Star Boost\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a bid to upgrade urban infrastructure too, the Bihar Cabinet has approved the construction of a five-star hotel near Income Tax Golumber in Patna.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe project will be developed by Kumar Infratrade Enterprises Ltd under the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model, with a 90-year land lease. Two more luxury hotels are in the bidding process â€” one near Bankipore Bus Stand and another near R Golumber.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis signals Biharâ€™s readiness to welcome global and domestic business travellers, while supporting tourism.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupporting Farmers and Soldiers â€” All in One Meeting\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis cabinet meeting was not just about planes and hotels. The government also fixed the Minimum Support Price (MSP) for key crops:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChana: â‚¹5,650 Mustard: â‚¹5,950 Masoor: â‚¹6,700\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChana: â‚¹5,650\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMustard: â‚¹5,950\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMasoor: â‚¹6,700\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso, the contracts of 1,717 retired army personnel serving in Special Auxiliary Police (SAP) were extended till 2025-26.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEducation Sector Gets Attention Too\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor schools and libraries across the state, the cabinet approved new recruitment guidelines for clerks and librarians. Under the updated rules:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e50% of clerk posts in the Education Department will be filled via compassionate appointments The rest will be open for direct recruitment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e50% of clerk posts in the Education Department will be filled via compassionate appointments\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe rest will be open for direct recruitment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Airport Decision Matters for You\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just about travel â€” itâ€™s about transforming Biharâ€™s identity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom job creation to real estate boosts, tourism upliftment to global access â€” this decision carries impact far beyond its â‚¹150 crore tag. Bihar is no longer waiting; itâ€™s building its future, one airport at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ What Next?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpect groundbreaking ceremonies soon. As infrastructure rolls in, so will opportunities. Whether youâ€™re a startup founder in Muzaffarpur, a student from Saharsa, or a tourist eyeing Valmiki Nagarâ€™s wildlife sanctuary â€” your access is about to become easier than ever.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“Œ Want to Stay Updated on Biharâ€™s Growth Stories?ðŸ‘‰ Head over to www.biharsay.com for regular updates and powerful, apolitical stories that redefine Biharâ€™s image.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâœ… Join our 11k-strong global communityâœ… Follow Bihar Say â€” Biharâ€™s leading digital storytelling platform with top engagement on LinkedIn, collabs with DailyHunt, and the creator of BiharCast, Biharâ€™s flagship podcast.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:#Bihar airports bihar cabinet decision Bihar development news Bihar infrastructure Bihar MSP new airports in Bihar Patna five-star hotel regional connectivity Bihar UDAN Scheme Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:#Bihar airports bihar cabinet decision Bihar development news Bihar infrastructure Bihar MSP new airports in Bihar Patna five-star hotel regional connectivity Bihar UDAN Scheme Bihar\u003c/p\u003e",
