        "id":  "bihar-becomes-1st-state-to-adopt-e-voting-system-for-urban-polls",
        "title":  "Bihar becomes 1st state to adopt e-voting system for urban polls",
        "summary":  "Bihar Creates History! Indiaâ€™s 1st E-Voting System Rolls Outâ€”No Booth, Just a Tap! Booth par line nahi, ab sirf mobile ka sign!Bihar has officially become the first Indian state to introduce an e-voting system for urban body e...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar Creates History! Indiaâ€™s 1st E-Voting System Rolls Outâ€”No Booth, Just a Tap!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBooth par line nahi, ab sirf mobile ka sign!Bihar has officially become the first Indian state to introduce an e-voting system for urban body elections. This shift marks a significant moment in the countryâ€™s democratic journeyâ€”where voting is no longer confined to booths but extends to mobile screens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile much of India remains tied to traditional voting methods, Bihar has boldly reimagined the electoral process. The Bihar State Election Commission (BSEC) is enabling citizens to vote with just a tap on their Android devices, redefining the way elections are held.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInclusive Voting: A System That Reaches Everyone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe e-voting initiative is set to debut in the upcoming municipal and urban body polls on 28th June. As per State Election Commissioner Deepak Prasad, over 10,000 voters have already registered, and the system will enable 50,000 voters to participate without visiting polling booths.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost importantly, this system caters to sections of society often left out of the voting process. These include migrant labourers, differently-abled citizens, pregnant women, senior citizens, and those suffering from serious illnesses. By giving these individuals a chance to vote remotely, Bihar is taking a strong step towards a more inclusive and representative democracy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Technology Behind E-Voting\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe BSEC has introduced two mobile apps to carry out the e-voting process:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ee-Voting SECBHR, developed in collaboration with the Centre for Development of Advanced Computing (C-DAC) A second application built by the Bihar State Election Commission\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ee-Voting SECBHR, developed in collaboration with the Centre for Development of Advanced Computing (C-DAC)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA second application built by the Bihar State Election Commission\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth apps incorporate multiple layers of security to ensure a tamper-proof and transparent voting process. These features include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBlockchain technology Liveness detection Face match Live face scan Face comparison\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBlockchain technology\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLiveness detection\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFace match\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLive face scan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFace comparison\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuch like the VVPAT system used with EVMs, the e-voting setup includes an audit trail for verification and transparency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Consistent Trail of Innovation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not the first time Bihar has led the way in electoral innovation. The Bihar State Election Commission has already pioneered several tech-driven solutions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFace Recognition System (FRS) for real-time voter verification Optical Character Recognition (OCR) for accurate and fast vote counting Digital locking mechanisms for enhanced EVM security\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFace Recognition System (FRS) for real-time voter verification\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOptical Character Recognition (OCR) for accurate and fast vote counting\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDigital locking mechanisms for enhanced EVM security\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese measures not only modernize the voting process but also set a national benchmark in electoral integrity and efficiency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Joins Global E-Voting Pioneers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGlobally, only a few regions have implemented secure remote e-voting systems. Estonia is the only known country to have successfully used nationwide e-voting. With this launch, Bihar joins a select league of global innovators in electoral technology.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSource : www.newsonair.gov.in\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Tuned!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want to keep discovering how Bihar is rewriting its narrative with technology, inclusion, and pride, then donâ€™t miss out.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become part of our 11k+ strong community worldwide. From grassroots revolutions to cutting-edge innovation, Bihar Say is where Biharâ€™s real stories come alive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ—£ï¸ Bihar Say â€” Biharâ€™s digital voice to the world.\u003c/p\u003e",
