        "title":  "â€˜Made-in-Biharâ€™ Locomotive to Power Africaâ€™s 3,000 Cr Iron Ore Project",
        "summary":  "ðŸ‡®ðŸ‡³ Bihar Builds for the World: First â€˜Made-in-Marhowrahâ€™ Locomotive to Power Africaâ€™s Largest Iron Ore Project ðŸŒ From Bihar to Guinea: How a Quiet Town is Powering Africaâ€™s Iron Backbone â€œBihar ka Marhowrah, ab ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eðŸ‡®ðŸ‡³ Bihar Builds for the World: First â€˜Made-in-Marhowrahâ€™ Locomotive to Power Africaâ€™s Largest Iron Ore Project ðŸŒ\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Bihar to Guinea: How a Quiet Town is Powering Africaâ€™s Iron Backbone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œBihar ka Marhowrah, ab duniya ke nakshon pe!â€Yes, you read that right. On June 20, 2025, Prime Minister Narendra Modi will flag off the first indigenous locomotive for export, built not in a metro city, but at Marhowrah in Biharâ€”a town now redefining Indiaâ€™s industrial story.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just a one-off milestone. This is India making a bold, global markâ€”straight from the heart of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn Export Worth â‚¹3,000 Crore, A Message Worth Billions\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Marhowrah manufacturing facility, operated by Wabtec Corporation, will supply 150 locomotives to SimFerâ€™s Simandou iron ore project in the Republic of Guinea over the next three years.The total project value? More than â‚¹3,000 crore.This is not just businessâ€”itâ€™s an international endorsement of Indiaâ€™s engineering brilliance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilt for Performance: Speed, Strength, and Smart Tech\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese locomotives are no ordinary machines.Theyâ€™re capable of hauling 100 wagons in pairs at peak performance, complete with air-conditioned cabins, microwaves, refrigerators, and even waterless toilets.Not only that, but they meet top-tier emission norms, come with fire detection systems, and are engineered for ergonomic comfort.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks to features like DPWCS (Distributed Power Wireless Control System), these locos promise synchronised operation and high-efficiency freight managementâ€”something thatâ€™s rare even in many developed economies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThree Gauges, One Factory: Built for the Global Grid\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo manufacture these diverse machines, Marhowrahâ€™s Wabtec plant laid down broad gauge, standard gauge, and cape gauge tracksâ€”an engineering feat that few factories in the world can claim.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis flexible infrastructure allowed India to win the project via global bidding, not just compete.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJobs, Innovation, and Global Reputationâ€”All in One Package\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExecutive Director Dilip Kumar of the Railway Board noted how this export project is positioning Marhowrah as a global hub.From local employment to cutting-edge technology transfer, Bihar is not just making trainsâ€”itâ€™s making headlines.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just about Guinea or locomotives. Itâ€™s about Indiaâ€™s promise to the world. Itâ€™s about Atmanirbhar Bharatâ€”India as a producer, innovator, and global infrastructure partner.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndia-Africa Ties: Now on Fast Track\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this project, India isnâ€™t just exporting locomotivesâ€”itâ€™s laying tracks to deeper economic partnerships with Africa.Guineaâ€™s largest iron ore project will now run on the wheels of Indian engineering and Bihari resilience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMr. Kumar summed it up best:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œThis is a shining example of Atmanirbhar Bharat powering global infrastructure through innovation and quality manufacturing.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œThis is a shining example of Atmanirbhar Bharat powering global infrastructure through innovation and quality manufacturing.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is building more than machinesâ€”itâ€™s building its global identity.Marhowrah is not just making trainsâ€”itâ€™s making history.India is not just exporting hardwareâ€”itâ€™s exporting trust.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ To read more powerful updates from Bihar that break stereotypes and inspire change,follow www.biharsay.comJoin our 11K+ global community reshaping Biharâ€™s narrativeâ€”one powerful story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
