        "summary":  "Bihar Shines Loud in Silence: Deaf Athletes Lead Nation in Taekwondo Gloryâ€ When the world listens less, Bihar speaks loudestâ€”through strength, skill, and spirit.In a historic moment at the 27th National Deaf Senior and 10th J...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar Shines Loud in Silence: Deaf Athletes Lead Nation in Taekwondo Gloryâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen the world listens less, Bihar speaks loudestâ€”through strength, skill, and spirit.In a historic moment at the 27th National Deaf Senior and 10th Junior \u0026 Sub-Junior Championships held at VSSD College, Kanpur, Biharâ€™s deaf athletes stole the spotlight. With unmatched determination, Bihar claimed both senior and junior taekwondo titles, outclassing competitors from across the nation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Deaf Champions Break Barriers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSport isnâ€™t just about medalsâ€”itâ€™s about moments, and Bihar created many of them.Their victories at the national deaf championships are not just triumphs of skill but stories of grit, discipline, and untold potential.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile Punjab finished as the runner-up and Uttar Pradesh and Haryana shared the third spot, it was Biharâ€™s dominance in taekwondoâ€”both junior and senior categoriesâ€”that became the highlight of the championship.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJudo Warriors Also Made Their Mark\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBesides taekwondo, the championship also hosted intense judo battles, where young deaf athletes showcased astonishing power and technique.From UPâ€™s Shabnam and Pragati clinching the 44 kg and 48 kg womenâ€™s categories to Maharashtraâ€™s Raghunath Prasad and Omkar Suresh dominating the 55 kg and 100 kg menâ€™s groupsâ€”every bout was a showcase of unspoken power.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTop Performers in Judo:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSenior Women: 44 kg â€“ Shabnam (UP) 48 kg â€“ Pragati (UP) 52 kg â€“ Niranjana (Haryana) 63 kg â€“ Aditi (Delhi) Senior Men: 60 kg â€“ Himanshu Singh (UP) 81 kg â€“ Sumit Saini (Punjab) 110 kg+ â€“ Karandeep (Delhi)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSenior Women:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e44 kg â€“ Shabnam (UP) 48 kg â€“ Pragati (UP) 52 kg â€“ Niranjana (Haryana) 63 kg â€“ Aditi (Delhi)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e44 kg â€“ Shabnam (UP)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e48 kg â€“ Pragati (UP)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e52 kg â€“ Niranjana (Haryana)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e63 kg â€“ Aditi (Delhi)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSenior Men:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e60 kg â€“ Himanshu Singh (UP) 81 kg â€“ Sumit Saini (Punjab) 110 kg+ â€“ Karandeep (Delhi)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e60 kg â€“ Himanshu Singh (UP)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e81 kg â€“ Sumit Saini (Punjab)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e110 kg+ â€“ Karandeep (Delhi)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese names deserve applauseâ€”not just for the wins, but for the voices they raise for thousands of differently-abled athletes across India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKanpurâ€™s Young Fighters Also Emerge Strong\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe host city, Kanpur, added local pride to the event. Four young fighters from the UP team gave a stellar performance, winning 2 silver and 2 bronze medals in taekwondo.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKrishna Agarwal and Yuvraj Chaurasia â€“ Silver Arman and Srishti Gupta â€“ Bronze\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKrishna Agarwal and Yuvraj Chaurasia â€“ Silver\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArman and Srishti Gupta â€“ Bronze\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese young warriors, especially from the deaf community, proved that no barrier is louder than passion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Is Not Just Competingâ€”Itâ€™s Leading a Revolution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t the first time Bihar has led from the front. But the victory here is differentâ€”it reflects a deeper story of empowerment, inclusion, and quiet leadership.From grassroots training to disciplined dedication, these athletes are rewriting whatâ€™s possible for deaf sports in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s consistent rise in adaptive sports sends a message loud and clear: With the right support, silence becomes strength.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Join the JourneyIf this story inspired you, imagine the thousands of unheard tales waiting to be told.ðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com to stay updated with more such incredible stories and be a part of our 11,000+ strong global community.Letâ€™s celebrate the real Biharâ€”one untold story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
