        "title":  "Artkalaâ€™s DIY Revolution Started in Patna and Now Has 14 Million Fans",
        "summary":  "How Artkala Reached 14 Million Followers and Became Indiaâ€™s DIY Powerhouse In a quiet lane of Patna, where dreams often collide with reality, Pawan Kumar, along with his two sisters Puja and Sneha, and girlfriend Sweta, started ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eHow Artkala Reached 14 Million Followers and Became Indiaâ€™s DIY Powerhouse\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a quiet lane of Patna, where dreams often collide with reality, Pawan Kumar, along with his two sisters Puja and Sneha, and girlfriend Sweta, started something that would soon touch millions of hearts. Today, with 14 million+ followers across platforms, Artkala is not just a DIY channelâ€”itâ€™s a movement from the heart of Bihar that proves creativity can change lives.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2016: When Art Became a Lifeline for a Middle-Class Family\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBack in 2016, the journey began not with funding or fame, but with frustration. Coming from a middle-class family in Bihar, the trio of siblings and Sweta turned their everyday struggle into something beautifulâ€”one craft video at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing household items, handmade dÃ©cor, and unshakable belief, they uploaded their first DIY video on YouTubeâ€”hoping to earn a little but determined to express a lot. Their only investment? Paper, glue, and passion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday, Artkala stands tall as one of Indiaâ€™s most loved DIY communities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore Than Just Views: A Bihar Startup with Heart\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe team behind Artkala isnâ€™t a companyâ€”itâ€™s a family. Pawan, Puja, Sneha, and Sweta didnâ€™t just create content; they created a bond with millions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTogether, they launched:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArtkala DIY for full tutorials Artkala Shorts for quick inspiration Artkala Angan for traditional crafts and home vibes\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArtkala DIY for full tutorials\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArtkala Shorts for quick inspiration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArtkala Angan for traditional crafts and home vibes\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir mission was clear: Creativity is for everyone, not just those with resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMilestones That Speak for Themselves\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom receiving YouTubeâ€™s Golden Play Buttons to breaking viral records with craft hacks, the Artkala team proved that consistency matters. Their 14 million+ fans across platforms include kids, parents, teachers, and art lovers across the globe.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSweta, Pawanâ€™s girlfriend, has played a major creative role in Artkala Shortsâ€™ success, bringing fresh, relatable content that drives the brandâ€™s modern edge.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir content has been more than â€œDIYâ€â€”itâ€™s become â€œDo It Your way.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Patna to Pan-India: A Digital Brand is Born\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat began as a YouTube hobby now fuels a full-fledged online store, selling DIY kits, handmade gifts, and festive decor. All designed, packed, and shippedâ€”right from Patna.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArtkala isnâ€™t just creating products. Theyâ€™re creating local employment, spotlighting regional talent, and bringing Biharâ€™s creativity to the world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJosh Talks Bihar: The Story Behind the Spotlight\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen Pawan shared his story on Josh Talks Bihar, he wasnâ€™t just celebrating success. He was reminding every young dreamer that a small space can create a big impact.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWeâ€™re not influencers. Weâ€™re creators from Biharâ€”building something with heart and hands.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWeâ€™re not influencers. Weâ€™re creators from Biharâ€”building something with heart and hands.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat We Can All Learn from Artkala\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou donâ€™t need a studioâ€”you need a reason. Bihar doesnâ€™t wait for validationâ€”it builds from scratch. Creativity doesnâ€™t need permissionâ€”it just needs passion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou donâ€™t need a studioâ€”you need a reason.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar doesnâ€™t wait for validationâ€”it builds from scratch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCreativity doesnâ€™t need permissionâ€”it just needs passion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf youâ€™re still wondering where innovation comes from, look beyond the metros. Itâ€™s already happening in places like Patna, in rooms filled with hope and hard work.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want more untold stories of Biharâ€™s creators? Join the 11k+ global community at www.biharsay.com for daily inspiration.\u003c/p\u003e",
