        "title":  "Bihar to get its 1st nuclear power plant under SMR scheme",
        "summary":  "â€œà¤…à¤¬ à¤¬à¤¿à¤¹à¤¾à¤° à¤¬à¤¦à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾ à¤Šà¤°à¥à¤œà¤¾ à¤•à¥€ à¤ªà¤°à¤¿à¤­à¤¾à¤·à¤¾â€ Nuclear Power Boost for Bihar: Clean Energy, Jobs, and Growth Ahead Bihar Takes a Bold Step Towards Energy Security Bihar is entering a n...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œà¤…à¤¬ à¤¬à¤¿à¤¹à¤¾à¤° à¤¬à¤¦à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾ à¤Šà¤°à¥à¤œà¤¾ à¤•à¥€ à¤ªà¤°à¤¿à¤­à¤¾à¤·à¤¾â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNuclear Power Boost for Bihar: Clean Energy, Jobs, and Growth Ahead\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Takes a Bold Step Towards Energy Security\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is entering a new era of energy independence. The central government has approved a Small Modular Reactor (SMR) for the state. This modern nuclear power unit is part of a national plan to install six SMRs across India. Biharâ€™s inclusion signals its growing importance in the countryâ€™s clean energy landscape.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe SMR announcement came during a press conference in Patna. The state government had requested a nuclear energy project, and the central authorities gave their full support. This approval isnâ€™t just symbolicâ€”itâ€™s a catalyst for economic growth, sustainability, and self-reliance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Bihar Needs Nuclear Power Now\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar has long faced issues related to energy shortage and dependency on external grids. Although progress has been made in power generation, rising industrial and residential demand continues to push the limits.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt this critical moment, nuclear power emerges as a reliable solution. Unlike coal or gas, SMRs provide uninterrupted, emission-free energy. With Bihar preparing for rapid infrastructure and industrial expansion, a clean and consistent energy source becomes essential.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, this project aligns with Indiaâ€™s broader vision: enabling every state to contribute to the nationâ€™s energy security.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat Makes SMRs Ideal for Bihar?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSmall Modular Reactors (SMRs) differ from conventional nuclear plants in several ways. They are compact, cost-effective, and significantly safer. These features make them particularly suitable for states like Bihar that are building new-age infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHereâ€™s how SMRs stand out:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRapid Deployment: SMRs require less time to install compared to traditional reactors. Lower Costs: Their modular design makes them more affordable and scalable. High Safety: Modern containment systems reduce operational risks. Minimal Footprint: These reactors can function in smaller, semi-urban areas. Green Credentials: They release no carbon emissions, supporting global climate goals.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRapid Deployment: SMRs require less time to install compared to traditional reactors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLower Costs: Their modular design makes them more affordable and scalable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHigh Safety: Modern containment systems reduce operational risks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMinimal Footprint: These reactors can function in smaller, semi-urban areas.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreen Credentials: They release no carbon emissions, supporting global climate goals.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks to these advantages, SMRs are being seen as the future of nuclear powerâ€”not just in India, but worldwide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond Energy: Development That Touches Lives\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe introduction of an SMR in Bihar will deliver far-reaching benefits. Firstly, it will help eliminate power cuts and voltage issues, ensuring round-the-clock electricity across sectors. Secondly, the project will create thousands of direct and indirect jobsâ€”from construction to maintenance and technical operations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, it is expected to attract further investments in energy tech and manufacturing. Stable electricity will make it easier to run schools, hospitals, factories, and digital infrastructure across both rural and urban areas.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, the SMR facility will require highly skilled professionals, encouraging upskilling and technical education within the state. Biharâ€™s youth will no longer need to migrate elsewhere for such opportunities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Future Powered by Clean Energy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis nuclear power project isnâ€™t just a plant. Itâ€™s a turning point. It showcases Biharâ€™s readiness to be part of Indiaâ€™s clean energy revolution and to lead from the front. With careful planning and consistent support, the project will demonstrate how technology can serve both development and the environment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs the country scales its green ambitions, states like Bihar must play a leading role. By stepping into nuclear energy now, Bihar secures not just electricity, but also a reputation for innovation and resilience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Ahead with Stories That Matter\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to know how Bihar is shaping its future?Explore real, impactful stories that highlight culture, business, and grassroots transformation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Visit www.biharsay.com for regular updates.Join our community of 12,000+ readers across the world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is your go-to digital platform for apolitical storytellingâ€”reshaping the stateâ€™s image, one powerful story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
