        "title":  "Bihar Govt Forms Trust to Build Grand Janaki Temple at Punaura Dham, Sitamarhi",
        "summary":  "â€˜Punaura Dham Is Callingâ€™: Biharâ€™s Cultural Pride Gets a Majestic Makeover â€œYeh sirf mandir nahi, Bihar ke gaurav ki nayi pehchaan hai.â€In a landmark step, Bihar has initiated a spiritual and cultural revival by announci...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€˜Punaura Dham Is Callingâ€™: Biharâ€™s Cultural Pride Gets a Majestic Makeover\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œYeh sirf mandir nahi, Bihar ke gaurav ki nayi pehchaan hai.â€In a landmark step, Bihar has initiated a spiritual and cultural revival by announcing a grand Janaki Mandir at Punaura Dham, the birthplace of Goddess Sita. Located just 5 km from Sitamarhi town, this sacred site is set to receive a transformative makeover, inspired by the majestic Ram Temple in Ayodhya.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo fast-track this development, the state government has formed a dedicated nine-member trust, marking a bold stride in preserving Biharâ€™s heritage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrust Formed to Lead Construction and Redevelopment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs per the Law Departmentâ€™s gazette notification, the newly constituted body, named Shree Janaki Janam Bhumi Punaura Dham Mandir Nyas Samiti, came into immediate effect. This trust is not just symbolicâ€”it has clear responsibilities and leadership.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Chief Secretary leads the trust as its Chairman. Development Commissioner takes charge as Vice-Chairman. Sitamarhiâ€™s District Magistrate and Deputy Development Commissioner will serve as Secretary and Treasurer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Chief Secretary leads the trust as its Chairman.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopment Commissioner takes charge as Vice-Chairman.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSitamarhiâ€™s District Magistrate and Deputy Development Commissioner will serve as Secretary and Treasurer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, the Mahanth of Punaura Dham Mutth, secretaries of Tourism, Road Construction, and Urban Development and Housing departments, along with the Divisional Commissioner of Tirhut, are key members. Together, they bring administrative strength and spiritual insight.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportantly, the trustâ€™s bank account will be jointly managed by the Secretary and Treasurer to ensure transparency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCM Shares Blueprint of the Temple\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn June 22, Biharâ€™s Chief Minister Nitish Kumar publicly unveiled the final design of the new temple complex. Sharing it on social media, he wrote:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œIt gives me immense pleasure to announce that the design for the comprehensive development of Punaura Dham, Sitamarhi, that includes construction of a grand temple and other structures, is now complete.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œIt gives me immense pleasure to announce that the design for the comprehensive development of Punaura Dham, Sitamarhi, that includes construction of a grand temple and other structures, is now complete.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis announcement wasnâ€™t just ceremonial. It followed the cabinetâ€™s approval to appoint a private design consultant and a sanctioned budget of â‚¹120 croreâ€”highlighting the scale and commitment to the project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHereâ€™s What the Punaura Dham Makeover Will Include\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar isnâ€™t just constructing a templeâ€”itâ€™s building an entire spiritual experience. Under the redevelopment plan, visitors can expect:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSita Vatika and Luv-Kush Vatika, dedicated to the divine family A sacred Parikrama Path for pilgrims Interactive kiosks showcasing the life and legacy of Goddess Sita A cafeteria, childrenâ€™s play zones, and improved public amenities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSita Vatika and Luv-Kush Vatika, dedicated to the divine family\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA sacred Parikrama Path for pilgrims\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInteractive kiosks showcasing the life and legacy of Goddess Sita\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA cafeteria, childrenâ€™s play zones, and improved public amenities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearly, the transformation aims to serve not only spiritual seekers but also families, tourists, and culture enthusiasts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Punaura Dham Matters: A Blend of History, Faith \u0026 Tourism\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery year, thousands of devotees flock to Punaura Dham, yet its infrastructure didnâ€™t match its significance. This revamp bridges that gap, offering both religious reverence and tourism potential. Unlike other temple projects, this initiative is being driven with administrative clarity, cultural sensitivity, and non-political focus.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuch developments also contribute to Biharâ€™s image makeover, showcasing a state that celebrates its ancient roots while embracing modern planning.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ðŸ½ Want to stay ahead on cultural revival and heritage updates like this?ðŸ”— Follow www.biharsay.com and join our 11k+ strong global community.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, spotlighting changemakers, traditions, and cultural rebirths that define the real Bihar. With top LinkedIn impressions, over 11,000 followers, and partnerships with platforms like Dailyhunt, we are building a new digital narrative for the state.\u003c/p\u003e",
