        "title":  "How DeWall Ads Is Monetizing Indiaâ€™s Walls",
        "summary":  "â€œFrom Village Walls to Digital Boards: How DeWall Ads is Painting a New Ad Story from Biharâ€A Feature from the â€™60 Days â€“ 60 Startups from Biharâ€™ Series by Bihar Say â€œWalls once ignored are now incomes unlocked.â€That...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œFrom Village Walls to Digital Boards: How DeWall Ads is Painting a New Ad Story from Biharâ€A Feature from the â€™60 Days â€“ 60 Startups from Biharâ€™ Series by Bihar Say\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWalls once ignored are now incomes unlocked.â€Thatâ€™s how Raushan Kumar, a young visionary from Bihar, describes the idea that birthed DeWall Adsâ€”a Noida-based startup determined to reshape outdoor advertising in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn 2024, without a penny in external funding but powered by belief and hustle, Raushan launched DeWall Ads. What started as a simple observationâ€”â€Why do so many blank walls go unused while businesses struggle to find outdoor ad space?â€â€”has turned into a digital platform with the potential to transform the out-of-home (OOH) advertising industry.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2024: A Bihar-born Startup Quietly Disrupts Outdoor Advertising\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen you walk through urban and rural India, one thing is commonâ€”walls. From tea stalls to rooftops, these concrete canvases often lie idle. But Raushan saw them as micro billboardsâ€”each one a business opportunity waiting to be tapped.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeWall Ads is more than a tech product. Itâ€™s a bridgeâ€”connecting local wall owners (who need income) with businesses (who need visibility). Through their mobile application, now live on the Play Store, users can either list their walls for rent or book ad spaces by location, square footage, and visibility range.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWe are not just digitizing walls,â€ Raushan says. â€œWeâ€™re decentralizing advertisingâ€”bringing power to people and paint to places.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWe are not just digitizing walls,â€ Raushan says. â€œWeâ€™re decentralizing advertisingâ€”bringing power to people and paint to places.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis simplicity has fueled rapid interest. Even without funding, DeWall Ads now competes with 161 companies globally, including giants like Focus Media, oOh! Media, and Daktronics. That alone speaks volumes about the relevance of their model.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Self-Sustained Model: No Investors, Only Innovators\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeWall Ads operates without external funding. In the startup world, thatâ€™s often seen as a disadvantage. But for Raushan, it has become their biggest strength.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œEvery rupee we earn, every partnership we buildâ€”it all makes us sharper, closer to the ground, and resilient,â€ Raushan explains.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œEvery rupee we earn, every partnership we buildâ€”it all makes us sharper, closer to the ground, and resilient,â€ Raushan explains.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis lean approach has helped DeWall Ads build features that reflect grassroots realities:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWall owners can upload location, dimensions, and visibility factors. Agents are assigned to manage printing, placement, and reporting. Clients can track ad performance through an intuitive dashboard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWall owners can upload location, dimensions, and visibility factors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAgents are assigned to manage printing, placement, and reporting.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClients can track ad performance through an intuitive dashboard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe platform isnâ€™t just about buying or selling spaceâ€”itâ€™s about creating a trust-driven ecosystem for hyperlocal advertising.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar to Noida: The Spirit of Grit, Growth, and Going Beyond\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRaushanâ€™s story isnâ€™t just about business. Itâ€™s about belief.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA native of Bihar, he represents a new wave of founders who arenâ€™t waiting for metros or venture funds to validate their dreams. They are building for Indiaâ€”by India and in India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat makes DeWall Ads inspiring isnâ€™t just the technology or the strategyâ€”itâ€™s the story of a Bihar founder who saw potential not in pitch decks but on peeling paint and village walls.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf a wall can become a window of opportunityâ€”imagine what your idea can become.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com to discover more untold startup stories and become a part of Biharâ€™s growing 12,000+ global community.\u003c/p\u003e",
