        "title":  "NTPC Barh Adds 370 MW to Bihar Grid",
        "summary":  "Bihar Powers Up: NTPC Barh Adds 370 MW, Strengthening the Stateâ€™s Energy Backbone Kya aapne suna? Bihar has taken a bold step toward energy independence. The NTPC Barh Super Thermal Power Plant has successfully commissioned its ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar Powers Up: NTPC Barh Adds 370 MW, Strengthening the Stateâ€™s Energy Backbone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKya aapne suna? Bihar has taken a bold step toward energy independence. The NTPC Barh Super Thermal Power Plant has successfully commissioned its fifth unit, adding 370 MW of electricity to the stateâ€™s power grid. This is not just another infrastructure updateâ€”itâ€™s a significant milestone in Biharâ€™s path to reliable and robust energy supply.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNTPC Barhâ€™s New Unit Goes Live\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocated in Patna district, the Barh power plant has now completed the final commissioning of Stage-1, Unit-3, with a capacity of 660 MW. After a successful trial completed on June 5, the unit is scheduled to start commercial operations from July 1. Out of this, Bihar will directly receive 370 MW of electricity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis newly operational unit builds on the earlier four units of the plant, each also rated at 660 MW, which are already supplying power to the state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Total Capacity of 3300 MW â€“ What It Means for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the fifth unit coming online, the total generation capacity of NTPC Barh now reaches 3300 MW. Hereâ€™s how the allocation breaks down:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStage-1 (3 units Ã— 660 MW): Bihar gets a 56.08% share, which amounts to 1110 MW. Stage-2 (2 units Ã— 660 MW): The state receives a higher 86.04% share, resulting in 1136 MW.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStage-1 (3 units Ã— 660 MW): Bihar gets a 56.08% share, which amounts to 1110 MW.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStage-2 (2 units Ã— 660 MW): The state receives a higher 86.04% share, resulting in 1136 MW.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn total, Bihar now secures 2246 MW of power from the Barh plant. This level of allocation marks a significant improvement in the stateâ€™s energy availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImpact on Biharâ€™s Energy Landscape\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis increase in power supply is more than just numbers. It ensures:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUninterrupted electricity during high-demand periods. Improved quality of life for residents with fewer power cuts. A stronger foundation for industrial and commercial expansion. More stable rural electrification efforts. Greater control over energy planning for the coming years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUninterrupted electricity during high-demand periods.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImproved quality of life for residents with fewer power cuts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA stronger foundation for industrial and commercial expansion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore stable rural electrification efforts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreater control over energy planning for the coming years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn short, it lays the groundwork for Biharâ€™s long-term development across sectors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNTPC: Powering the Progress\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe National Thermal Power Corporation (NTPC) is behind this strategic project. As Indiaâ€™s largest energy company, NTPC has played a key role in transforming Biharâ€™s energy sector. The Barh Super Thermal Power Plant is a major part of this mission, supplying not only electricity but also confidence in Biharâ€™s ability to meet its energy needs independently.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a clear example of how infrastructure investments can power progress and support governance objectives at the grassroots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated with Biharâ€™s Development\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more such regular updates on infrastructure, energy, and innovation in Bihar, follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 11,000+ strong global community.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change. With thousands of readers, top LinkedIn impressions, and collaborations with platforms like DailyHunt, we are the digital voice of a changing Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur flagship podcast and video series, BiharCast, dives deep into untold stories and rising voices from the heart of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
