        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Sunny Kumar Wins Silver in Indian Open Long Jump, Leaps Into National Spotlight\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Practice Fields to Podiums: Sunny Kumarâ€™s Silver Shines for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œà¤œà¤¹à¤¾à¤‚ à¤œà¤¼à¤®à¥€à¤¨ à¤›à¥‚à¤¤à¥€ à¤¹à¥ˆ à¤¹à¥Œà¤¸à¤²à¥‹à¤‚ à¤•à¥€ à¤Šà¤‚à¤šà¤¾à¤ˆ, à¤µà¤¹à¥€à¤‚ à¤¸à¥‡ à¤¶à¥à¤°à¥‚ à¤¹à¥‹à¤¤à¥€ à¤¹à¥ˆ à¤¬à¤¿à¤¹à¤¾à¤° à¤•à¥€ à¤•à¤¹à¤¾à¤¨à¥€!â€At the Indian Open Athletics Meet in Bengaluru, Biharâ€™s Sunny Kumar made headlines by winning the silver medal in the menâ€™s long jump. He secured second place with a jump of 7.90 meters, missing the gold by just three centimeters. The top position went to Muhammed Anees Yahiya, who managed 7.93 meters, while David P settled for bronze.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe event was held at the Kanteerava Stadium, and Sunnyâ€™s performance stood out among the nationâ€™s best jumpers. His hard work and progress over the past few years have now placed him among Indiaâ€™s rising track and field athletes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Journey Marked by Grit and Growth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEarlier this year, Sunny had already proven his potential. He earned gold at the 4th Indian Open Jumps Competition at the Anju Bobby High Performance Centre with a leap of 7.80 meters. Since then, he has continued to train in Thiruvananthapuram, improving his technique and strength.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis consistent performance is the result of long-term dedication. According to Raveendran Sankaran, Director General and CEO of the Bihar State Sports Authority (BSSA),\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œSunnyâ€™s medal is the result of three years of focused effort. His journey is an inspiration not just for Bihar, but for athletes across India.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œSunnyâ€™s medal is the result of three years of focused effort. His journey is an inspiration not just for Bihar, but for athletes across India.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach of Sunnyâ€™s six jumps on the final day tells a story of resilience:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst: 7.70 meters Second: 7.90 meters (his best) Third: Foul Fourth: 7.87 meters Fifth: 5.14 meters Sixth: No improvement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst: 7.70 meters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSecond: 7.90 meters (his best)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThird: Foul\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFourth: 7.87 meters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFifth: 5.14 meters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSixth: No improvement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlthough he didnâ€™t beat Aneesâ€”an international athlete who has competed in the Commonwealth Games and World Athletics Championshipsâ€”Sunny showed he belongs in elite competition.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA New Chapter for Biharâ€™s Sporting Dreams\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSunny Kumarâ€™s silver isnâ€™t just a personal victory. It represents a bigger moment for sports in Bihar. His progress shows whatâ€™s possible with proper training, guidance, and institutional support.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn fact, Bihar is slowly building its presence in national athletics. With facilities like the Anju Bobby High Performance Centre and guidance from bodies like BSSA, young athletes now have platforms to perform and grow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat makes Sunnyâ€™s story even more powerful is that it started far from the spotlight. His rise proves that talent from smaller towns can compete at the highest level. As more athletes follow his path, Biharâ€™s name will appear more often on the national stage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Connected with Stories That Matter\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWant to discover more stories like Sunnyâ€™s?Follow www.biharsay.com for in-depth coverage on Biharâ€™s rising talent, local changemakers, and untold progress stories.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin our 11,000+ strong global community that believes in Biharâ€™s potential.Bihar Say is not just a media platform. Itâ€™s a movement to reframe Biharâ€™s narrativeâ€”with stories that matter and voices that inspire.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can also check out BiharCast, our exclusive podcast and video series, where we dive deep into the journeys that define Bihar today.\u003c/p\u003e",
