        "title":  "Meet Bihari Visionary Who Founded The Viral Fever (TVF)",
        "summary":  "When Indiaâ€™s digital entertainment space evolved, one name quietly led the movementâ€”Arunabh Kumar, the proud Bihari founder of The Viral Fever (TVF). This feature is part of the â€œ60 Days â€“ 60 Startups from Biharâ€ series ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eWhen Indiaâ€™s digital entertainment space evolved, one name quietly led the movementâ€”Arunabh Kumar, the proud Bihari founder of The Viral Fever (TVF).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is part of the â€œ60 Days â€“ 60 Startups from Biharâ€ series by Bihar Say, celebrating homegrown visionaries who are redefining Biharâ€™s identity in the world of innovation and creativity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Muzaffarpur to Media Leadership\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArunabh Kumar was born and raised in Muzaffarpur, Bihar. He graduated from IIT Kharagpur with a degree in Electrical Engineering. While the world expected him to follow a conventional career path, Arunabh chose storytelling.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe began his creative career as an assistant director at Red Chillies Entertainment, contributing to the blockbuster film Om Shanti Om. This experience solidified his interest in content creation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat blend of technical discipline and creative energy led him to launch one of Indiaâ€™s most groundbreaking content brandsâ€”The Viral Fever.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTVF: A Pioneer in Indian Web Content\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFounded in 2010, The Viral Fever (TVF) was Indiaâ€™s first YouTube-based content studio dedicated to telling stories for and about Indian youth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnder Arunabhâ€™s leadership, TVF produced long-form, original series that quickly became cultural benchmarks. These include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKota Factory â€“ Indiaâ€™s first black-and-white web series focused on the life of IIT aspirants TVF Pitchers â€“ a trailblazing startup drama that resonated with aspiring entrepreneurs Panchayat â€“ a relatable tale of a young professional adjusting to rural India Tripling â€“ a story of sibling bonding and self-discovery Permanent Roommates â€“ one of Indiaâ€™s earliest and most-loved relationship dramas\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKota Factory â€“ Indiaâ€™s first black-and-white web series focused on the life of IIT aspirants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTVF Pitchers â€“ a trailblazing startup drama that resonated with aspiring entrepreneurs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePanchayat â€“ a relatable tale of a young professional adjusting to rural India\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTripling â€“ a story of sibling bonding and self-discovery\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePermanent Roommates â€“ one of Indiaâ€™s earliest and most-loved relationship dramas\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTVFâ€™s strength lies in its authenticity. The stories are rooted, emotionally intelligent, and reflective of real India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTVFâ€™s Reach and Impact\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs of 2025, TVF has reached significant milestones:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOver 13 million YouTube subscribers More than 1.4 billion lifetime views Panchayat Season 3 earned 28.2 million views Kota Factory Season 3 reached 15.8 million views Pitchers Season 1 Episode 1 has over 7.7 million views Permanent Roommates crossed 50 million views\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOver 13 million YouTube subscribers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore than 1.4 billion lifetime views\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePanchayat Season 3 earned 28.2 million views\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKota Factory Season 3 reached 15.8 million views\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePitchers Season 1 Episode 1 has over 7.7 million views\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePermanent Roommates crossed 50 million views\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTVF is now expanding into four Indian languages and will release 20 new web series and its first feature film in 2025. Its rise is not just a content successâ€”it is a storytelling revolution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Bihari Founder Who Redefined Digital India\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArunabh Kumarâ€™s story is proof that big ideas often come from humble beginnings. From Muzaffarpur to Mumbai, his journey reflects Biharâ€™s growing footprint in Indiaâ€™s digital and entrepreneurial space.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs the founder of TVF, Arunabh gave Indian youth a mirror, and in doing so, helped millions find their stories online. His impact on web series and digital content is profound and lasting.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e60 Days â€“ 60 Startups: A Bihar Say Initiative\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis blog is part of â€œ60 Days â€“ 60 Startups from Biharâ€ by Bihar Say, an initiative to spotlight creators, founders, and changemakers rooted in Bihar who are reshaping industries nationwide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo read more powerful founder journeys, follow www.biharsay.com and join our 12,000+ strong global community that believes in Biharâ€™s talent and future.\u003c/p\u003e",
