        "id":  "bihar-to-launch-150-new-electric-buses-by-aug-2025",
        "title":  "Bihar to launch 150 new Electric Buses by Aug 2025",
        "summary":  "à¤¸à¤«à¤° à¤¬à¤¦à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾, à¤¬à¤¿à¤¹à¤¾à¤° à¤šà¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾: 150 Electric Buses Ready to Roll Out Across Biharâ€™s Roads! Biharâ€™s Green Leap: 150 Electric Buses to Hit the Roads Soon! Imagine hopping onto a silent, zero-emissi...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eà¤¸à¤«à¤° à¤¬à¤¦à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾, à¤¬à¤¿à¤¹à¤¾à¤° à¤šà¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾: 150 Electric Buses Ready to Roll Out Across Biharâ€™s Roads!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Green Leap: 150 Electric Buses to Hit the Roads Soon!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine hopping onto a silent, zero-emission electric bus on a busy Patna morning. No diesel smoke, no engine roarâ€”just a smooth ride powered by clean energy. That future is almost here. Bihar is preparing to launch 150 brand-new electric buses across major routes in the state, setting the stage for a greener, cleaner transportation revolution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eElectric Buses in Bihar: Whatâ€™s Coming and Where?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe state government, in collaboration with the central government, has finalized plans to roll out these eco-friendly buses in phases. According to transport department sources, 80 electric buses will soon be operating within Patna city and its key areasâ€”Bailey Road, Danapur, Patna City, Phulwari AIIMS, Bihta, Maner, and Digha.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMeanwhile, 30 more buses will serve Patnaâ€™s rural blocks such as Masaurhi, Naubatpur, and Paliganj, offering reliable travel options to thousands.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe remaining 40 buses will be allocated to other major cities like Gaya, Purnia, Bhagalpur, and Muzaffarpurâ€”bringing better public transport to tier-2 cities that have long needed it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCharging Stations and Infrastructure: Ready to Power Up\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo support this transition, dedicated charging stations are being built at full speed. Two major hubs are already being developed in Phulwarisharif Transport Complex and Bairiya Bus Terminal in Patna. These will have the capacity to charge up to 30 buses simultaneously, ensuring that the service remains uninterrupted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, charging points in other cities have been identified, and installation will be completed by end of August 2025, in time for the bus rollout.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDaily Operations and Routes: What Commuters Can Expect\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuses will operate daily till 9 PM, covering both intra-city and inter-block routes. Transport officials confirm that each route will have 10 to 15 electric buses, ensuring a consistent and timely commute for citizens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, all buses will be GPS-tracked and monitored in real-time via the Transport Corporationâ€™s Control and Command Room. In case of emergencies, passengers will receive immediate assistanceâ€”a big leap in commuter safety and accountability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen Will the Buses Hit the Road?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMark your calendar. By the end of August 2025, these 150 electric buses will start rolling out one by one. This project marks a turning point in Biharâ€™s public transportation system, blending innovation with sustainability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ If youâ€™re tired of traffic, pollution, and unreliable transportâ€”this is the change youâ€™ve been waiting for. A Bihar that moves with the times, quietly and cleanly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“¢ Want more such transformative updates from Bihar?Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 11k+ strong global community!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e#BiharSay is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, spotlighting positive change in culture, business, and grassroots development.From impact podcasts (BiharCast) to in-depth stories, weâ€™re reshaping Biharâ€™s narrativeâ€”one headline at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
