        "id":  "railrestro-bihar-born-founders-revolutionize-train-food",
        "title":  "Bihar-Born Founders Who Revolutionized Train Food",
        "summary":  "â€œOne train ride. One craving. And Biharâ€™s biggest food-tech journey began.â€ Who Founded RailRestro? Meet Manish Chandra \u0026 Suman Priya In 2015, Manish Chandra and Suman Priya, a husband-wife duo from Patna, Bihar, found thems...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œOne train ride. One craving. And Biharâ€™s biggest food-tech journey began.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWho Founded RailRestro? Meet Manish Chandra \u0026 Suman Priya\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn 2015, Manish Chandra and Suman Priya, a husband-wife duo from Patna, Bihar, found themselves facing the same problem that millions of train passengers silently endureâ€”a lack of hot, hygienic food while traveling. Instead of complaining, they decided to solve the problem themselves.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat decision gave birth to RailRestro, a tech-powered food delivery startup for Indian Railways. Over time, what started as a simple solution evolved into a national movement across thousands of trains and stations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Common Struggle: A Problem Too Familiar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery Indian whoâ€™s taken a long-distance train knows the struggleâ€”meals that are cold, tasteless, or unhygienic. While pantry food is often unreliable, stepping off at stations risks missing the train.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eManish and Sumanâ€”both frequent travelersâ€”faced this every time. However, they realized that the solution wasnâ€™t to wait for change, but to create it. After several brainstorming sessions during their own travels, they envisioned a service that could connect passengers to quality restaurants near train stationsâ€”bringing food directly to their seats.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Humble Start: Tech, Tenacity \u0026 Trust\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThey officially launched RailRestro in September 2015, under their company Yescom India Softech Pvt. Ltd.. At first, the journey was anything but easy. For example, restaurant partners were hesitant, and integrating with IRCTC took effort. Nevertheless, their belief in the mission never faded.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInitially bootstrapped, the company began processing around 600 orders daily within just nine months. As they continued building trust, their network expanded rapidly, covering more trains and more stations across India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eScaling Up: From 84,000 Orders to 60 Lakh+ Meals\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith a customer-first approach, RailRestro grew fast. In their first year, they completed 84,000 orders. The next year, this rose to 4 lakh, and by 2019, they were delivering over 11 lakh meals annually.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy early 2021, despite COVID-19 setbacks, RailRestro had crossed 60 lakh+ total deliveries. Through smart tech, excellent vendor management, and constant adaptation, they reached passengers on 7000+ trains across India.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, they partnered with 2,100+ restaurants, all FSSAI-approved, ensuring high standards of hygiene and variety.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGoing Beyond Food: Building a Travel Companion\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportantly, Manish and Suman didnâ€™t stop at food. They built RailMitra, a sister platform offering live train running status, seat availability, PNR checks, and other toolsâ€”designed to simplify every step of the train journey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince network issues are common during travel, they also ensured their app and website work even in weak connectivity zones. In fact, RailRestro became one of the first to offer WhatsApp-based food ordering for travelers, making the process faster and more accessible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRooted in Bihar, Built for Bharat\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat makes this story exceptional is where it started. From the lanes of Patna to thousands of train routes, RailRestroâ€™s impact has been massive. Theyâ€™ve delivered everything from pure Jain food to south Indian dishes, north Indian thalis, Chinese combos, beverages, and even baby foodâ€”right to peopleâ€™s seats.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDespite the scale, they stayed grounded. They remained bootstrapped and focused on sustainability. As a result, they continue to grow not just as a company, but as a trusted rail-travel brand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTheir story is proof that Bihar isnâ€™t just participating in Indiaâ€™s startup storyâ€”itâ€™s shaping it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy RailRestro Matters More Than Ever\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilt on real pain points: No corporate strategyâ€”just a need every Indian could relate to Tech-driven: Seamless ordering via app, website, calls, and WhatsApp Massive menu: From Jain to regional cuisine, all approved by FSSAI National reach: Operating at over 400+ stations in 375+ cities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilt on real pain points: No corporate strategyâ€”just a need every Indian could relate to\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTech-driven: Seamless ordering via app, website, calls, and WhatsApp\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMassive menu: From Jain to regional cuisine, all approved by FSSAI\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNational reach: Operating at over 400+ stations in 375+ cities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis journey began with hunger, but runs on hustle.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRailRestro isnâ€™t just about foodâ€”itâ€™s about solving real-world problems with local insight and national ambition. It shows what happens when a simple idea meets relentless execution and rooted values.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“Œ This story is part of the â€œ60 Days â€“ 60 Startups from Biharâ€ series by Bihar Sayâ€”where we uncover the real founders, raw journeys, and rising voices of Biharâ€™s startup ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸŒ Join 12,000+ readers worldwide who believe that the next big story can come from the smallest of places.\u003c/p\u003e",
