        "title":  "BSRTC to Train 2,000 Women Drivers for Pink Bus",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Big Drive: 2,000 Women to Power the Pink Bus Fleet by August 2025! What if public transport wasnâ€™t just a way to commute, but a vehicle for change? Bihar is proving it can be. In a transformative step toward gender equ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Big Drive: 2,000 Women to Power the Pink Bus Fleet by August 2025!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat if public transport wasnâ€™t just a way to commute, but a vehicle for change? Bihar is proving it can be. In a transformative step toward gender equality and safe mobility, the Bihar State Road Transport Corporation (BSRTC) is set to train 2,000 women drivers to operate a fleet of 80 pink buses by August 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese women wonâ€™t just be driving buses. Theyâ€™ll be driving change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInside the Training Plan: Phased, Powerful, Practical\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo roll this out efficiently, BSRTC has divided the training into three structured phases. Each round will include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e500 women trained over 30 days Applicants must have a valid LMV (Light Motor Vehicle) licence Only those who demonstrate proper bus-handling skills will receive certification\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e500 women trained over 30 days\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApplicants must have a valid LMV (Light Motor Vehicle) licence\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnly those who demonstrate proper bus-handling skills will receive certification\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, these training centers must meet strict safety and hygiene standards. BSRTC has mandated the presence of:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClean, separate toilets Safe drinking water access High boundary walls for security\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClean, separate toilets\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSafe drinking water access\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHigh boundary walls for security\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearly, the state wants women to train not just with competenceâ€”but also with confidence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArrival of Pink Buses: More Than Just a Fleet\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to BSRTC Administrator Atul Kumar Verma, 80 pink buses are expected to arrive in Bihar by August-end. These will be exclusively driven by women who complete the training.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition, the Transport Department is preparing a residential training framework. To streamline execution, it is working closely with motor vehicle training centers to ensure a standard learning experience across districts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpecial Duty Officer Aruna Kumari is actively leading the coordination between training providers and the department, ensuring that timelines and quality are both met.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDistricts Already Onboard\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t a pilot project in just a few locations. Itâ€™s already spanning across districts. Training centers from these regions are participating:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePurnia Aurangabad Lakhisarai Munger Banka Gopalganj Darbhanga Siwan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePurnia\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAurangabad\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLakhisarai\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMunger\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBanka\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGopalganj\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDarbhanga\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSiwan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs more districts join, the outreach and impact of this initiative are set to expand even further.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot Just Employmentâ€”This Is Empowerment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLetâ€™s be clearâ€”this isnâ€™t just about giving jobs to women. Itâ€™s about breaking old narratives and creating visible representation in public spaces. A woman behind the wheel sends a strong message that gender roles are shifting in Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFurthermore, this initiative supports financial independence and promotes safety in public transport. Women passengers often feel unsafe during commutes. With more women drivers, the state addresses both supply-side employment and demand-side safety.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ”” Follow Biharâ€™s Journey of Change\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInspired by how Bihar is reshaping its narrative?Curious to know whatâ€™s coming next?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“² Follow www.biharsay.com for authentic, people-first stories from across the state.ðŸ“£ Be part of our 11,000+ global community who trust us for real news and uplifting updates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸŽ§ Donâ€™t forget to check out BiharCast, our podcast series that dives deep into the voices, stories, and traditions of the heartland.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“° Bihar Say is Biharâ€™s largest apolitical digital storytelling platform, giving voice to everyday changemakers, culture, and business with impact.\u003c/p\u003e",
