        "title":  "Reliance Industries to Set Up Rs 125 Cr Biogas Plant in Bihar",
        "summary":  "Reliance Powers Biharâ€™s Green Future: â‚¹125 Cr Biogas Plant to Transform Madhubaniâ€™s Rural Economy! â€œBig Money Meets Big Change in Bihar!â€ Reliance Industriesâ€™ â‚¹125 Crore Green Bet in Madhubani Will Fuel Jobs, Farmers...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eReliance Powers Biharâ€™s Green Future: â‚¹125 Cr Biogas Plant to Transform Madhubaniâ€™s Rural Economy!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œBig Money Meets Big Change in Bihar!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReliance Industriesâ€™ â‚¹125 Crore Green Bet in Madhubani Will Fuel Jobs, Farmersâ€™ Income \u0026 Biharâ€™s Biogas Dream\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a bold and inspiring move, Reliance Industries is setting the stage for one of Biharâ€™s most transformative green energy projects. A whopping â‚¹125 crore investment is powering the upcoming Compressed Biogas (CBG) plant in Madhubaniâ€™s Lohat Industrial Area, promising not just cleaner energyâ€”but a cleaner, stronger future for thousands.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreen Energy Meets Rural Empowerment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRelianceâ€™s CBG plant is not just another infrastructure project. Itâ€™s a bridge between modern clean technology and Biharâ€™s deeply rooted agricultural economy.The numbers are massiveâ€”and so is the impact:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProduction Capacity: 7,875 metric tonnes of Compressed Biogas annually By-product: 80,000 tonnes of organic fertiliser Land Area: 27.44 acres allocated by BIADA (Bihar Industrial Area Development Authority)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProduction Capacity: 7,875 metric tonnes of Compressed Biogas annually\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy-product: 80,000 tonnes of organic fertiliser\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLand Area: 27.44 acres allocated by BIADA (Bihar Industrial Area Development Authority)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore importantly, this initiative will create:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e100 direct jobs 150+ indirect jobs Additional income for local farmers through the purchase of agricultural waste\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e100 direct jobs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e150+ indirect jobs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional income for local farmers through the purchase of agricultural waste\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe plant will use agricultural residue as raw material, making it a textbook example of a circular economy model in action.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEmployment, Entrepreneurship, and Eco-Growth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndustries Minister Nitish Mishra has rightly called this a milestone for Bihar.He said,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œIt is expected to not only strengthen the rural economy but also position the state as a key player in Indiaâ€™s renewable energy transition.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œIt is expected to not only strengthen the rural economy but also position the state as a key player in Indiaâ€™s renewable energy transition.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just a plantâ€”itâ€™s a vision taking shape. One where farmers become energy providers, and Bihar becomes a national example of green industrialisation done right.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMadhubaniâ€™s Biggest Private Investment Yet\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMadhubani hasnâ€™t seen an investment of this scale before. As one of the largest private ventures in the district, this project could attract more green investments in the future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith climate goals tightening globally and India pushing hard on its renewable targets, Biharâ€”often overlookedâ€”is rising to the occasion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRelianceâ€™s presence in the heart of Mithilanchal is a vote of confidence. It shows that corporate India believes in Biharâ€™s potentialâ€”its land, its people, and its future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat This Means for Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just a win for Madhubani or Reliance. Itâ€™s a symbolic shift for Biharâ€”where progress isnâ€™t just about highways and bridges, but about sustainable models that benefit both planet and people.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt its core, this initiative aligns with everything Bihar Say stands for: celebrating real change, local resilience, and untold stories that deserve the spotlight.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ”¥ Want more stories like thisâ€”real, rooted, and refreshing?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates on Biharâ€™s industrial leaps, inspiring entrepreneurs, and cultural evolution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸŒ Join our growing global community of over 11,000 changemakers!#BiharSay is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical storytelling platform, reshaping the stateâ€™s image through powerful voices, one blog at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
