        "id":  "guru-purnima-2025-bihars-legendary-gurus-who-shaped-india",
        "title":  "Guru Purnima 2025: Biharâ€™s Legendary Gurus Who Shaped India",
        "summary":  "â€œBiharâ€™s Gurus, The Minds That Moved The Worldâ€ From Buddhaâ€™s silence to Chanakyaâ€™s strategyâ€”Biharâ€™s soil gave rise to Gurus who shaped civilizations. Why Biharâ€™s Soil Is Sacred On Guru Purnima Guru Purnima isnâ€™t...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œBiharâ€™s Gurus, The Minds That Moved The Worldâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Buddhaâ€™s silence to Chanakyaâ€™s strategyâ€”Biharâ€™s soil gave rise to Gurus who shaped civilizations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Biharâ€™s Soil Is Sacred On Guru Purnima\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGuru Purnima isnâ€™t just another date on the calendar. Itâ€™s a day when India bows to the light that dispels ignorance â€” the Guru. While the world remembers Maharshi Ved Vyasa, the land of Bihar echoes with the footsteps of spiritual titans and scholarly giants.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat makes Bihar so special on this sacred day? Itâ€™s the birthplace, workplace, and karmabhoomi of some of Indiaâ€™s most iconic Gurus â€” men of vision, character, and timeless wisdom.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGautam Buddha: The Enlightenment That Began in Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore he was called Buddha, he was Siddhartha â€” a seeker of truth. Under the Bodhi Tree in Bodh Gaya, he attained enlightenment. But what followed was even greater. He chose Guru Purnima to deliver his first sermon, making this day historically spiritual.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday, Bodh Gaya attracts seekers from across the globe. But it began with one manâ€™s silence under a tree in Bihar. His teachings on compassion, detachment, and mindfulness changed the world forever.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChanakya: The Political Sage Born to Build Empires\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMove from spirituality to strategy, and you meet Chanakya, the brilliant mind behind Indiaâ€™s first major empire. He mentored Chandragupta Maurya in Pataliputra (now Patna) and wrote the Arthashastra â€” a political playbook still relevant.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChanakya wasnâ€™t just a teacher. He was a kingmaker, a thinker, and a doer. His wisdom made Bihar not just a land of saints but also of statesmen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNagarjuna: The Philosopher Who Redefined Emptiness\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCenturies later, in the classrooms of Nalanda, walked Acharya Nagarjuna, a Buddhist philosopher who questioned everything. His concept of â€œShunyataâ€ (emptiness) challenged the most rigid minds. But more than theories, his teachings nurtured open thinking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks to Gurus like him, Biharâ€™s ancient universities became global knowledge hubs. Wisdom wasnâ€™t memorized here â€” it was debated, questioned, and reborn.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGuru Gobind Singh Ji: The Warrior Born in Patna\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn Patna Sahib, a warrior saint was born â€” Guru Gobind Singh Ji, the tenth Sikh Guru. He was only nine when he became Guru. But his courage, poetry, and vision made him eternal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom spiritual guidance to the formation of the Khalsa Panth, his legacy teaches that a Guru leads from the front â€” with a sword of justice and the heart of a poet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVed Vyasa: The Guru of All Gurus\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThough not exclusive to Bihar, Maharshi Ved Vyasaâ€™s connection with the region comes through age-old traditions. Guru Purnima is observed on his birthday because he compiled the Vedas and authored the Mahabharata â€” the foundation of Indian thought.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHis legacy is why this day is called Guru Purnima. Every Guru we celebrate stands on the shoulders of this one master.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar: The Forgotten Land of Intellectual Giants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s easy to overlook Bihar today. But in truth, this land has mentored the world. From Bodh Gaya to Nalanda, from Takshashila-trained thinkers to warrior saints, Bihar raised Gurus who gave India â€” and humanity â€” direction.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s not just history. Itâ€™s heritage. And Guru Purnima is the perfect reminder to revisit it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“£ Ready to Rediscover Bihar?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt Bihar Say, we donâ€™t just tell stories â€” we retell Biharâ€™s identity. As Indiaâ€™s leading apolitical storytelling platform, weâ€™re committed to showcasing the real Bihar â€” its changemakers, its traditions, and its wisdom.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Join us at www.biharsay.com and become part of our 11k+ strong global community.Letâ€™s reclaim Biharâ€™s legacy â€” one story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e",
