        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œHistory on Track: Patna to Host Indian Open Athletics Meet for the First Time!â€ ðŸ…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Steps Into the Big League of Indian Athletics\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œBihar ke dil mein ab sirf sapne nahi, daudte hain champions!â€For the first time in history, Patna is set to host the prestigious Indian Open Athletics Meet on July 19 â€” a monumental moment for Biharâ€™s sporting journey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore than 250 elite athletes, both men and women, from across the nation will compete at the Patliputra Sports Complex. Representing top institutions like ONGC and Indian Railways, these athletes arenâ€™t just chasing medalsâ€”theyâ€™re chasing spots in the upcoming Asian and Commonwealth Games.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not just a sporting eventâ€”itâ€™s Bihar announcing itself on the national athletics map.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat to Expect at the Meet?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe championship, organised by the Athletics Association of Bihar under the umbrella of the Athletics Federation of India (AFI), will feature a wide array of track and field events:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSprints \u0026 Relays (100m to 4x400m) Long \u0026 Middle-Distance Runs Steeplechase, Marathon, and Half Marathon High-Intensity Jumps like Long Jump, High Jump, Triple Jump, and Pole Vault Power Events including Shot Put, Discus Throw, Javelin, Hammer Throw And multi-discipline events like the Decathlon and Heptathlon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSprints \u0026 Relays (100m to 4x400m)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLong \u0026 Middle-Distance Runs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteeplechase, Marathon, and Half Marathon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHigh-Intensity Jumps like Long Jump, High Jump, Triple Jump, and Pole Vault\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePower Events including Shot Put, Discus Throw, Javelin, Hammer Throw\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd multi-discipline events like the Decathlon and Heptathlon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery stride, jump, and throw will count â€” not just for medals, but as a ticket to international games.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Sports Authority Sounds the Bugle\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Ravindran Shankar (IPS), DG of Bihar State Sports Authority, this championship will act as a qualifier for selecting athletes for prestigious international events like the Asian Games and the Commonwealth Games.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just good news for athletesâ€”itâ€™s a game-changer for sports lovers, budding talents, and youth from Bihar.This is the first step towards building Bihar as a national sports hub.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePowerlifting Glory: Patna Boy Lifts Biharâ€™s Name in Japan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn another proud moment for Bihar, Amit Kishan of Patna clinched Gold in the Asian-African Pacific Powerlifting and Bench Press Championship in Japan.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHe made headlines by lifting 182.5kg in the 120+kg weight category bench press, proving that Biharâ€™s strength is felt globally. Earlier this year, he had secured a silver medal at the Senior National Championship in Punjab.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmitâ€™s story reflects the rise of new icons from Bihar who are making India proud on the world stage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatnaâ€™s inclusion in the Indian athletics calendar is not a small winâ€”itâ€™s a massive milestone. It signifies Biharâ€™s growing stature in the world of sports infrastructure, event management, and athlete development.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, events like these inspire a new generation of runners, jumpers, lifters, and dreamers from every corner of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGet Real-Time Updates on Biharâ€™s Sporting Revolution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Stay ahead with regular updates, athlete stories, and exclusive event coverage only on www.biharsay.com.Become a part of our 11,000+ global community that celebrates Biharâ€™s transformation.ðŸ“² Bihar Say isnâ€™t just newsâ€”itâ€™s the voice of a new Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
