        "title":  "Bihar Becomes Fastest-Growing State in Stock Market Investors | NSE Report 2025",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Equity Revolution: Fastest Investor Growth in India, Ahead of Delhi \u0026 Punjab â€œBiharâ€™s rise in the Indian stock market is not just surprisingâ€”itâ€™s historic.â€ In a striking shift, Bihar has emerged as the fastest...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Equity Revolution: Fastest Investor Growth in India, Ahead of Delhi \u0026 Punjab\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œBiharâ€™s rise in the Indian stock market is not just surprisingâ€”itâ€™s historic.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a striking shift, Bihar has emerged as the fastest-growing state in India in terms of equity investors, according to a recent report by Business Standard, based on data from the National Stock Exchange (NSE).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBetween FY 2019-20 and May 2025, the number of investors from Bihar jumped from 700,000 to 5.2 millionâ€”a staggering growth of 678.8%. This surge places Bihar in the top 10 states in India with the highest number of registered equity investors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis growth isnâ€™t just impressiveâ€”itâ€™s unmatched by any other Indian state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“ˆ A CAGR of 48.8%: Bihar Beats Expectations\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe data reveals that Bihar clocked a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 48.8% during this five-year period.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn comparison, states like Delhi (3â€“4 million investors) and Punjab (around 3.5 million) lag behind Bihar in terms of overall growth and adoption. Maharashtra continues to hold the highest number of stock investors in India at 1.9 crore, followed by Uttar Pradesh (1.31 crore) and Gujarat (1 crore). Still, no state has witnessed growth at Biharâ€™s pace.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn comparison, states like Delhi (3â€“4 million investors) and Punjab (around 3.5 million) lag behind Bihar in terms of overall growth and adoption.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaharashtra continues to hold the highest number of stock investors in India at 1.9 crore, followed by Uttar Pradesh (1.31 crore) and Gujarat (1 crore).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStill, no state has witnessed growth at Biharâ€™s pace.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is particularly noteworthy because Bihar also has Indiaâ€™s lowest per capita income, just above â‚¹60,000 in FY24. In contrast:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDelhi: â‚¹4.6 lakh Haryana: â‚¹7.3 lakh Punjab: â‚¹1.95 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDelhi: â‚¹4.6 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHaryana: â‚¹7.3 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePunjab: â‚¹1.95 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDespite this economic disadvantage, Bihar has shown extraordinary participation in the capital markets.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEquity Over Debt: A Bold Risk Appetite\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is also demonstrating a higher risk-taking appetite than many industrialised states.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to the Association of Mutual Funds in India (AMFI):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e89% of Biharâ€™s mutual fund assets are invested in equity schemes. This surpasses: Jharkhand (87%) Chhattisgarh (86%) Uttar Pradesh (83%)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e89% of Biharâ€™s mutual fund assets are invested in equity schemes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis surpasses:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJharkhand (87%) Chhattisgarh (86%) Uttar Pradesh (83%)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJharkhand (87%)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChhattisgarh (86%)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUttar Pradesh (83%)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn comparison, more developed states prefer debt-oriented schemes, indicating a conservative approach. Biharâ€™s investors are flipping the script.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBehind the Numbers: The Face of Biharâ€™s Financial Shift\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTake the story of Akshay Kumar, a young resident of Bhojpur, Bihar. During the COVID-19 pandemic, he left a secure government job to run a Motilal Oswal Financial Services franchise.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHis bold decision has paid off. His trading volumes have grown 10x in less than four years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHis bold decision has paid off.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHis trading volumes have grown 10x in less than four years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAkshayâ€™s journey mirrors the larger shift happening across Biharâ€”young investors are turning to markets not just for income but for long-term wealth creation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Fueling This Growth?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSeveral trends explain Biharâ€™s rise:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMobile penetration in rural areas has increased significantly. Low-cost trading platforms like Zerodha, Upstox, and Groww have removed access barriers. Educational content on YouTube and social media has helped bridge knowledge gaps. Aspirational youth, even in Tier 2 and 3 towns, are now engaging with financial markets daily.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMobile penetration in rural areas has increased significantly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLow-cost trading platforms like Zerodha, Upstox, and Groww have removed access barriers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEducational content on YouTube and social media has helped bridge knowledge gaps.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAspirational youth, even in Tier 2 and 3 towns, are now engaging with financial markets daily.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost importantly, this change is organicâ€”driven by individuals, not government schemes or subsidies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters for India\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s financial awakening tells a larger story: Indiaâ€™s financial inclusion is deepening beyond metros and rich states.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt signals a maturing investment ecosystem. It highlights the power of digital platforms in democratising finance. It challenges the assumption that only high-income regions invest.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt signals a maturing investment ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt highlights the power of digital platforms in democratising finance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt challenges the assumption that only high-income regions invest.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s stock market journey is not an outlierâ€”it may be the beginning of a national trend.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâœ… Stay Updated with Biharâ€™s Growth Stories\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is changing. From infrastructure to entrepreneurship and now financial marketsâ€”the state is evolving quietly but rapidly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ For more verified, data-backed stories on Biharâ€™s rise, follow www.biharsay.comâ€”Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBe part of our growing 12,000+ global community that believes in the power of Biharâ€™s potential. From grassroots change to financial revolutions, Bihar Say brings you stories that matter.\u003c/p\u003e",
