        "title":  "Biharâ€™s 2 New Railway Lines Announced :161 KM Track, 14 Stations, 72 Underpasses",
        "summary":  "â€œà¤°à¥‡à¤² à¤µà¤¿à¤•à¤¾à¤¸ à¤¸à¥‡ à¤¬à¤¦à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾ à¤¦à¤°à¤­à¤‚à¤—à¤¾ à¤•à¤¾ à¤¨à¤œà¤¼à¤¾à¤°à¤¾! 15 Bridges, 72 Underpasses, and 2 New Rail Lines Set to Transform Biharâ€™s Connectivityâ€ â€œNot just tracks, itâ€™s Biharâ€™s ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œà¤°à¥‡à¤² à¤µà¤¿à¤•à¤¾à¤¸ à¤¸à¥‡ à¤¬à¤¦à¤²à¥‡à¤—à¤¾ à¤¦à¤°à¤­à¤‚à¤—à¤¾ à¤•à¤¾ à¤¨à¤œà¤¼à¤¾à¤°à¤¾! 15 Bridges, 72 Underpasses, and 2 New Rail Lines Set to Transform Biharâ€™s Connectivityâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œNot just tracks, itâ€™s Biharâ€™s track to transformation!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is racing ahead on the railway map of India, and the spotlight is on Darbhanga. With a massive infrastructure upgrade announced during Union Railway Ministerâ€˜s recent visit, the region is set to witness a historic makeover. The blessing comes in the form of two brand-new railway lines, 14 upcoming stations, 15 major bridges, and 72 underpasses, reshaping the travel narrative in North Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Coming? Two New Railway Lines Totalling 161 KM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Central Government has greenlit two much-needed railway lines:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaheriasarai to Saharsa â€“ 95 KM Laheriasarai to Muzaffarpur â€“ 66 KM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaheriasarai to Saharsa â€“ 95 KM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaheriasarai to Muzaffarpur â€“ 66 KM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTogether, these lines span 161 kilometers, bridging critical districts and enhancing regional mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaheriasaraiâ€“Saharsa Line: Game-Changer for Kosi Region\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis â‚¹2,376 crore project will cover 95 KM, out of which 70 KM lies within Darbhanga Parliamentary Constituency.Key Infrastructure on This Line:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e15 large bridges over the Kosi River 41 small bridges 72 underpasses 10 new railway stations\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e15 large bridges over the Kosi River\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e41 small bridges\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e72 underpasses\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e10 new railway stations\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis massive connectivity push is set to energize rural Bihar, linking agricultural zones with urban demand centers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaheriasaraiâ€“Muzaffarpur Line: Easing Urban \u0026 Healthcare Access\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe second proposed railway line of 66 KM will be developed at a cost of â‚¹1,213 crore.Highlights:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4 new stations, including one next to the upcoming AIIMS Darbhanga 3 halt points for better last-mile connectivity\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e4 new stations, including one next to the upcoming AIIMS Darbhanga\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e3 halt points for better last-mile connectivity\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis means easier access for people from Araria, Kishanganj, Purnia, and Katihar, especially for those needing treatment at AIIMS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOverbridge for Faster Daily Travel\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApart from long-distance development, Darbhangaâ€™s urban infrastructure gets a boost with a new â‚¹6.16 crore overbridge in Laheriasarai. This will significantly reduce travel time between Laheriasarai to Benipur and Kusheshwarsthan, especially for two-wheeler commuters.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo New Train Services Announced\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo make the region even more connected, Railway Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw announced:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Darbhangaâ€“Lucknow express An extended Amrit Bharat train from Amritsar to Saharsa via Darbhanga\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Darbhangaâ€“Lucknow express\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn extended Amrit Bharat train from Amritsar to Saharsa via Darbhanga\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese additions ensure better inter-state mobility and more economic opportunities for locals.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Demands to Deliveries\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal railway officials had placed the demand for these lines during a special meeting at the Samastipur Railway Division Office. Within a short span, the proposal received active approvalâ€”highlighting the governmentâ€™s commitment to boosting connectivity in underserved regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Growth is on Track\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isnâ€™t just railway development. Itâ€™s Biharâ€™s leap toward better infrastructure, healthcare access, regional balance, and economic revival. By bridging remote areas, Biharâ€™s rail blueprint is making sure no one is left behind.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“¢ Want to stay updated with Biharâ€™s transformation?ðŸ‘‰ Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates.Join the 11K+ strong community worldwide thatâ€™s reshaping Biharâ€™s digital identityâ€”one story at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media \u0026 storytelling platform, spotlighting real changeâ€”from traditions to transformations, from local heroes to national headlines.\u003c/p\u003e",
