        "id":  "bihar-govt-sanctions-over-rs-3000-crore-for-universities-and-colleges-covers-salaries-pensions-and-welfare-benefits",
        "title":  "Bihar Govt Sanctions â‚¹3,026 Crore for Universities and Colleges",
        "summary":  "â€œâ‚¹3,000 Crore Power Boost for Bihar Universities: Govt Shows Itâ€™s Not Just About Infrastructure, Itâ€™s About People!â€ Bihar Delivers a Bold Statement: â‚¹3,026 Crore for Education Workforce â€œSirf budget nahi, bharosa mi...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œâ‚¹3,000 Crore Power Boost for Bihar Universities: Govt Shows Itâ€™s Not Just About Infrastructure, Itâ€™s About People!â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Delivers a Bold Statement: â‚¹3,026 Crore for Education Workforce\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œSirf budget nahi, bharosa mila hai!â€The Bihar government has done more than just allocate funds â€” it has delivered a powerful message. Teachers and staff across the stateâ€™s higher education institutions now have something solid to lean on: a â‚¹3,026.219 crore grant-in-aid for the financial year 2025â€“26.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis grant isnâ€™t just about numbers. Itâ€™s about valuing the people who educate, manage, and build the future. Deputy Chief Minister Samrat Chaudhary announced the fund to support universities, aided colleges, and minority educational institutions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere the Money Goes â€” And Why It Matters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLetâ€™s break it down.Of the total amount:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ’¼ â‚¹1,385.769 crore goes toward salaries ðŸ¥ â‚¹1,640.45 crore covers non-salary needs â€” pensions, gratuity, leave encashment, medical support\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ’¼ â‚¹1,385.769 crore goes toward salaries\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ¥ â‚¹1,640.45 crore covers non-salary needs â€” pensions, gratuity, leave encashment, medical support\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis allocation supports both serving and retired staff â€” from professors to non-teaching personnel. Most importantly, the payout spans from June 2025 to February 2026.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut thereâ€™s a catch. Institutions must utilise funds within a month and submit a utilisation certificate. Delays beyond three months? The unspent money goes back to the treasury.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis tight deadline ensures the funds serve their true purpose: timely financial support to those whoâ€™ve dedicated their lives to education.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePeople First: The Shift Bihar Was Waiting For\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpeaking on the development, Samrat Chaudhary called it a step forward for employee welfare and institutional stability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œThe government is equally focused on strengthening higher education infrastructure and safeguarding the interests of employees.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œThe government is equally focused on strengthening higher education infrastructure and safeguarding the interests of employees.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThatâ€™s a refreshing tone â€” and one that Biharâ€™s education community has long waited to hear.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy prioritizing welfare, the state is building trust. When salaries are consistent and pensions are secure, performance follows. More than anything, this move gives dignity to educators, especially those whoâ€™ve retired and await their dues.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpotlight: Dr. Rajendra Prasad Central Agricultural University\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne standout example is the Dr. Rajendra Prasad Central Agricultural University, Pusa, Samastipur. The university has received a dedicated â‚¹55 crore package.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis amount focuses entirely on:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearing pending pensions Providing gratuity and benefits Offering timely financial relief to retired staff\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClearing pending pensions\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProviding gratuity and benefits\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOffering timely financial relief to retired staff\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAuthorities have instructed the university to spend the funds immediately and ensure proper documentation. This focused allocation shows that Bihar is finally acknowledging the long-pending gaps in employee welfare.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s More Than a Policy â€” Itâ€™s a Promise\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis grant-in-aid isnâ€™t just a one-time gesture. It reflects a larger shift in governance â€” one that listens, acts, and delivers. For too long, higher education staff faced uncertainty around payments. Now, with this allocation, they see a future backed by financial stability and government accountability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is rewriting the story. From grassroots education to top universities, from young aspirants to retired professors â€” everyone is part of this change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ”¥ This is the Bihar you didnâ€™t hear about on national headlines.Want more such updates, insights, and local power stories?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ“² Follow www.biharsay.comBe part of our 11K+ global community thatâ€™s changing how the world sees Bihar.Weâ€™re not just news. Weâ€™re the digital voice of Bihar â€” through stories, impact, and untold journeys.\u003c/p\u003e",
