        "title":  "RPCAU Develops 3 New Maize Varieties to Boost Bihar Agriculture \u0026 Nutrition",
        "summary":  "â€œMaize Miracle in Bihar! RPCAU Launches 3 Game-Changing Varieties for Farmers, Nutrition \u0026 Marketsâ€ Biharâ€™s Maize Revolution Begins at Dholi Bihar is sowing the seeds of an agricultural revolution â€” and it starts with thre...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eâ€œMaize Miracle in Bihar! RPCAU Launches 3 Game-Changing Varieties for Farmers, Nutrition \u0026 Marketsâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Maize Revolution Begins at Dholi\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is sowing the seeds of an agricultural revolution â€” and it starts with three remarkable maize varieties tailored just for its land, climate, and people.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a breakthrough for eastern Indiaâ€™s farming sector, Rajendra Prasad Central Agricultural University (RPCAU) has unveiled three innovative maize hybrids that are set to reshape farming income, nutrition, and agri-business in Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese varietiesâ€”Rajendra Baby Corn-1, Rajendra Pop Corn-1, and Shaktiman-5â€”are not just new crops. They are tools of transformation for small and marginal farmers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRajendra Baby Corn-1: Quick Income, Dual Purpose\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeveloped by the maize breeding team at Tirhut College of Agriculture (TCA), Dholi, Rajendra Baby Corn-1 is Biharâ€™s first region-specific baby corn hybrid. It matures in just two months, giving farmers a fast turnaround crop with 12â€“15 quintals per hectare of fresh baby corn.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut thereâ€™s moreâ€”this hybrid also yields up to 300 quintals per hectare of green fodder, making it a dual-purpose boon for farmers with livestock.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œBaby corn has a strong demand in cities and food industries, but Bihar lacked a variety that fits our unique climate. This hybrid fills that gap,â€ said Ajay Kumar, maize scientist at RPCAU.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œBaby corn has a strong demand in cities and food industries, but Bihar lacked a variety that fits our unique climate. This hybrid fills that gap,â€ said Ajay Kumar, maize scientist at RPCAU.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith rapid growth and urban demand, this variety is a clear win for farmers seeking both speed and sustainability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRajendra Pop Corn-1: From Fields to Packaged Snacks\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePopcorn is no longer just a cinema treatâ€”itâ€™s a booming snack industry, and RPCAU wants Biharâ€™s farmers to get their slice of the pie.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRajendra Pop Corn-1, specially tailored for Biharâ€™s agro-climatic zones, matures in just 80â€“90 days. It thrives in both Rabi and late Kharif seasons, delivering 30â€“40 quintals per hectare.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIts secret weapon? A popping ratio of 34â€“36 cc/g and 95% popping success, producing premium butterfly-type flakes loved by snack brands.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor farmers, this means not just yield, but market-ready quality.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShaktiman-5: Feeding Futures with Biofortified Protein\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore than a crop, Shaktiman-5 is a nutritional intervention. This biofortified Quality Protein Maize (QPM) is rich in lysine and tryptophanâ€”two essential amino acids missing in most cereals.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy does it matter? Because protein deficiency still affects large rural populations, especially children. Shaktiman-5 aligns with national goals like Poshan Abhiyaan, the National Biofortification Mission, and even strengthens food schemes like mid-day meals and anganwadi nutrition.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œThis variety isnâ€™t just for fieldsâ€”itâ€™s for kitchens, schools, and hospitals,â€ noted RPCAU Vice-Chancellor P.S. Pandey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œThis variety isnâ€™t just for fieldsâ€”itâ€™s for kitchens, schools, and hospitals,â€ noted RPCAU Vice-Chancellor P.S. Pandey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom better child development to improved livestock feed, this variety offers high returns with high impact.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy It Matters for Bihar Farmers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese three maize varieties offer:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHigher returns in shorter durations Suitability for Biharâ€™s climate Nutrition-led innovation Dual-use crops for income + fodder Strong urban and industry demand\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHigher returns in shorter durations\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSuitability for Biharâ€™s climate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNutrition-led innovation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDual-use crops for income + fodder\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStrong urban and industry demand\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThey also support crop diversification, resilient farming, and agri-entrepreneurship, essential for doubling farm incomes and empowering rural Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s Next?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRPCAU has shown the way. Now itâ€™s time for farmers, policymakers, and agri-entrepreneurs to act. Whether youâ€™re looking to improve farm economics, food security, or agro-industrial linkages, these three maize hybrids are your starting point.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want more such exclusive updates from Biharâ€™s fields, labs, and changemakers?Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 11k+ strong global community.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar Say is your leading apolitical platform reshaping Biharâ€™s image through culture, business, and grassroots stories.From podcasting with innovators to spotlighting unsung heroes, weâ€™re telling real stories that matter.\u003c/p\u003e",
