        "id":  "75-subsidy-on-vegetable-seeds-plants-under-bihars-new-scheme",
        "title":  "75% Subsidy on Vegetable Seeds \u0026 Plants Under Biharâ€™s New Scheme",
        "summary":  "à¤•à¤¿à¤¸à¤¾à¤¨à¥‹à¤‚ à¤•à¥‡ à¤šà¥‡à¤¹à¤°à¥‡ à¤ªà¤° à¤®à¥à¤¸à¥à¤•à¤¾à¤¨! | 75% Subsidy on Vegetable Seeds \u0026 Plants Under Biharâ€™s New Scheme Biharâ€™s Vegetable Revolution: 75% Subsidy Sparks Hope for Farmers in 2025-26 A 3-rup...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eà¤•à¤¿à¤¸à¤¾à¤¨à¥‹à¤‚ à¤•à¥‡ à¤šà¥‡à¤¹à¤°à¥‡ à¤ªà¤° à¤®à¥à¤¸à¥à¤•à¤¾à¤¨! | 75% Subsidy on Vegetable Seeds \u0026 Plants Under Biharâ€™s New Scheme\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Vegetable Revolution: 75% Subsidy Sparks Hope for Farmers in 2025-26\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA 3-rupee plant can now change a farmerâ€™s life.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThatâ€™s not just a lineâ€”itâ€™s a real shift taking place in Bhabhua, Bihar. The Horticulture Department has launched a powerful new initiative under the Vegetable Development Scheme (à¤¸à¤¬à¥à¤œà¥€ à¤µà¤¿à¤•à¤¾à¤¸ à¤¯à¥‹à¤œà¤¨à¤¾). With a massive 75% subsidy on hybrid vegetable seeds and plants, farmers can now grow more, spend less, and earn betterâ€”all within this crop cycle.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhatâ€™s the Scheme Offering?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the financial year 2025â€“26, Biharâ€™s horticulture department is focusing on Rabi and summer vegetable cultivation. The goal is to improve agricultural productivity and increase farmer income by lowering seed input costs and encouraging high-yield hybrid crops.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKey highlights of the scheme:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSubsidy: 75% on hybrid seeds and saplings Per-plant subsidy: â‚¹2.25 on a unit cost of â‚¹3 Minimum land area eligible: 25 dismil (approx. 0.25 acre) Maximum land area covered: 1 hectare per farmer Mode of application: Online (link below)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSubsidy: 75% on hybrid seeds and saplings\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePer-plant subsidy: â‚¹2.25 on a unit cost of â‚¹3\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMinimum land area eligible: 25 dismil (approx. 0.25 acre)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMaximum land area covered: 1 hectare per farmer\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMode of application: Online (link below)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCrops Covered and Distribution Targets\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Dr. Abhay Kumar Gaurav, District Horticulture Officer, the scheme aims to distribute the following hybrid saplings:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e12,000 Broccoli plants 12,000 Shimla Mirch (Capsicum) plants 8,000 Tomato plants 12,000 Cauliflower plants 12,000 Cabbage plants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e12,000 Broccoli plants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e12,000 Shimla Mirch (Capsicum) plants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e8,000 Tomato plants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e12,000 Cauliflower plants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e12,000 Cabbage plants\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to this, cultivation across 20 hectares has been planned for green peas, carrots, and brinjals. Meanwhile, crops like pumpkin, ridge gourd, and bitter gourd will be grown on 35 hectares.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach eligible farmer will receive between 1,000 to 10,000 hybrid saplings, depending on land size and crop selection.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow Farmers Can Apply Online\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo avail the scheme benefits, farmers must submit their application online through the official portal of Biharâ€™s Horticulture Department.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApply here: horticulture.bihar.gov.in Required documents include land proof, Aadhaar card, and bank details. Applications are processed based on landholding and crop preference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApply here: horticulture.bihar.gov.in\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRequired documents include land proof, Aadhaar card, and bank details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApplications are processed based on landholding and crop preference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis scheme is first-come, first-servedâ€”so act quickly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Scheme Is a Game Changer\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHistorically, small and marginal farmers in Bihar have faced steep costs when purchasing quality seeds. This scheme not only eases the financial burden but also brings technology-driven farming inputs like hybrid seeds into the mainstream.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy expanding the area under cultivation and focusing on income-oriented crops, the program aims to lift thousands of families out of poverty through structured support.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItâ€™s more than a subsidyâ€”itâ€™s a strategy for economic self-reliance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDonâ€™t miss this opportunity to grow smarter and earn more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo stay informed about more such updates that truly matter, follow www.biharsay.com â€” Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform with a global community of over 11,000 followers. From grassroots success stories to deep insights on policy and culture, Bihar Say is reshaping the stateâ€™s narrative.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin us today and be part of the real stories changing Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
