        "title":  "Litchi-Pattern Sarees in High Demand, Orders Coming from India and Abroad",
        "summary":  "From Muzaffarpur to the World: Women Turning Litchi Designs into a Global Fashion Statement Muzaffarpurâ€™s Women Weaving Litchi Dreams into Global Fashion Muzaffarpur â€” the land of the world-famous Shahi Litchi â€” is now givin...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eFrom Muzaffarpur to the World: Women Turning Litchi Designs into a Global Fashion Statement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpurâ€™s Women Weaving Litchi Dreams into Global Fashion\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMuzaffarpur â€” the land of the world-famous Shahi Litchi â€” is now giving birth to a new wave of cultural pride and economic growth. In bustling city lanes and nearby villages, women are hand-painting vibrant litchi designs on sarees, clothes, purses, bedsheets, and even umbrellas. Their artistry is so unique that orders are now pouring in from across India and even from Australia, Canada, and the UK.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Birth of â€œLitchipuramâ€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe movement, known as Litchipuram, began with a mission â€” to blend art, livelihood, and environmental awareness. It started on 3rd June, with a symbolic offering of a litchi bouquet to Baba Garibnath. Since then, it has grown into a livelihood revolution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnvironmental activist Suresh Gupta explains, â€œThis campaign is preserving litchi trees, promoting a clean environment, and giving women sustainable income.â€\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMeet the Women Behind the Designs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese women are not just artists; they are entrepreneurs rewriting Biharâ€™s economic story.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNeetu Tulsyan (Saraiyaganj) â€” Founder of â€˜Gyandeep,â€™ she offers free education to over 100 girls. Her litchi sarees and bedsheets are in demand from Australia, Canada, and the UK, earning her over â‚¹1 lakh a month. Shweta Srivastava (Balughat) â€” Creates litchi-themed purses, diaries, curtains, sarees, and bedsheets. Her products have steady buyers in Delhi and Lucknow, bringing in â‚¹25,000+ every month. Ranjana Jha (Sherpur) â€” Known for her stunning litchi designs on traditional â€œPagâ€ headgear and chadars. Her work adds cultural depth while bringing strong income.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNeetu Tulsyan (Saraiyaganj) â€” Founder of â€˜Gyandeep,â€™ she offers free education to over 100 girls. Her litchi sarees and bedsheets are in demand from Australia, Canada, and the UK, earning her over â‚¹1 lakh a month.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShweta Srivastava (Balughat) â€” Creates litchi-themed purses, diaries, curtains, sarees, and bedsheets. Her products have steady buyers in Delhi and Lucknow, bringing in â‚¹25,000+ every month.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRanjana Jha (Sherpur) â€” Known for her stunning litchi designs on traditional â€œPagâ€ headgear and chadars. Her work adds cultural depth while bringing strong income.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Local Streets to Global Orders\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe products have already become household favourites in Muzaffarpur and are spreading across Biharâ€™s districts. Cities like Mumbai, Hyderabad, Bengaluru are new markets, while global interest continues to rise.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe impact is undeniable â€” many women now earn between â‚¹25,000 and â‚¹1.5 lakh per month. With government support, the artists believe these designs could become a global brand representing Biharâ€™s craft excellence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Itâ€™s More Than Just Fashion\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis initiative isnâ€™t only about income. Itâ€™s about empowerment, preserving litchi heritage, and inspiring rural creativity. Plans are underway to expand the campaign by providing design and hand-painting training in more villages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlongside art, the movement features poems, songs, and cultural programs dedicated to the litchi â€” keeping the tradition alive for future generations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo read more inspiring stories from Biharâ€™s heartlands and join our growing 12,000+ community worldwide, follow www.biharsay.com â€” Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform.\u003c/p\u003e",
