        "id":  "patna-unites-in-pride-79-metre-tricolour-march-lights-up-ganga-path-this-independence-day",
        "title":  "Patna Unites in Pride: 79-Metre Tricolour March Lights Up Ganga Path This Independence Day",
        "summary":  "Patnaâ€™s Heart Beats in Tricolor: 79-Metre Flag March Transforms Ganga Path This Independence Day A Morning That Radiated Patriotism Patna came alive on the morning of August 14, 2025. The cityâ€™s pulse matched the vibrant hues ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatnaâ€™s Heart Beats in Tricolor: 79-Metre Flag March Transforms Ganga Path This Independence Day\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Morning That Radiated Patriotism\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePatna came alive on the morning of August 14, 2025. The cityâ€™s pulse matched the vibrant hues of a 79-metre tricolor, proudly carried along Ganga Path by hundreds of students. The air buzzed with excitement, and smiles bloomed everywhere. Radio City orchestrated this event, turning a familiar route into a runway of national pride.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFreedom Fighters Breathed Life Through Youth\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStudents didnâ€™t just marchâ€”they became our freedom heroes. Rani Lakshmibai, Babu Kunwar Singh, Bhagat Singh, Chandrashekhar Azad, Rajguru, Sukhdev, and Mahatma Gandhi came alive in costume and conviction. Together, they honored Patnaâ€™s seven local martyrs, and you could feel the legacy stirring in the crowdâ€™s cheers. Their reenactment was more than a tableauâ€”it was a moment of collective memory, and a heartfelt tribute.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Pledge for Health and Progress\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen came something deeper. Dr. Sujata Mukherjee, Director at Geetanjali Patho Lab, called for more than patriotismâ€”she urged action. She led an oath to promote cervical vaccination and rallied listeners toward a shared vision: a developed India by 2027. This moment wasnâ€™t just spokenâ€”it resonated. ISM Patnaâ€™s street play added a layer of social conscience to the celebration. Their performance reminded everyone that independence is also about caring for each other.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSchools Weaving History into Reality\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery school contributed its unique thread to the tapestry. B.D. Public School paid homage to Patnaâ€™s martyrs. Patna Central School brought Babu Kunwar Singhâ€™s rebellion to life. The International Scholars School and others recreated the Dandi March with such clarity, you could feel the salt dust under your feet. These scenes werenâ€™t just performances; they were heartfelt lessons in resilience and remembrance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEmbracing Tradition, Energising Tomorrow\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis celebration wasnâ€™t just about the past. It resonated with the vibrancy found in human-centric storytellingâ€”like blogs youâ€™d find on Medium, where personal reflections and cultural context mingle freely It mirrored the warm school community narratives that transform history into lived experienceâ€”like in stories where children recite poems about freedom, and their smiles make history tangible. For many attending, this wasnâ€™t just Independence Dayâ€”it was an invitation to reflect, to act, and to belong.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Stay connected with www.biharsay.com for regular updatesâ€”and become part of our growing 12k-strong global community! Bihar Say is Biharâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling hub. Weâ€™re reshaping Biharâ€™s image with impactful stories on culture, business, and grassroots change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith more than 12,000 followers, top LinkedIn engagement for Bihar-focused content, and partnerships with platforms like DailyHunt, Bihar Say is the digital voice of the state. Our podcast and video seriesâ€”BiharCastâ€”delve deep into untold stories, spotlight changemakers, traditions, and rising voices from the heart of Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
