        "title":  "Bihar Energy Secretary Reviews Gaya-Punpun Transmission Projects",
        "summary":  "A Strong Push for Reliable Power â€œUninterrupted electricity is not a luxury, it is a necessity.â€ With these words, Biharâ€™s Energy Secretary Manoj Kumar Singh set the tone at a high-level review meeting in Patna. The meeting ...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA Strong Push for Reliable Power\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œUninterrupted electricity is not a luxury, it is a necessity.â€ With these words, Biharâ€™s Energy Secretary Manoj Kumar Singh set the tone at a high-level review meeting in Patna. The meeting focused on the Gaya-Punpun transmission projects, critical to ensuring steady power supply during peak demand and major events.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSingh directed officials to prepare an annual preventive maintenance roster for all equipment and grid substations. He emphasised that strict compliance with Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) will not only strengthen infrastructure but also improve service reliability for lakhs of households.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePreparing Ahead of Pitru Paksha Mela\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe directions carry extra urgency this year. The famous Pitru Paksha Mela in Gaya begins on September 6, attracting thousands of visitors. Singh instructed field engineers and officers to maintain transmission structures and carefully assess grid load flow. This step will guarantee continuous electricity in Gaya and Punpun during the spiritual gathering.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt the meeting, senior officers, Rahul Kumar (MD of the Transmission Company), and field engineers discussed ground realities. Singh reminded them that timely action today prevents power failures tomorrow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoint Efforts for Stronger Infrastructure\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOfficials stressed that distribution and transmission companies must not work in silos. They were directed to conduct joint inspections of power substations and transmission lines. Teams must evaluate conditions, identify weaknesses, and act quickly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, Singh highlighted the need for adequate staffing at all grids and substations. Proper manpower ensures fast responses to technical issues and avoids prolonged outages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLooking Beyond: Industry and Future Demand\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar is growing, and so is its energy demand. Singh urged Transmission Company officers to coordinate with the Industry Department and BIADA. By tracking upcoming industrial clusters, planners can design grids that support factories, jobs, and urban expansion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis forward-looking strategy shows how energy planning is tied to Biharâ€™s broader development. Reliable electricity doesnâ€™t just light homesâ€”it fuels industries, supports education, and powers digital progress.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want more such powerful updates from Biharâ€™s development frontlines? Follow www.biharsay.com and become part of our 12k+ worldwide community. Bihar Say is the stateâ€™s leading apolitical media and storytelling platform, reshaping Biharâ€™s image through stories on culture, business, and grassroots change. Join us and discover untold stories through our flagship BiharCast podcast and video series.\u003c/p\u003e",
