        "id":  "bihar-govt-to-provide-free-rooftop-solar-panels-to-58-89-lakh-families",
        "title":  "Bihar Govt to Provide Free Rooftop Solar Panels to 58.89 Lakh Families",
        "summary":  "Patna, August 16, 2025 â€“ Imagine a Bihar where every low-income home runs on clean, free energy from the sun. That dream is turning into reality, as the state government launches one of Indiaâ€™s largest green energy missionsâ€”...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003ePatna, August 16, 2025 â€“ Imagine a Bihar where every low-income home runs on clean, free energy from the sun. That dream is turning into reality, as the state government launches one of Indiaâ€™s largest green energy missionsâ€”free rooftop solar panels for 58.89 lakh Kutir Jyoti (BPL) households.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Landmark Step Toward Green Energy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Bihar government has taken a bold leap to make renewable energy a household reality. Under this initiative, every Kutir Jyoti family will receive a 1.1 KW rooftop solar panelâ€”absolutely free.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnergy Department Secretary and BSPHCL CMD Manoj Kumar Singh explained that the government has designed the scheme under the PM Surya Ghar Yojana. The central government will contribute â‚¹33,000, while the state will provide â‚¹27,000, covering the full cost of each installation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe projectâ€™s total budget stands at â‚¹16,000 crore. The state plans to meet this target within two years by using existing subsidy allocations, ensuring no extra financial burden.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExtending Support Beyond BPL Families\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe scheme is not just for Kutir Jyoti consumers. The state will also provide financial assistance to 1.30 crore domestic consumers who wish to install solar panels. This wider support ensures more households shift from traditional electricity to renewable power.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Energy Minister Bijendra Prasad Yadav, Bihar aims to cut dependence on conventional power sources and accelerate renewable adoption. The goal is clear: reduce bills, boost sustainability, and empower citizens with clean energy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Vision Backed by Leadership\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDuring a virtual outreach, Chief Minister Nitish Kumar reaffirmed the stateâ€™s commitment to solar energy. He reminded citizens that all government buildings already run on solar power.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe current plan takes inspiration from the Jal-Jeevan-Hariyali Mission, under which more than 12,000 government installations in Bihar have been equipped with solar plants. Building on that momentum, the government now wants to install panels across all domestic buildings within three years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Matters for Biharâ€™s Future\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis initiative means much more than free panels. It signals a shift in Biharâ€™s energy storyâ€”from dependence on traditional sources to a future powered by sustainability. Families will see lower electricity costs, while the state contributes to Indiaâ€™s clean energy goals.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor millions, sunlight will no longer just brighten homes. It will also power aspirations, reduce expenses, and improve quality of life.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Stay connected with Bihar Say for more such impactful stories. Join our 12k-strong global community and be part of Biharâ€™s digital voiceâ€”reshaping the stateâ€™s image with stories of change, culture, and innovation.\u003c/p\u003e",
