        "id":  "amrit-bharat-express-to-start-from-gaya-to-delhi-on-august-22-pm-modi-to-inaugurate",
        "title":  "Amrit Bharat Express to Start From Gaya to Delhi on August 22 â€“ PM Modi to Inaugurate",
        "summary":  "Rail passengers in Bihar are set to receive a major boost in connectivity. Beginning August 22, 2025, the Amrit Bharat Express will run from Gaya Junction to Delhi, offering faster and more comfortable travel. The inauguration wil...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eRail passengers in Bihar are set to receive a major boost in connectivity. Beginning August 22, 2025, the Amrit Bharat Express will run from Gaya Junction to Delhi, offering faster and more comfortable travel. The inauguration will be carried out by Prime Minister Narendra Modi, marking a significant milestone for the Magadh region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoute and Key Stops\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amrit Bharat Express will begin its inaugural journey on August 22 at 10:50 AM from Gaya Junction. It will reach Delhi the following morning at 4:30 AM. The train will halt at important stations including Anugrah Narayan Road, Dehri-on-Sone, Sasaram, Bhabhua Road, DDU, Prayagraj (Subedarganj), Kanpur (Govindpuri), Tundla, and Ghaziabad.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis route ensures that passengers across several districts in Bihar and Uttar Pradesh will have convenient access to Delhi.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRegular Operations and Schedule\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter the special inaugural run, regular operations will commence from August 28. The train will operate with the following schedule:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Gaya to Delhi: Train no. 13697 will depart every Sunday and Thursday at 4:30 PM, reaching Delhi by 12:00 noon the next day. From Delhi to Gaya: Train no. 13698 will depart every Monday and Friday at 2:00 PM, arriving at Gaya by 8:55 AM the next day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Gaya to Delhi: Train no. 13697 will depart every Sunday and Thursday at 4:30 PM, reaching Delhi by 12:00 noon the next day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Delhi to Gaya: Train no. 13698 will depart every Monday and Friday at 2:00 PM, arriving at Gaya by 8:55 AM the next day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis twice-a-week service will provide passengers with reliable options to plan their journeys in advance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCoach Composition and Facilities\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe train will run with 22 coaches designed for both comfort and affordability. These include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e8 Sleeper Class Coaches 11 General Class Coaches 1 Pantry Car 2 Seating cum Luggage Rake (SLR) Coaches\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e8 Sleeper Class Coaches\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e11 General Class Coaches\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e1 Pantry Car\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e2 Seating cum Luggage Rake (SLR) Coaches\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this configuration, passengers will benefit from adequate seating capacity and onboard catering facilities, ensuring a smoother travel experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSignificance for Bihar and Beyond\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe launch of the Amrit Bharat Express is more than just the introduction of a new train service. It represents improved regional connectivity and greater ease of travel for thousands of people in the Magadh and Gaya region. Students, professionals, and families will all benefit from this link to the national capital.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFurthermore, Gayaâ€™s importance as a spiritual and tourism hub will strengthen with improved access for domestic and international visitors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStay Updated with Bihar Say\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe introduction of the Amrit Bharat Express marks another step forward for Biharâ€™s transport network and its integration with the rest of the country.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ For regular updates on Biharâ€™s development, culture, and grassroots stories, follow www.biharsay.com. Become part of our 12k+ worldwide community and stay connected with Biharâ€™s journey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags:#Bihar Connectivity #Indian Railways Amrit Bharat Express Bihar news Bihar travel Gaya Delhi Train Gaya Junction PM Modi\u003c/p\u003e",
