        "title":  "Bihar Farmers to Get 60% Subsidy for Dragon Fruit Farming",
        "summary":  "A New Hope for Biharâ€™s Farmers What if one fruit could change the future of Biharâ€™s farmers? The Bihar government has launched the Dragon Fruit Vikas Yojana to make this a reality. With a 60% subsidy, the scheme promises to tr...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eA New Hope for Biharâ€™s Farmers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat if one fruit could change the future of Biharâ€™s farmers? The Bihar government has launched the Dragon Fruit Vikas Yojana to make this a reality. With a 60% subsidy, the scheme promises to transform farming income, crop diversity, and long-term prosperity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat the Dragon Fruit Vikas Yojana Offers\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe scheme, active during 2025â€“26 and 2026â€“27, covers 22 districts, including Bhagalpur, Muzaffarpur, Purnia, Rohtas, Darbhanga, Siwan, and Kishanganj. Farmers who join will receive Rs 2.7 lakh as subsidy per hectare, divided into two parts:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst Year â€“ Rs 1.62 lakh Second Year â€“ Rs 1.08 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst Year â€“ Rs 1.62 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSecond Year â€“ Rs 1.08 lakh\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe total cost of dragon fruit farming is about Rs 6.75 lakh per hectare, and this support will reduce the burden significantly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Dragon Fruit is the Smart Choice\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDragon fruit is not just attractiveâ€”it is profitable. Unlike many other crops, it needs less water and grows well in Biharâ€™s climate. Once planted, it continues to provide returns for several years. Because of its high demand in the market, farmers can earn steadily without depending on seasonal crops.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow to Apply for the Scheme\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFarmers can apply online through the agriculture departmentâ€™s website. They can also visit their district horticulture officer for detailed guidance. By joining early, farmers can ensure they donâ€™t miss the first round of benefits.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBigger Picture â€“ Income and Diversity\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExperts believe that this scheme will not only improve farmer incomes but also promote crop diversity across Bihar. With government support, dragon fruit farming could become a new identity for Biharâ€™s agriculture, similar to how litchi shaped Muzaffarpurâ€™s image.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want to stay ahead with such transformative stories? Follow www.biharsay.com for more regular updates and become part of the 12k+ worldwide community that celebrates Biharâ€™s growth and change!\u003c/p\u003e",
