        "title":  "Shekhar Suman \u0026 Prakash Jha Unite for Janadesh â€“ A Film on Democracy",
        "summary":  "Legends Return, Bihar Leads the Way When two legends from Bihar join hands, history doesnâ€™t just repeatâ€”it gets rewritten. Actor, anchor, and performer Shekhar Suman, the face behind classics like Dekh Bhai Dekh, Movers \u0026 Shak...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eLegends Return, Bihar Leads the Way\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen two legends from Bihar join hands, history doesnâ€™t just repeatâ€”it gets rewritten. Actor, anchor, and performer Shekhar Suman, the face behind classics like Dekh Bhai Dekh, Movers \u0026 Shakers, and Netflixâ€™s Heera Mandi, is back with a bang. This time, he teams up with the fearless filmmaker Prakash Jha, the mind behind cinematic milestones such as Gangaajal, Raajneeti, Aarakshan, and the hard-hitting Aashram series.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTogether, they are ready to create something extraordinary with their upcoming film Janadesh, which begins shooting in August 2025.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond Politics: A Story About Democracy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnlike traditional political dramas, Janadesh breaks the mold. It doesnâ€™t chase power struggles or electoral drama. Instead, it explores a bigger questionâ€”what does democracy truly mean for the people?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePrakash Jha, known for blending social issues with cinema, explains that the film is not about politics. Rather, it will tell stories that highlight what has really happened to democracy over time. His legacy of hard-hitting realism continues, but this time the lens is sharper, bolder, and more human.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Film Rooted in Biharâ€™s Soul\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAuthenticity is at the heart of Janadesh. To make the story deeply connected to the soil, Jha plans to feature nearly 200 local artists alongside the lead stars. These fresh voices will bring raw energy and grassroots authenticity, ensuring that the film feels lived-in and real.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis decision isnâ€™t just castingâ€”itâ€™s a cultural revolution. By involving local talent, the film provides Biharâ€™s youth and artists a stage to shine on the national screen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShekhar Sumanâ€™s Charisma Meets Jhaâ€™s Storytelling\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShekhar Sumanâ€™s versatility has always won audiences. From laughter to hard-hitting roles, his presence has lit up Indian entertainment for decades. On the other side, Prakash Jhaâ€™s uncompromising storytelling has never shied away from truth. Together, their synergy promises fireworks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Sumanâ€™s screen command and Jhaâ€™s fierce narrative, Janadesh is not just another film. It is set to become a cultural storm, born in Bihar yet destined to resonate with every Indian who values democracy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Sons Are Back\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis project isnâ€™t only about cinemaâ€”itâ€™s about identity, pride, and voice. Biharâ€™s sons have returned, and they are here to redefine democracy through storytelling. With Janadesh, Bihar once again takes the cultural spotlight, showing that its stories matter to the nation and the world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Want to stay ahead on stories like this? Follow www.biharsay.com for regular updates and become part of our 12k+ global community. Bihar Say is Indiaâ€™s leading apolitical platform, reshaping Biharâ€™s image with stories of culture, business, and grassroots change.\u003c/p\u003e",
