        "title":  "Adani Power to Build 2,400 MW Thermal Power Plant in Bihar",
        "summary":  "Bihar is gearing up for a historic leap in its energy sector. Adani Power Ltd has secured a Letter of Award (LoA) from the Bihar State Power Generation Company Ltd (BSPGCL) to establish a 2,400 MW greenfield ultra-supercritical th...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar is gearing up for a historic leap in its energy sector. Adani Power Ltd has secured a Letter of Award (LoA) from the Bihar State Power Generation Company Ltd (BSPGCL) to establish a 2,400 MW greenfield ultra-supercritical thermal power plant in Pirpainti, Bhagalpur district. This project will not only supply electricity but also create jobs, boost industries, and power Biharâ€™s future growth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA 25-Year Deal to Light Up Bihar\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe LoA confirms a 25-year electricity supply agreement between Adani Power and BSPGCL. Both North Bihar Power Distribution Company Ltd (NBPDCL) and South Bihar Power Distribution Company Ltd (SBPDCL) will benefit from the project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe plant will have three 800 MW units, designed with ultra-supercritical technology to deliver efficient and reliable electricity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eâ€œWith our Pirpainti project in Bihar, we are setting new benchmarks in efficiency and sustainability. This plant will bring affordable and uninterrupted power to the people of Bihar, driving industrialization and prosperity,â€ said S.B. Khyalia, CEO of Adani Power.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA $3 Billion Investment and Thousands of Jobs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdani Power plans to invest nearly $3 billion in the plant and related infrastructure. This makes it one of the largest private energy investments in Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe project will create 10,000â€“12,000 direct and indirect jobs during construction. Once the plant begins operations, it will continue to employ over 3,000 people, providing stable employment for local communities.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Bihar Needs This Energy Boost\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIndiaâ€™s electricity demand is rising rapidly. From the current 250 GW, peak demand is projected to touch 400 GW by 2031-32 and exceed 700 GW by 2047. Bihar requires a strong and consistent power supply to support industries, cities, and villages alike.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlthough renewable energy is growing, thermal power still ensures round-the-clock reliability. It remains the backbone of Indiaâ€™s energy security, offering crucial base-load and grid balancing support. To meet demand, the government plans to add 100 GW of new thermal capacity by 2035. The Pirpainti project positions Bihar as a central part of this growth strategy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdani Powerâ€™s Proven Record\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdani Power currently operates 18,110 MW of installed thermal capacity across 12 plants in India. It has repeatedly shown its ability to deliver large-scale, dependable power.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn BSPGCLâ€™s competitive bidding, Adani Power won by offering the lowest tariff of â‚¹6.075 per kWh. With its proven expertise, the company is set to play a defining role in Biharâ€™s development journey.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ”¥ Bihar stands at the edge of an energy revolution, with Bhagalpur becoming the epicenter. This plant is more than powerâ€”itâ€™s progress, jobs, and prosperity for millions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ To keep track of Biharâ€™s biggest business and cultural stories, follow www.biharsay.com and join our 12,000+ global community shaping a new digital voice for Bihar.\u003c/p\u003e",
