        "id":  "sitamarhi-delhi-special-train-timing-stoppage-announced",
        "title":  "Sitamarhiâ€“Delhi Special Train Timing \u0026 Stoppage Announced",
        "summary":  "Festive season travel just got easier! The Railways has announced a special train between Delhi and Sitamarhi, giving thousands of passengers relief from festive rush. This train service aims to ease the crowd during peak travel m...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eFestive season travel just got easier! The Railways has announced a special train between Delhi and Sitamarhi, giving thousands of passengers relief from festive rush. This train service aims to ease the crowd during peak travel months when getting a confirmed ticket feels impossible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Special Train Matters\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery year, as the festive season approaches, trains from Delhi to Bihar get packed beyond capacity. Families, students, and workers struggle to book seats. To solve this, Indian Railways has introduced the Anand Vihar Terminalâ€“Sitamarhi Special Train (04016/04015).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this move, travel will become smoother, and passengers can reach Sitamarhi without the usual stress of overcrowding.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTiming of Anand Viharâ€“Sitamarhi Special Train\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain Number 04016 will run from 29 September to 30 November. It will depart Anand Vihar at 15:30 hrs daily. The train will reach Lucknow at 01:20 hrs the next day. Finally, it will arrive in Sitamarhi by 15:00 hrs on the second day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain Number 04016 will run from 29 September to 30 November.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt will depart Anand Vihar at 15:30 hrs daily.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe train will reach Lucknow at 01:20 hrs the next day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, it will arrive in Sitamarhi by 15:00 hrs on the second day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis schedule ensures that passengers traveling during festivals get a comfortable journey without last-minute ticket worries.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReturn Journey: Sitamarhi to Delhi\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain Number 04015 will operate from 30 September to 1 December. It will leave Sitamarhi at 16:30 hrs daily. The train will pass through Lucknow at 08:40 hrs next morning. It will then continue to Delhi, giving travelers a direct and hassle-free return option.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain Number 04015 will operate from 30 September to 1 December.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt will leave Sitamarhi at 16:30 hrs daily.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe train will pass through Lucknow at 08:40 hrs next morning.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt will then continue to Delhi, giving travelers a direct and hassle-free return option.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRailway Officials Speak on Festive Travel\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccording to Pankaj Kumar Singh, CPRO of North Eastern Railway, festive demand has pushed the need for special services. He mentioned that weekly special trains via Lucknow will start from 27 September, while the Gomti Nagarâ€“Bengaluru service will also run till December to support extra demand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOther Special Train Announcements\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlongside Sitamarhi, another special service will benefit travelers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain 05017 Mauâ€“Udhna Weekly Special will run every Saturday from 27 September to 1 November. Departure: 05:30 hrs from Mau. Major stops: Badshahnagar (14:02 hrs), Aishbagh (14:40 hrs). Arrival: Udhna at 12:00 hrs the next day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTrain 05017 Mauâ€“Udhna Weekly Special will run every Saturday from 27 September to 1 November.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeparture: 05:30 hrs from Mau.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMajor stops: Badshahnagar (14:02 hrs), Aishbagh (14:40 hrs).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eArrival: Udhna at 12:00 hrs the next day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe return service, Train 05018 Udhnaâ€“Mau, will operate every Sunday from 28 September to 2 November. It will leave Udhna at 15:00 hrs and stop at Aishbagh (14:15 hrs) and Badshahnagar (14:47 hrs) before heading further.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy You Shouldnâ€™t Miss This Update\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you plan to travel during Durga Puja, Diwali, or Chhath, these trains are your golden chance. Early booking will ensure comfort, safety, and timely arrival. With railway authorities expanding services, traveling between Delhi, Lucknow, Sitamarhi, Mau, and Udhna has never been more convenient.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Stay updated on every train announcement, development project, and travel update across Bihar. Follow www.biharsay.com and join our growing global community of 11,000+ people who love authentic, apolitical stories about Bihar!\u003c/p\u003e",
