        "id":  "gaya-ji-pitru-paksha-fair-2025-vishnupad-declared-no-pollution-no-horn-no-vehicle-zone",
        "title":  "Gaya Ji Pitru Paksha Fair 2025: Vishnupad Declared No Pollution, No Horn, No Vehicle Zone",
        "summary":  "Biharâ€™s Sacred Fair Gets a Pollution-Free Makeover Every year, lakhs of pilgrims from across India and abroad gather in Gaya Ji to honor their ancestors during the Pitru Paksha Mela. This year, the district administration has ta...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Sacred Fair Gets a Pollution-Free Makeover\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery year, lakhs of pilgrims from across India and abroad gather in Gaya Ji to honor their ancestors during the Pitru Paksha Mela. This year, the district administration has taken a remarkable step to ensure comfort, safety, and spirituality blend together.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Vishnupad temple area has been officially declared a No Pollution, No Horn, and No Vehicle Zone. This initiative aims to provide a peaceful atmosphere to devotees while keeping the sacred site clean and congestion-free.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Big Step Towards a Hassle-Free Pilgrimage\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo implement this change, DM Shashank Shubhankar and SSP Anand Kumar personally traveled by e-rickshaw from Chand Choura to Vishnupad Mandir, symbolizing the new system. By doing this, they not only set an example but also encouraged devotees to embrace this eco-friendly approach.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportantly, vehicles are now restricted beyond Chand Choura and Bengali Ashram. Pilgrims can only reach the temple either by foot or through free e-rickshaw services provided by the administration. This move ensures the narrow temple lanes remain free from traffic jams, making the spiritual journey smooth and serene.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSpecial Facilities for Devotees and Seniors\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnderstanding the needs of elderly visitors, the administration has deployed 60 e-rickshaws in three shifts. From Pretshila parking points to Pretshila temple, special arrangements have been made so that senior citizens face no difficulty.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, at Gaya Railway Station, pilgrims will find free e-rickshaw services to different pind-daan spots. This facility will not only save time but also offer much-needed convenience for those unfamiliar with the city.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy This Step Matters for Bihar and Pilgrims\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Pitru Paksha Mela is not just a religious gathering; it is a lifeline of Biharâ€™s cultural and spiritual identity. With lakhs of devotees pouring in, mismanagement can lead to chaos. However, this eco-conscious decision brings hope that the Vishnupad temple complex will remain safe, pollution-free, and spiritually uplifting.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, this effort reflects how Bihar is gradually embracing modern solutions while respecting deep-rooted traditions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eðŸ‘‰ Stay connected with www.biharsay.com for more such meaningful updates and become part of our 12k+ global community. Bihar Say is not just mediaâ€”itâ€™s a movement to reshape Biharâ€™s image with stories of culture, business, and grassroots change.\u003c/p\u003e",
