        "title":  "Bihar Governmentâ€™s Agriculture Department Wins Scotch Gold Award",
        "summary":  "Bihar Government Wins Scotch Gold Award: A Historic Achievement Biharâ€™s Agriculture Department has recently received the prestigious Scotch Gold Award, recognizing excellence in agriculture and innovative initiatives. This award...",
        "content":  "\u003cp\u003eBihar Government Wins Scotch Gold Award: A Historic Achievement\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBiharâ€™s Agriculture Department has recently received the prestigious Scotch Gold Award, recognizing excellence in agriculture and innovative initiatives. This award celebrates the departmentâ€™s consistent efforts to enhance farmer welfare, promote sustainable practices, and implement impactful programs. Moreover, it positions Bihar as a state leading in agricultural development and environmental responsibility.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVikramshila Gangetic Dolphin Sanctuary: Biharâ€™s Ecological Treasure\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocated in Bhagalpur, the Vikramshila Gangetic Dolphin Sanctuary is Indiaâ€™s only dolphin sanctuary. Spanning nearly 60 kilometers of the Ganga River, it is home to the endangered Gangetic dolphin, Indiaâ€™s national aquatic mammal. The sanctuary plays a crucial role in conserving this vulnerable species while safeguarding the broader river ecosystem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFurthermore, it attracts researchers, environmentalists, and eco-tourists who wish to witness the rare aquatic wildlife and understand river ecology first-hand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConservation Efforts and Biodiversity\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe sanctuary is not limited to dolphins. It hosts smooth-coated otters, freshwater turtles, and a variety of waterbirds. Conservation teams, alongside local communities, work tirelessly to prevent river pollution, illegal fishing, and other threats. They actively monitor wildlife, educate locals, and implement sustainable practices that ensure the long-term survival of these species.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConsequently, the sanctuary is becoming a model for community-led environmental conservation, proving that human intervention can harmonize with nature.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBihar on the Global Environmental Map\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThrough initiatives like the Vikramshila Dolphin Sanctuary, Bihar is gaining global recognition for its environmental stewardship. The sanctuary highlights the stateâ€™s commitment to protecting endangered species while promoting eco-tourism and raising awareness about biodiversity. It reflects a balance between ecological preservation and socio-economic development, making Bihar a model for other regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJoin Bihar Say â€“ Become Part of a Global Community\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want regular updates on Biharâ€™s culture, biodiversity, and grassroots stories, visit www.biharsay.com. Join over 11,000 followers worldwide and explore inspiring stories, news, and updates from Biharâ€™s heart. Become part of our growing community and stay connected to Biharâ€™s journey of change.\u003c/p\u003e",
